window.ART_ARTISTS={"Camille Pissarro":{"zh":"卡米耶·毕沙罗","en":"Camille Pissarro","born":"1830","died":"1903","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"卡米耶·毕沙罗，出生于丹属圣托马斯岛的法国印象派与新印象派画家。他是印象派运动的核心人物，也是唯一参加了全部八次印象派画展的画家；塞尚与高更皆尊其为师，以描绘乡村风景与农民劳作著称。","bio_en":"Camille Pissarro was a Danish-French Impressionist and Neo-Impressionist painter born on St Thomas. A central figure of the movement and the only artist to exhibit at all eight Impressionist shows, he was a mentor to Cézanne and Gauguin and is celebrated for his rural landscapes and scenes of peasant life.","p":"images/a/Q134741.jpg"},"Leonardo da Vinci":{"zh":"列奥纳多·达·芬奇","en":"Leonardo da Vinci","born":"1452","died":"1519","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"列奥纳多·迪·塞尔·皮耶罗·达·芬奇，意大利文艺复兴时期博学者：在绘画、音乐、建筑、数学、几何学、解剖学、生理学、动物学、植物学、天文学、气象学、地质学、地理学、物理学、光学、力学、发明、土木工程等领域都有显著的成就。","bio_en":"Leonardo di ser Piero da Vinci was an Italian polymath of the High Renaissance who was active as a painter, draughtsman, engineer, scientist, theorist, sculptor, and architect.","p":"images/a/Q762.png"},"Vincent van Gogh":{"zh":"文森特·梵高","en":"Vincent van Gogh","born":"1853","died":"1890","cty_zh":"荷兰王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of the Netherlands","bio_zh":"文森·威廉·梵高，荷兰后印象派画家。他是表现主义的先驱，对二十世纪艺术特别是野兽派与德国表现主义产生了深刻的影响。梵高的作品，如《星夜》、《向日葵》、《有乌鸦的麦田》等，早已跻身世界名作行列。","bio_en":"Vincent Willem van Gogh was a Dutch Post-Impressionist painter who is among the most famous and influential figures in the history of Western art.","p":"images/a/Q5582.jpg"},"Edvard Munch":{"zh":"爱德华·蒙克","en":"Edvard Munch","born":"1863","died":"1944","cty_zh":"挪威","cty_en":"Norway","bio_zh":"爱德华·蒙克，挪威画家。其最著名作品《呐喊》为当代艺术标志性图像之一。 他的童年被疾病、丧亲之痛以及对遗传家族精神疾病的恐惧所笼罩。","bio_en":"Edvard Munch was a Norwegian painter. His 1893 work The Scream has become one of the most iconic and acclaimed images in all of Western art.","p":"images/a/Q41406.jpg"},"Johannes Vermeer":{"zh":"约翰尼斯·弗美尔","en":"Johannes Vermeer","born":"1632","died":"1675","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"约翰尼斯·维米尔，又称扬·维米尔、约翰·维米尔，是一位17世纪的荷兰黄金时代画家。他毕生工作生活于荷兰的代尔夫特，有时也被称为代尔夫特的维米尔。","bio_en":"Johannes Vermeer was a Dutch painter who specialized in domestic interior scenes of middle-class life. He is considered one of the greatest painters of the Dutch Golden Age.","p":"images/a/Q41264.jpg"},"Pablo Picasso":{"zh":"巴勃罗·毕加索","en":"Pablo Picasso","born":"1881","died":"1973","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"巴勃罗·鲁伊斯·毕卡索，西班牙画家、雕塑家、版画家、舞台设计师、作家和法国共产党党员，和乔治·布拉克同为立体主义的创始者，是20世纪现代艺术的主要代表人物之一，遗作逾两万件。","bio_en":"Pablo Ruiz Picasso was a Spanish painter and sculptor who spent most of his adult life in France. One of the most influential artists of the 20th century, he is known for co-founding the Cubist moveme…","p":"images/a/Q5593.jpg"},"Sandro Botticelli":{"zh":"桑德罗·波提切利","en":"Sandro Botticelli","born":"1445","died":"1510","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"桑德罗·波提切利，原名亚历桑德罗·迪马里亚诺·迪万尼·菲利佩皮是欧洲文艺复兴早期的佛罗伦斯画派艺术家。","bio_en":"Alessandro di Mariano di Vanni Filipepi , better known as Sandro Botticelli or simply Botticelli, was an Italian painter of the Early Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5669.jpg"},"Michelangelo":{"zh":"米开朗琪罗","en":"Michelangelo","born":"1475","died":"1564","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"米高安哲罗…","bio_en":"Michelangelo di Lodovico Buonarroti Simoni , known mononymously as Michelangelo, was an Italian sculptor, painter, architect, and poet of the High Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5592.jpg"},"Rembrandt":{"zh":"伦勃朗","en":"Rembrandt","born":"1606","died":"1669","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"伦勃朗·哈尔门松·范·莱因，通称伦勃朗，巴洛克绘画艺术的代表画家之一，也是17世纪荷兰黄金时代绘画的主要人物，被认为是荷兰历史上最伟大的画家；在2004年票选最伟大的荷兰人当中，他排行位于第九，次于第八的安妮·弗兰克。","bio_en":"Rembrandt Harmenszoon van Rijn , known mononymously as Rembrandt, was a Dutch Golden Age painter, printmaker, and draughtsman.","p":"images/a/Q5598.jpg"},"Salvador Dalí":{"zh":"萨尔瓦多·达利","en":"Salvador Dalí","born":"1904","died":"1989","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"萨尔瓦多·多明哥·菲利普·哈辛托·达利-多梅内克，普波尔侯爵，一般简称萨尔瓦多·达利，是著名的西班牙加泰罗尼亚画家，因为其超现实主义作品而闻名，他与毕加索和米罗一同被认为是西班牙20世纪最有代表性的三位画家。","bio_en":"Salvador Domingo Felipe Jacinto Dalí i Domènech, Marquess of Dalí de Púbol , known as Salvador Dalí, was a Spanish surrealist artist renowned for his technical skill, precise draftsmanship, and the st…","p":"images/a/Q5577.jpg"},"Eugène Delacroix":{"zh":"欧仁·德拉克罗瓦","en":"Eugène Delacroix","born":"1798","died":"1863","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"欧仁·德拉克罗瓦是法国著名浪漫主义画家。","bio_en":"Ferdinand Victor Eugène Delacroix was a French Romantic artist who was regarded as the leader of the French Romantic school.","p":"images/a/Q33477.jpg"},"Claude Monet":{"zh":"克劳德·莫奈","en":"Claude Monet","born":"1840","died":"1926","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"奥斯卡-克劳德·莫奈，法国画家，印象派代表人物及创始人之一，「印象」一词即是源自其名作《印象·日出》，该画作于1874年在莫奈及其同事举办的第一次独立展览中展出。","bio_en":"Oscar-Claude Monet was a French painter and founder of Impressionism who is seen as a key precursor to modernism, especially in his attempts to paint nature as he perceived it.","p":"images/a/Q296.jpg"},"Gustav Klimt":{"zh":"古斯塔夫·克里姆特","en":"Gustav Klimt","born":"1862","died":"1918","cty_zh":"奥地利帝国","cty_en":"Austrian Empire","bio_zh":"古斯塔夫·克林姆，是出身维也纳的象征主义画家，也是维也纳分离派运动最具代表性的成员之一。克里姆特以其绘画、壁画、素描和其他艺术品而闻名。","bio_en":"Gustav Klimt was an Austrian symbolist painter and a founding member of the Vienna Secession movement. His work helped define the Art Nouveau style in Europe.","p":"images/a/Q34661.jpg"},"Grant Wood":{"zh":"格兰特·伍德","en":"Grant Wood","born":"1891","died":"1942","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"格兰特·伍德，美国画家，出生于艾奥瓦州阿纳穆斯。1930年因创作《美国哥特式》油画而一举成名，该作品也是美国艺术史上最著名的作品之一，也是为数不多的公认的文化标志之一，与列奥纳多·达·芬奇的《蒙娜丽莎》和爱德华·孟克的《呐喊》相提并论。","bio_en":"Grant DeVolson Wood was an American artist and representative of Regionalism, best known for his paintings depicting the rural American Midwest.","p":"images/a/Q217434.jpg"},"Georges Seurat":{"zh":"乔治·皮埃尔·秀拉","en":"Georges Seurat","born":"1859","died":"1891","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"乔治·皮埃尔·秀拉，是法国后印象派及新印象派画家。他以其运用色彩理论之分色主义与点彩画作品为人所知；同时，他的conté蜡笔粉彩作品也广受赞誉。","bio_en":"Georges Pierre Seurat was a French post-Impressionist artist. He devised the painting techniques known as chromoluminarism and pointillism and used conté crayon for drawings on paper with a rough surf…","p":"images/a/Q34013.jpg"},"Jean-François Millet":{"zh":"让-弗朗索瓦·米勒","en":"Jean-François Millet","born":"1814","died":"1875","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-弗朗索瓦·米勒法国巴比松派画家。他以写实手法描绘的乡村风俗画闻名法国画坛，被认为是写实主义艺术运动的参与者。代表作有《拾穗》《晚祷》等。","bio_en":"Jean-François Millet was a French painter and one of the founders of the Barbizon school in rural France. Millet is noted for his paintings of peasant farmers and can be categorized as part of the Rea…","p":"images/a/Q148458.jpg"},"Raphael":{"zh":"拉斐尔·圣齐奥","en":"Raphael","born":"1483","died":"1520","cty_zh":"神圣罗马帝国","cty_en":"Holy Roman Empire","bio_zh":"拉斐洛·桑齐奥·达·乌尔比诺，通称拉斐尔，意大利文艺复兴时期画家与建筑师，与列奥纳多·达·芬奇和米开朗基罗并称「文艺复兴三杰」。他的作品因其清晰的形式、流畅的构图以及对新柏拉图主义人类宏伟理想的视觉呈现而备受赞誉。","bio_en":"Raffaello Sanzio da Urbino , now generally known in English as Raphael , was an Italian painter and architect of the High Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5597.jpg"},"Diego Velázquez":{"zh":"委拉斯开兹","en":"Diego Velázquez","born":"1599","died":"1660","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"迭戈·罗德里奎兹·德·席尔瓦-委拉斯开兹是文艺复兴后期、巴洛克时代、西班牙黄金时代画家，对后世画家启发很大，弗朗西斯科·戈雅认为他是自己的“伟大教师之一”。","bio_en":"Diego Rodríguez de Silva y Velázquez was a Spanish Baroque painter, the leading artist in the court of King Philip IV of Spain and Portugal, and of the Spanish Golden Age.","p":"images/a/Q297.jpg"},"Katsushika Hokusai":{"zh":"葛饰北斋","en":"Katsushika Hokusai","born":"1760","died":"1849","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"葛饰北斋，日本江户时代浮世绘画家、版画家，自号「画狂人」。以木版画组画《富岳三十六景》（内含《神奈川冲浪里》）闻名于世，一生创作逾三万幅作品，其构图与色彩深刻影响了欧洲印象派与新艺术运动。","bio_en":"Katsushika Hokusai was a Japanese ukiyo-e painter and printmaker of the Edo period, best known for the woodblock series Thirty-Six Views of Mount Fuji, which includes the iconic Great Wave off Kanagawa. Extraordinarily prolific, his compositions and colour profoundly influenced European Impressionism and Art Nouveau.","p":"images/a/Q5586.jpg"},"Édouard Manet":{"zh":"爱德华·马奈","en":"Édouard Manet","born":"1832","died":"1883","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"爱德华·马奈，法国巴黎人，著名现代主义画家，被认为是写实派过渡到印象派的关键人物。 马奈的画风乍看之下应该属于古典的写实派画风，其人物细节都相当有真实感。","bio_en":"Édouard Manet was a French modernist painter. He was one of the first 19th-century artists to paint modern life, as well as a pivotal figure in the transition from Realism to Impressionism.","p":"images/a/Q40599.jpg"},"Paul Cézanne":{"zh":"保罗·塞尚","en":"Paul Cézanne","born":"1839","died":"1906","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"保罗·塞尚，法国后印象派画家，风格介于印象派到立体主义画派之间。他的作品为19世纪的艺术观念转换到20世纪的艺术风格奠定基础，被亨利·马蒂斯与巴勃罗·毕卡索誉为“我们所有人的父亲”。","bio_en":"Paul Cézanne was a French Post-Impressionist painter whose work introduced new modes of representation, influenced avant-garde artistic movements of the early 20th century and formed the bridge betwee…","p":"images/a/Q35548.jpg"},"Henri Matisse":{"zh":"亨利·马蒂斯","en":"Henri Matisse","born":"1869","died":"1954","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"亨利·埃米尔·伯努瓦·马蒂斯，法国画家、雕塑家及版画家，野兽派的创始人。 马蒂斯与毕卡索、马歇尔·杜尚一起为20世纪初的造型艺术带来巨大变革。","bio_en":"Henri Émile Benoît Matisse was a French visual artist, known for both his use of colour and his fluid and original draughtsmanship.","p":"images/a/Q5589.jpg"},"Piet Mondrian":{"zh":"皮特·蒙德里安","en":"Piet Mondrian","born":"1872","died":"1944","cty_zh":"荷兰王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of the Netherlands","bio_zh":"彼得·科内利斯·蒙德里安，通称皮特·蒙德里安，是一名荷兰画家，风格派 运动幕后艺术家和非具象绘画的创始者之一，对后代的建筑、设计等影响很大。","bio_en":"Pieter Cornelis Mondriaan , known after 1911 as Piet Mondrian , was a Dutch painter and art theoretician, who is regarded as one of the greatest artists of the 20th century.","p":"images/a/Q151803.jpg"},"Wassily Kandinsky":{"zh":"瓦西里·康定斯基","en":"Wassily Kandinsky","born":"1866","died":"1944","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"瓦西里·瓦西里耶维奇·康丁斯基，出生于俄罗斯的画家和美术理论家。 儒略历1866年12月4日，康丁斯基出生于俄罗斯莫斯科，在敖德萨度过童年。","bio_en":"Wassily Wassilyevich Kandinsky was a Russian painter and art theorist active in Germany during the late Belle Époque and Interwar eras.","p":"images/a/Q61064.jpg"},"Lucas Cranach the Elder":{"zh":"老卢卡斯·克拉纳赫","en":"Lucas Cranach the Elder","born":"1472","died":"1553","cty_zh":"德国","cty_en":"Germany","bio_zh":"老卢卡斯·克拉纳赫是德国文艺复兴时期画家，他的儿子小卢卡斯·克拉纳赫也是杰出的画家。 克拉纳赫出生于法兰克尼亚地区的克罗纳赫，其姓氏即源自出生地。","bio_en":"Lucas Cranach the Elder was a German Renaissance painter and printmaker in woodcut and engraving. He was court painter to the Electors of Saxony for most of his career, and is known for his portraits…","p":"images/a/Q191748.jpg"},"Titian":{"zh":"提香","en":"Titian","born":"1490","died":"1576","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"提香·维伽略－1576年8月27日），常简称提香，他是意大利文艺复兴后期威尼斯画派的代表画家。提香出生于意大利东北部阿尔卑斯山地区的卡多列，10岁时随兄长到威尼斯，在乔瓦尼·贝利尼的画室学画，与画家乔尔乔内是同学。","bio_en":"Tiziano Vecellio , Latinized as Titianus, hence known in English as Titian , was an Italian Renaissance painter.","p":"images/a/Q47551.jpg"},"Hieronymus Bosch":{"zh":"耶罗尼米斯·博斯","en":"Hieronymus Bosch","born":"1450","died":"1516","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":"Northern Low Countries","bio_zh":"耶罗尼米斯·博斯，又名希耶罗尼米斯·博斯或耶伦·博斯，原名耶罗尼米斯·范阿肯，荷兰十五至十六世纪作品丰富的画家。他的多数画作描绘罪恶与人类道德的沉沦。","bio_en":"Hieronymus Bosch ]; c. 1450 – 9 August 1516) was a Dutch painter from Brabant. He is one of the most notable representatives of the Early Netherlandish painting school.","p":"images/a/Q130531.jpg"},"Jan van Eyck":{"zh":"扬·范·艾克","en":"Jan van Eyck","born":"1390","died":"1441","cty_zh":"南尼德兰","cty_en":"Southern Netherlands","bio_zh":"扬·范艾克，活跃于布鲁日的弗拉芒画家。他是早期尼德兰画派的创新者之一，也是北方文艺复兴的代表人物。除与其兄许贝特·范艾克合作完成的《根特祭坛画》和签有字母「Hand G」的《都灵-米兰时光》泥金装饰手抄本之外…","bio_en":"Jan van Eyck was an early Netherlandish painter active in Bruges who was one of the early innovators of what became known as early Netherlandish painting, and one of the supreme figures of the Early N…","p":"images/a/Q102272.jpg"},"Pieter Brueghel the Elder":{"zh":"老彼得·布吕赫尔","en":"Pieter Brueghel the Elder","born":"1525","died":"1569","cty_zh":"布拉班特公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Brabant","bio_zh":"老彼得·布吕赫尔，文艺复兴时期布拉班特公国画家，以地景与农民景象的画作闻名。根据卡雷尔·范曼德尔的记载，他出生于邻近布雷达的布罗赫尔，但不确定所指的是拉丁语中位于荷兰的布雷达，或指比利时的布雷。","bio_en":"Pieter Bruegel the Elder was among the most significant artists of Dutch and Flemish Renaissance painting, a painter and printmaker, known for his landscapes and peasant scenes ; he was a pioneer in p…","p":"images/a/Q43270.jpg"},"Hans Holbein the Younger":{"zh":"小汉斯·霍尔拜因","en":"Hans Holbein the Younger","born":"1497","died":"1543","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"小汉斯·霍尔拜因是德国画家，最擅长油画和版画，属于欧洲北方文艺复兴时代的艺术家，他最著名的作品是许多肖像画和系列木版画《死神之舞》。","bio_en":"Hans Holbein the Younger was a German painter and printmaker of Swiss descent who worked in a Northern Renaissance style, and is considered one of the greatest portraitists of the 16th century.","p":"images/a/Q48319.jpg"},"Peter Paul Rubens":{"zh":"彼得·保罗·鲁本斯","en":"Peter Paul Rubens","born":"1577","died":"1640","cty_zh":"西属尼德兰","cty_en":"Spanish Netherlands","bio_zh":"彼得·保罗·鲁本斯爵士，弗兰德画家，巴洛克画派早期的代表人物。鲁本斯的画有浓厚的巴洛克风格，强调运动、颜色和感官。鲁本斯以其反宗教改革的祭坛画、肖像画、风景画以及有关神话及寓言的历史画闻名。","bio_en":"Sir Peter Paul Rubens was a Flemish artist and diplomat. He is considered the most influential artist of the Flemish Baroque tradition.","p":"images/a/Q5599.jpg"},"Caravaggio":{"zh":"卡拉瓦乔","en":"Caravaggio","born":"1571","died":"1610","cty_zh":"米兰公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Milan","bio_zh":"米开朗基罗·梅里西·达·卡拉瓦乔，意大利画家，活跃于16世纪末至17世纪初，主要创作于罗马，在他生命的最后四年里，他辗转于那不勒斯、马耳他和西西里。","bio_en":"Michelangelo Merisi da Caravaggio , known mononymously as Caravaggio, was an Italian painter active in Rome for a significant portion of his artistic life.","p":"images/a/Q42207.jpg"},"Artemisia Gentileschi":{"zh":"阿尔泰米西娅·真蒂莱斯基","en":"Artemisia Gentileschi","born":"1593","died":"1653","cty_zh":"教皇国","cty_en":"Papal States","bio_zh":"阿尔泰米西娅·洛米·真蒂莱斯基，意大利巴洛克画家。在那个女画家十分少见的年代，她率先创作了历史及宗教画。","bio_en":"Artemisia Lomi Gentileschi was an Italian Baroque painter. Gentileschi is considered among the most accomplished 17th-century artists, initially working in the style of Caravaggio.","p":"images/a/Q212657.jpg"},"Anthony van Dyck":{"zh":"安东尼·范戴克","en":"Anthony van Dyck","born":"1599","died":"1641","cty_zh":"西属尼德兰","cty_en":"Spanish Netherlands","bio_zh":"安东尼·范戴克爵士，比利时弗拉芒族画家，是英格兰国王查理一世时期的首席宫廷画家。查理一世及其皇族的许多著名画像都是由范戴克创作的。他的画像轻松高贵的风格，影响了英国肖像画将近150年。","bio_en":"Sir Anthony van Dyck was a Flemish Baroque artist, who became the leading court painter in England after success in the Spanish Netherlands and Italy.","p":"images/a/Q150679.jpg"},"Gian Lorenzo Bernini":{"zh":"济安·贝尼尼","en":"Gian Lorenzo Bernini","born":"1598","died":"1680","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"济安·洛伦佐·贝尼尼，意大利巴洛克艺术的核心人物，雕塑家兼建筑家。代表作有《圣特蕾莎的沉迷》《阿波罗与达芙妮》，并主持设计了圣彼得大教堂广场的柱廊。","bio_en":"Gian Lorenzo Bernini was the leading figure of the Italian Baroque, a sculptor and architect whose masterpieces include the Ecstasy of Saint Teresa and Apollo and Daphne; he also designed the great colonnade of St Peter's Square.","p":"images/a/Q160538.jpg"},"Jean-Honoré Fragonard":{"zh":"让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔","en":"Jean-Honoré Fragonard","born":"1732","died":"1806","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔，法国罗可可时代最后一位重要代表画家。","bio_en":"Jean-Honoré Fragonard was a French painter and printmaker whose late Rococo manner was distinguished by remarkable facility, exuberance, and hedonism.","p":"images/a/Q127171.jpg"},"Antoine Watteau":{"zh":"安托万·华托","en":"Antoine Watteau","born":"1684","died":"1721","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-安托万·华托，法国洛可可绘画的开创者。首创「雅宴」题材，以轻盈的笔触描绘游园男女的优雅风姿与淡淡愁绪。","bio_en":"Jean-Antoine Watteau was the originator of the French Rococo, inventing the fête galante genre that depicts elegant outdoor gatherings with a light touch and a note of gentle melancholy.","p":"images/a/Q183221.jpg"},"Jacques-Louis David":{"zh":"雅克-路易·大卫","en":"Jacques-Louis David","born":"1748","died":"1825","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"雅克-路易·大卫，又译达维特，法国画家，新古典主义画派的奠基人和杰出代表，他在1780年代绘成的一系列历史画标志著当代艺术由洛可可风格向古典主义的转变。","bio_en":"Jacques-Louis David was a French painter in the Neoclassical style, considered to be the preeminent painter of the era.","p":"images/a/Q83155.jpg"},"Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres":{"zh":"让·奥古斯特·多米尼克·安格尔","en":"Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres","born":"1780","died":"1867","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让·奥古斯特·多米尼克·安格尔是法国画家，新古典主义画派的最后一位代表人物，他和浪漫主义画派的杰出代表欧仁·德拉克罗瓦之间的著名争论震动了整个法国画坛。","bio_en":"Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres was a French Neoclassical painter. Ingres was profoundly influenced by past artistic traditions and aspired to become the guardian of academic orthodoxy against the ascen…","p":"images/a/Q23380.jpg"},"Francisco Goya":{"zh":"弗朗西斯科·戈雅","en":"Francisco Goya","born":"1746","died":"1828","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"弗朗西斯科·荷西·德·戈雅-路西恩特斯是西班牙浪漫主义画家与版画家。他被认为是18世纪末至19世纪初最重要的西班牙艺术家。他的画作、素描与版画反映了当时的历史动荡，并对19至20世纪的重要画家产生了深远影响。","bio_en":"Francisco José de Goya y Lucientes was a Spanish romantic painter and printmaker. He is considered the most important Spanish artist of the late 18th and early 19th centuries.","p":"images/a/Q5432.jpg"},"Théodore Géricault":{"zh":"泰奥多尔·籍里柯","en":"Théodore Géricault","born":"1791","died":"1824","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-路易·安德烈·泰奥多尔·杰利柯是法国浪漫主义画派的先驱，对浪漫主义画派和现实主义画派的发展有重要影响。","bio_en":"Jean-Louis André Théodore Géricault was a French painter and lithographer. His best-known painting is The Raft of the Medusa.","p":"images/a/Q184212.jpg"},"Caspar David Friedrich":{"zh":"卡斯帕·弗里德里希","en":"Caspar David Friedrich","born":"1774","died":"1840","cty_zh":"瑞典","cty_en":"Sweden","bio_zh":"卡斯帕·大卫·弗里德里希，19世纪德国浪漫主义风景画家，生于瑞典波美拉尼亚的格赖夫斯瓦尔德镇。1798年起，弗里德里希开始在哥本哈根学习。","bio_en":"Caspar David Friedrich was a German Romantic landscape painter, generally considered the most important German artist of his generation, whose often symbolic, and anti-classical work, conveys a subjec…","p":"images/a/Q104884.jpg"},"J. M. W. Turner":{"zh":"约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳","en":"J. M. W. Turner","born":"1775","died":"1851","cty_zh":"大不列颠王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Great Britain","bio_zh":"约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳…","bio_en":"Joseph Mallord William Turner , known in his time as William Turner, was an English Romantic painter, printmaker and watercolourist.","p":"images/a/Q159758.jpg"},"John Constable":{"zh":"约翰·康斯特勃","en":"John Constable","born":"1776","died":"1837","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"约翰·康斯特勃 RA，英国风景画画家。他的很多作品描绘的是家乡附近的戴德姆谷风景，此地因此得名“康斯特勃之乡”。","bio_en":"John Constable was an English landscape painter in the Romantic tradition. Born in Suffolk, he is known principally for revolutionising the genre of landscape painting with his pictures of Dedham Vale…","p":"images/a/Q159297.jpg"},"Gustave Courbet":{"zh":"居斯塔夫·库尔贝","en":"Gustave Courbet","born":"1819","died":"1877","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"古斯塔夫·库尔贝，法国著名画家，现实主义画派的创始人，主张艺术应以现实为依据，反对粉饰生活。他的名言是：“我不会画天使，因为我从来没有见过他们。","bio_en":"Jean Désiré Gustave Courbet was a French painter who led the Realism movement in 19th-century French painting. Committed to painting only what he could see, he rejected academic convention and the Rom…","p":"images/a/Q34618.jpg"},"John Everett Millais":{"zh":"约翰·艾佛雷特·米莱","en":"John Everett Millais","born":"1829","died":"1896","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"第一代从男爵约翰·艾佛雷特·米莱 PRA，英国画家与插图画家，也是前拉斐尔派的创始人之一。","bio_en":"Sir John Everett Millais, 1st Baronet was an English painter and illustrator who was one of the founders of the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood.","p":"images/a/Q159606.jpg"},"Dante Gabriel Rossetti":{"zh":"但丁·加百列·罗塞蒂","en":"Dante Gabriel Rossetti","born":"1828","died":"1882","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"加百利·查理斯·但丁·罗塞蒂是英国画家、诗人、插图画家和翻译家，是前拉斐尔派的创始人之一。","bio_en":"Gabriel Charles Dante Rossetti , generally known as Dante Gabriel Rossetti , was an English poet, illustrator, painter and translator.","p":"images/a/Q186748.jpg"},"Edgar Degas":{"zh":"埃德加·德加","en":"Edgar Degas","born":"1834","died":"1917","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"伊莱尔-热尔曼-埃德加·德加，生于巴黎，法国印象派画家、雕塑家。","bio_en":"Edgar Degas was a French Impressionist artist famous for his pastel drawings and oil paintings. Degas also produced bronze sculptures, prints, and drawings.","p":"images/a/Q46373.jpg"},"Pierre-Auguste Renoir":{"zh":"皮耶-奥古斯特·雷诺瓦","en":"Pierre-Auguste Renoir","born":"1841","died":"1919","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"皮耶-奥古斯特·雷诺阿是一位著名的法国画家，也是印象派发展史上的领导人物之一。其画风承袭彼得·保罗·鲁本斯与让-安托万·华托的传统，对于女性形体的描绘最为著名。","bio_en":"Pierre-Auguste Renoir was a leading French Impressionist artist. In his depiction of feminine beauty, Renoir has been described as \"the final representative of a tradition which runs directly from Rub…","p":"images/a/Q39931.jpg"},"Paul Gauguin":{"zh":"保罗·高更","en":"Paul Gauguin","born":"1848","died":"1903","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"欧仁·亨利·保罗·高更，生于法国巴黎，印象派画家。大部份艺术史家将他归于后印象派。他的作品在其生后才开始名声大噪。 他是印象派的代表人物，除去绘画之外，在雕塑、陶艺、版画和写作上也有一定的成就。","bio_en":"Eugène Henri Paul Gauguin was a French painter, sculptor, printmaker, ceramist, and writer, whose work has been primarily associated with the Post-Impressionist and Symbolist movements.","p":"images/a/Q37693.png"},"Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec":{"zh":"亨利·德·图卢兹-劳特累克","en":"Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec","born":"1864","died":"1901","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"亨利·马里·雷蒙·德·土鲁斯-劳特累克-蒙法，简称亨利·德·土鲁斯-劳特累克，法国贵族、后印象派画家、近代海报设计与石版画艺术先驱，为人称作「蒙马特之魂」。","bio_en":"Comte Henri Marie Raymond de Toulouse-Lautrec-Montfa , known as Toulouse-Lautrec , was a French painter, printmaker, draughtsman, caricaturist, and illustrator.","p":"images/a/Q82445.jpg"},"Kazimir Malevich":{"zh":"卡济米尔·谢韦里诺维奇·马列维奇","en":"Kazimir Malevich","born":"1879","died":"1935","cty_zh":"苏联","cty_en":"Soviet Union","bio_zh":"卡济米尔·谢韦里诺维奇·马列维奇，俄罗斯前卫艺术及乌克兰前卫艺术的主要代表人物，至上主义流派的创始人，与康定斯基、蒙德里安并列为早期抽象艺术的三大代表人物，其开创性贡献深刻地影响了20世纪现代艺术的发展。","bio_en":"Kazimir Severinovich Malevich was a Russian avant-garde artist and art theorist, whose work and writings pioneered the development of abstract painting in the 20th century.","p":"images/a/Q130777.jpg"},"Marcel Duchamp":{"zh":"马塞尔·杜尚","en":"Marcel Duchamp","born":"1887","died":"1968","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"马塞尔·杜尚，法裔美籍艺术家，达达主义与观念艺术的先驱。以「现成品」《泉》和《下楼梯的裸女》颠覆了传统艺术观念，深刻影响了二十世纪当代艺术。","bio_en":"Marcel Duchamp was a French-American artist and pioneer of Dada and conceptual art whose readymades, notably Fountain, and Nude Descending a Staircase overturned traditional notions of art and shaped twentieth-century practice.","p":"images/a/Q5912.jpg"},"Marc Chagall":{"zh":"马克·夏加尔","en":"Marc Chagall","born":"1887","died":"1985","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"马克·夏卡尔，出生名莫伊舍·扎卡尔罗维奇·夏卡尔，是白俄罗斯犹太裔的俄法著名艺术家，游离于印象派、立体派、抽象表现主义等多流派间，作品形式包括绘画、素描、彩色玻璃、舞台布景、陶瓷等。","bio_en":"Marc Chagall was a Russian and French artist of Jewish ancestry. An early modernist, he was associated with the École de Paris, as well as several major artistic styles and created works in a wide ran…","p":"images/a/Q93284.jpg"},"Giorgio de Chirico":{"zh":"乔治·德·基里科","en":"Giorgio de Chirico","born":"1888","died":"1978","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"乔治·德·基里科，出生于希腊的意大利画家，形而上画派创始人。以空旷广场、拉长的阴影与古典拱廊营造出静谧而不安的梦境，启发了超现实主义。","bio_en":"Giorgio de Chirico was an Italian painter born in Greece and founder of the Metaphysical school; his empty piazzas, long shadows and classical arcades evoke a still, unsettling dreamscape that inspired Surrealism.","p":"images/a/Q156622.jpg"},"Paul Klee":{"zh":"保罗·克利","en":"Paul Klee","born":"1879","died":"1940","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"保罗·克利，是一位瑞士裔的德国籍的画家。他曾在慕尼黑美术学校学习画画，并制作了许多以黑白为主的版画和线画。1914年与好友赴突尼斯旅行期间获得灵感，从此成为了一位绘画彩色画的画家，创作出极为优异的作品，知名的作品包括Fish Magic、 …","bio_en":"Paul Klee was a Swiss-born German artist. His highly individual style was influenced by movements in art that included expressionism, cubism, and surrealism.","p":"images/a/Q44007.jpg"},"Joan Miró":{"zh":"胡安·米罗","en":"Joan Miró","born":"1893","died":"1983","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"胡安·米罗，西班牙加泰罗尼亚画家、雕塑家。以明快的色彩与富于童趣的生物形符号，构筑出充满诗意的超现实世界。","bio_en":"Joan Miró was a Catalan Spanish painter and sculptor whose bright colours and playful biomorphic signs create a poetic Surrealist world of his own.","p":"images/a/Q152384.jpg"},"René Magritte":{"zh":"勒内·马格利特","en":"René Magritte","born":"1898","died":"1967","cty_zh":"比利时","cty_en":"Belgium","bio_zh":"雷内·弗朗索瓦·吉兰·马格利特是比利时超现实主义画家，并且因为其超现实主义作品中带有些许诙谐以及许多引人审思的符号语言而闻名。他的作品对于许多观察家对于事先设想现实状况的情况提出挑战，并且影响今日许多插画风格。","bio_en":"René François Ghislain Magritte was a Belgian surrealist artist known for his depictions of familiar objects in unfamiliar, unexpected contexts, which often provoked questions about the nature and bou…","p":"images/a/Q7836.jpg"},"Frida Kahlo":{"zh":"弗里达·卡罗","en":"Frida Kahlo","born":"1907","died":"1954","cty_zh":"墨西哥","cty_en":"Mexico","bio_zh":"弗里达·卡罗，墨西哥画家，以强烈自传色彩的自画像闻名。作品融合墨西哥民间艺术与超现实意象，直面身体的苦痛、身份与女性经验。","bio_en":"Frida Kahlo was a Mexican painter known for her intensely autobiographical self-portraits, blending Mexican folk art with surreal imagery to confront physical pain, identity and female experience.","p":"images/a/Q5588.jpg"},"Edward Hopper":{"zh":"爱德华·霍普","en":"Edward Hopper","born":"1882","died":"1967","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"爱德华·霍普是一位美国绘画大师，以描绘寂寥的美国当代生活风景闻名。","bio_en":"Edward Hopper was an American realist painter and printmaker. He is one of America's most renowned artists and known for his skill in depicting modern American life and landscapes.","p":"images/a/Q203401.jpg"},"Andrew Wyeth":{"zh":"安德鲁·怀斯","en":"Andrew Wyeth","born":"1917","died":"2009","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"安德鲁·怀斯，美国现实主义画家，以蛋彩与水彩描绘宾夕法尼亚与缅因的乡间。代表作《克里斯蒂娜的世界》以细腻笔触传达孤寂与怀想。","bio_en":"Andrew Wyeth was an American Realist painter who portrayed rural Pennsylvania and Maine in tempera and watercolour; his best-known work, Christina's World, conveys solitude and longing through meticulous detail.","p":"images/a/Q316325.jpg"},"Jackson Pollock":{"zh":"杰克逊·波洛克","en":"Jackson Pollock","born":"1912","died":"1956","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"杰克逊·波洛克，美国抽象表现主义代表画家。以「滴画」技法在铺于地面的画布上泼洒、滴淌颜料，创造出充满能量的全幅式抽象绘画。","bio_en":"Jackson Pollock was a leading American Abstract Expressionist whose 'drip' technique—pouring and flinging paint onto canvas laid on the floor—produced energetic, all-over abstract paintings.","p":"images/a/Q37571.jpg"},"Mark Rothko":{"zh":"马克·罗斯科","en":"Mark Rothko","born":"1903","died":"1970","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"马克·罗斯科，出生于俄国的美国抽象表现主义画家，色域绘画的代表人物。以漂浮的大块矩形色域追求崇高、静默与直接的情感体验。","bio_en":"Mark Rothko was a Russian-born American Abstract Expressionist and leading Color Field painter whose floating rectangles of luminous colour seek the sublime, silence and direct emotional experience."},"Andy Warhol":{"zh":"安迪·沃霍尔","en":"Andy Warhol","born":"1928","died":"1987","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"安迪·沃荷，美国艺术家、印刷家、电影摄影师，是视觉艺术运动波普艺术的开创者之一。流行艺术运动的代表人物之一。安迪·沃荷在美国宾夕法尼亚州的匹兹堡出生，成长于一个移民家庭，在他的家乡匹兹堡有安迪·沃荷博物馆纪念他的作品及一生。","bio_en":"Andy Warhol was an American artist and filmmaker. Widely regarded as the most important artist of the second half of the 20th century, Warhol's practice spanned various media, including painting, film…","p":"images/a/Q5603.jpg"},"Roy Lichtenstein":{"zh":"罗伊·利希滕斯坦","en":"Roy Lichtenstein","born":"1923","died":"1997","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"罗伊·利希滕斯坦，美国波普艺术的代表画家。挪用连环漫画的图式与本戴网点，将大众文化图像转化为标志性的绘画语言。","bio_en":"Roy Lichtenstein was a leading American Pop artist who appropriated the imagery and Ben-Day dots of comic strips, turning mass-culture images into an instantly recognisable painterly language.","p":"images/a/Q151679.jpg"},"Jasper Johns":{"zh":"贾斯培·琼斯","en":"Jasper Johns","born":"1930","died":null,"cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"贾斯培·琼斯，美国当代艺术家，波普与新达达的先驱。以国旗、靶子、数字等熟悉符号入画，探讨图像、符号与观看之间的关系。","bio_en":"Jasper Johns is an American contemporary artist and a pioneer of Pop and Neo-Dada; painting familiar signs—flags, targets, numbers—he probes the relationship between image, symbol and seeing.","p":"images/a/Q155057.jpg"},"Banksy":{"zh":"班克斯","en":"Banksy","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"班克斯，身份成谜的英国街头艺术家与政治活动者。以模板喷绘在公共空间创作，作品充满反战、反消费主义与社会批判的黑色幽默。","bio_en":"Banksy is an anonymous England-based street artist and activist; working in stencilled spray paint in public spaces, the work is charged with anti-war, anti-consumerist and satirical black humour.","p":"images/a/Q133600.png"},"Auguste Rodin":{"zh":"奥古斯特·罗丹","en":"Auguste Rodin","born":"1840","died":"1917","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"奥古斯特·罗丹，法国雕塑家，被视为现代雕塑的奠基者。以《思想者》《加莱义民》《吻》等作品著称，善于以富有张力的形体表现人的情感与生命力。","bio_en":"Auguste Rodin was a French sculptor generally regarded as the founder of modern sculpture, celebrated for works such as The Thinker, The Burghers of Calais and The Kiss, in which he modelled the human form with unprecedented emotional and physical intensity.","p":"images/a/Q30755.jpg"},"Umberto Boccioni":{"zh":"翁贝托·波丘尼","en":"Umberto Boccioni","born":"1882","died":"1916","cty_zh":"意大利王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Italy","bio_zh":"翁贝托·薄邱尼是意大利的画家、雕塑家以及未来主义提倡者。弗朗切斯科·菲利皮尼 的“农业风景”是Umberto Boccioni早期创作阶段的“隐性典范”。","bio_en":"Umberto Boccioni was an influential Italian painter and sculptor. He helped shape the revolutionary aesthetic of the Futurism movement as one of its principal figures.","p":"images/a/Q152797.jpg"},"Constantin Brâncuși":{"zh":"康斯坦丁·布朗库西","en":"Constantin Brâncuși","born":"1876","died":"1957","cty_zh":"罗马尼亚","cty_en":"Romania","bio_zh":"康斯坦丁·布朗库西，罗马尼亚裔法国雕塑家，现代主义雕塑的先驱。以《空间之鸟》《吻》等作品将形体高度提炼、抽象，追求事物的本质。","bio_en":"Constantin Brâncuși was a Romanian-born French sculptor and pioneer of modernism who, in works such as Bird in Space and The Kiss, pared form down to a radical, essential abstraction.","p":"images/a/Q153048.jpg"},"Ancient Egyptian craftsmen":{"zh":"古埃及匠师","en":"Ancient Egyptian craftsmen","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Thutmose":{"zh":"图特摩斯","en":"Thutmose","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"古埃及","cty_en":"Ancient Egypt","bio_zh":"图特摩斯，古埃及第十八王朝的宫廷雕塑家，约活跃于公元前十四世纪；著名的《娜芙蒂蒂胸像》即出土于他位于阿马尔纳的工坊。","bio_en":"Thutmose was an ancient Egyptian court sculptor of the 18th Dynasty, active around the 14th century BC; the famous Bust of Nefertiti was found in his workshop at Amarna."},"Alexandros of Antioch":{"zh":"安提俄克的亚历山德罗斯","en":"Alexandros of Antioch","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"古希腊","cty_en":"Ancient Greece","bio_zh":"安提俄克的亚历山德罗斯，古希腊化时期雕塑家，被认为是《米洛的维纳斯》的作者，约活跃于公元前二世纪末。","bio_en":"Alexandros of Antioch was a Hellenistic Greek sculptor credited with the Venus de Milo, active around the late 2nd century BC.","p":"images/a/Q2415821.jpg"},"Anonymous":{"zh":"佚名","en":"Anonymous","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Myron":{"zh":"米隆","en":"Myron","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"古希腊","cty_en":"Ancient Greece","bio_zh":"米隆，古希腊古典早期雕塑家，活跃于公元前五世纪中叶。以青铜像《掷铁饼者》著称，善于捕捉运动瞬间的动势。","bio_en":"Myron was an early Classical Greek sculptor of the mid-5th century BC, celebrated for the bronze Discobolus (Discus-Thrower) and his mastery of arrested motion."},"Agesander and others":{"zh":"阿格桑德罗斯等","en":"Agesander and others","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"古希腊","cty_en":"Ancient Greece","bio_zh":"阿格桑德罗斯与另两位罗德岛雕塑家，被古罗马作家老普林尼记为《拉奥孔》群雕的作者，作品以强烈的痛苦表情与扭动的体态震撼后世。","bio_en":"Agesander and two fellow sculptors of Rhodes are named by Pliny the Elder as creators of the Laocoön group, whose anguished expressions and writhing forms astonished later ages."},"Qin dynasty artisans":{"zh":"秦代工匠","en":"Qin dynasty artisans","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Zhang Zeduan":{"zh":"张择端","en":"Zhang Zeduan","born":"1085","died":"1145","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"张择端，北宋画家，以长卷《清明上河图》闻名。作品生动描绘北宋都城汴京的市井百态，是中国风俗画的巅峰之作。","bio_en":"Zhang Zeduan was a Northern Song painter famed for the handscroll Along the River During the Qingming Festival, a panoramic masterpiece of Chinese genre painting depicting daily life in the capital Bianjing."},"Huang Gongwang":{"zh":"黄公望","en":"Huang Gongwang","born":"1269","died":"1354","cty_zh":"元朝","cty_en":"Yuan dynasty","bio_zh":"黄公望，字子久，号大痴、大痴道人、一峰道人，平江路常熟州人，元朝画家。","bio_en":"Huang Gongwang , birth name Lu Jian , was a Chinese painter, poet and writer born at the end of the Song dynasty in Changshu, Jiangsu.","p":"images/a/Q702525.jpg"},"Wang Ximeng":{"zh":"王希孟","en":"Wang Ximeng","born":"1096","died":"1119","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"王希孟，北宋天才画家，约十八岁绘成青绿山水长卷《千里江山图》，画成后不久即早逝，是中国山水画史上的传奇。","bio_en":"Wang Ximeng was a prodigy of the Northern Song who painted the monumental blue-green landscape A Thousand Li of Rivers and Mountains around the age of eighteen and died soon after—a legend of Chinese landscape painting."},"Gu Kaizhi (Song copy)":{"zh":"顾恺之（宋摹）","en":"Gu Kaizhi (Song copy)","born":"344","died":"406","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"顾恺之，东晋画家、绘画理论家，被誉为「画绝」。传世《女史箴图》（今存宋摹本）以「以形写神」的笔法，成为中国人物画的典范。","bio_en":"Gu Kaizhi was an Eastern Jin painter and theorist revered as a founding master of Chinese figure painting; the Admonitions Scroll, surviving in a later Song copy, exemplifies his ideal of conveying spirit through form."},"Gu Hongzhong":{"zh":"顾闳中","en":"Gu Hongzhong","born":"910","died":"980","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"顾闳中，五代南唐宫廷画家。奉命夜访大臣韩熙载府邸，凭记忆绘成《韩熙载夜宴图》，细腻记录了夜宴的场景与人物神态。","bio_en":"Gu Hongzhong was a court painter of the Southern Tang; sent to observe the minister Han Xizai's household by night, he painted the Night Revels of Han Xizai from memory, minutely recording the banquet and its figures.","p":"images/a/Q740673.jpg"},"Dunhuang artisans":{"zh":"敦煌匠师","en":"Dunhuang artisans","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Tang dynasty artisans":{"zh":"唐代匠师","en":"Tang dynasty artisans","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Persian court painters":{"zh":"波斯宫廷画师","en":"Persian court painters","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Ustad Ahmad Lahori":{"zh":"乌斯塔德·艾哈迈德","en":"Ustad Ahmad Lahori","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"莫卧儿帝国","cty_en":"Mughal Empire","bio_zh":"乌斯塔德·艾哈迈德·拉合里，莫卧儿帝国建筑家，被认为是泰姬陵的首席设计师，在沙贾汗时期主持了这座白色大理石陵墓的营建。","bio_en":"Ustad Ahmad Lahori was a Mughal architect regarded as the chief designer of the Taj Mahal, overseeing construction of the white marble mausoleum under Shah Jahan."},"Polykleitos":{"zh":"波留克列特斯","en":"Polykleitos","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"古希腊","cty_en":"Ancient Greece","bio_zh":"波留克列特斯，古希腊古典时期雕塑家，活跃于公元前五世纪。提出人体比例的「法则」，代表作《持矛者》成为理想人体的典范。","bio_en":"Polykleitos was a Classical Greek sculptor of the 5th century BC who formulated the Canon of ideal human proportion, exemplified by his Doryphoros (Spear-Bearer)."},"Canaletto":{"zh":"卡纳莱托","en":"Canaletto","born":"1697","died":"1768","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"吉奥瓦尼·安东尼奥·卡纳尔，意大利威尼斯共和国画家，是18世纪威尼斯画派的代表画家之一。 他是一位城市景观画家，画过威尼斯、罗马和伦敦的城市风光，也画过虚构的风景，尽管在他的作品中，真实与虚构的界限从来都不十分明确。","bio_en":"Giovanni Antonio Canal , commonly known as Canaletto , was an Italian painter from the Republic of Venice, considered an important member of the 18th-century Venetian school.","p":"images/a/Q182664.jpg"},"Thomas Gainsborough":{"zh":"托马斯·庚斯博罗","en":"Thomas Gainsborough","born":"1727","died":"1788","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"托马斯·庚斯博罗RA FRSARA FRSA—1788年8月2日）是一位英国肖像画及风景画家。他是皇家艺术研究院的创始人之一，曾为英国皇室绘制过许多作品，并与竞争对手约书亚·雷诺兹同为18世纪末期英国著名肖像画家。","bio_en":"Thomas Gainsborough – 2 August 1788) was an English painter, draughtsman and printmaker who specialised in portrait and landscape painting.","p":"images/a/Q192720.jpg"},"Fra Angelico":{"zh":"弗拉·安杰利科","en":"Fra Angelico","born":"1390","died":"1455","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"真福安杰利科修士本名圭多·迪·彼得，意大利早期文艺复兴画家，艺术史学家瓦萨里在其巨著艺苑名人传中称赞其拥有“稀世罕见的天才”。 安杰利科的同时代人称他作“菲耶索莱的若望修士”或“若望·安杰利科修士”…","bio_en":"Fra Giovanni da Fiesole , known posthumously as Fra Angelico , was an Italian Dominican friar and painter active during the early Florentine Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5664.jpg"},"Paolo Uccello":{"zh":"保罗·乌切洛","en":"Paolo Uccello","born":"1397","died":"1475","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"保罗·乌切洛，原名保罗·迪·多诺，意大利画家。由于乌切洛生活于中世纪末期和文艺复兴初期，因此他的作品相应地也呈现出跨时代的特征：他将晚期哥特式和透视法这两种不同的艺术潮流融合在了一起。","bio_en":"Paolo Uccello , born Paolo di Dono, was an Italian Renaissance painter and mathematician from Florence who was notable for his pioneering work on visual perspective in art.","p":"images/a/Q192488.jpg"},"Piero della Francesca":{"zh":"皮耶罗·德拉·弗朗切斯卡","en":"Piero della Francesca","born":"1415","died":"1492","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"皮耶罗·德拉·弗朗切斯卡，意大利文艺复兴早期画家兼理论家。弗朗切斯卡是皮鞋制造商的儿子，早年受到优良教育，1439年与人合作为佛罗伦萨新圣母医院创作湿壁画组画。","bio_en":"Piero della Francesca was an Italian painter, mathematician and geometer of the Early Renaissance, nowadays chiefly appreciated for his art.","p":"images/a/Q5822.jpg"},"Andrea Mantegna":{"zh":"安德烈亚·曼特尼亚","en":"Andrea Mantegna","born":"1431","died":"1506","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"安德烈亚·曼特尼亚是一名意大利画家，也是北意大利第一位文艺复兴画家。他是罗马考古学家雅科波·贝利尼的女婿及学生。安德烈亚在透视法上做了很多尝试，以此创造更宏大更震撼的视觉效果，如《哀悼死去的基督》中他选择从基督的脚的角度描绘基督的尸体。","bio_en":"Andrea Mantegna was an Italian Renaissance painter, a student of Roman archaeology, and the son-in-law of Jacopo Bellini.","p":"images/a/Q5681.jpg"},"Giorgione":{"zh":"乔尔乔内","en":"Giorgione","born":"1478","died":"1510","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"乔尔乔内，是意大利文艺复兴艺术大师。威尼斯画派画家。","bio_en":"Giorgio Barbarelli da Castelfranco , known as Giorgione, was an Italian painter of the Venetian school during the High Renaissance, who died in his thirties.","p":"images/a/Q8459.jpg"},"Parmigianino":{"zh":"帕尔米贾尼诺","en":"Parmigianino","born":"1503","died":"1540","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"吉罗拉莫·弗朗切斯科·马里亚·马佐拉，人称帕尔米贾尼诺，意大利文艺复兴时期的矫饰主义风格画家，同时他也是一名版画家，活跃于佛罗伦萨、罗马、博洛尼亚、帕尔马等意大利诸城。","bio_en":"Girolamo Francesco Maria Mazzola , also known as Francesco Mazzola or, more commonly, as Parmigianino , was an Italian Mannerist painter and printmaker active in Florence, Rome, Bologna, and his nativ…","p":"images/a/Q9348.jpg"},"Bronzino":{"zh":"布伦齐诺","en":"Bronzino","born":"1503","died":"1572","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"布龙齐诺，全名阿纽洛·迪·科西莫，亦称尼奥洛·布龙齐诺。是意大利佛罗伦萨的风格主义画家。布龙齐诺这个昵称的来历已不可考，但是应该和他黝黑的肤色或者他常用的肖像画主题有关。","bio_en":"Agnolo di Cosimo , usually known as Bronzino or Agnolo Bronzino, was an Italian Mannerist painter from Florence.","p":"images/a/Q7803.jpg"},"El Greco":{"zh":"埃尔·格列柯","en":"El Greco","born":"1541","died":"1614","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"多米尼克·提托克波洛斯，西班牙文艺复兴时期的画家、雕塑家与建筑师。因其希腊裔血统，他常被人们称为埃尔·格列柯。 格列柯出生于克里特岛，原受传统绘画教育，直到26岁时动身前往威尼斯旅行，画风随即突变。","bio_en":"Doménikos Theotokópoulos , most widely known as El Greco , was a Greek painter, sculptor and architect of the Spanish Renaissance, regarded as one of the greatest artists of all time.","p":"images/a/Q301.jpg"},"Paolo Veronese":{"zh":"保罗·委罗内塞","en":"Paolo Veronese","born":"1528","died":"1588","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"保罗·委罗内塞）是意大利文艺复兴时代的画家。委罗内塞与年长一代的提香，以及年长十岁的丁托列托，一起构成16世纪文艺复兴晚期主宰威尼斯画派的“三杰”。","bio_en":"Paolo Caliari , known as Paolo Veronese , was an Italian Renaissance painter based in Venice, known for extremely large history paintings of religion and mythology, such as The Wedding at Cana and The…","p":"images/a/Q9440.jpg"},"Jan Davidsz. de Heem":{"zh":"扬·达维茨·德·海姆","en":"Jan Davidsz. de Heem","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null,"p":"images/a/Q454656.jpg"},"Albrecht Dürer":{"zh":"阿尔布雷希特·丢勒","en":"Albrecht Dürer","born":"1471","died":"1528","cty_zh":"巴伐利亚公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Bavaria","bio_zh":"阿尔布雷希特‧丢勒，德国文艺复兴时期画家、版画家。 丢勒在青少年时期即投入于绘画活动，在米凯尔·瓦格莫特的工作室担任学徒，并有突出表现。","bio_en":"Albrecht Dürer , sometimes spelled in English as Durer or Duerer, was a German painter, printmaker, and theorist of the German Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5580.jpg"},"Matthias Grünewald":{"zh":"马蒂亚斯·格吕内瓦尔德","en":"Matthias Grünewald","born":"1480","died":"1528","cty_zh":"德国","cty_en":"Germany","bio_zh":"马蒂亚斯·格吕内瓦尔德，真名为马蒂亚斯·哥特哈德，德国文艺复兴时期画家，不过他仍坚持中世纪哥特式传统，是德国哥特式绘画的最后一位伟大代表。","bio_en":"Matthias Grünewald was a German Renaissance painter of religious works who ignored Renaissance classicism to continue the style of late medieval Central European art into the 16th century.","p":"images/a/Q154338.jpg"},"Ilya Repin":{"zh":"伊利亚·列宾","en":"Ilya Repin","born":"1844","died":"1930","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"伊利亚·叶菲莫维奇·列宾，乌克兰沙俄时期现实主义画家，巡回展览画派的主要代表人物。","bio_en":"Ilya Yefimovich Repin was a Ukrainian-born Russian painter. He became one of the most renowned artists in Russia in the 19th century.","p":"images/a/Q172911.jpg"},"Ivan Aivazovsky":{"zh":"伊万·康斯坦丁诺维奇·艾瓦佐夫斯基","en":"Ivan Aivazovsky","born":"1817","died":"1900","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"伊万·康斯坦丁诺维奇·艾瓦佐夫斯基，俄罗斯亚美尼亚裔画家，他居住和生活在克里米亚，以海景画著名，此类画作占其作品大半部分。","bio_en":"Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky was a Russian Romantic painter who is considered one of the greatest masters of marine art.","p":"images/a/Q181568.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/8ae9eff5d369995d380e8b3a3c59c98e":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/8ae9eff5d369995d380e8b3a3c59c98e","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/8ae9eff5d369995d380e8b3a3c59c98e","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"James McNeill Whistler":{"zh":"詹姆斯·惠斯勒","en":"James McNeill Whistler","born":"1834","died":"1903","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"詹姆斯·惠斯勒，著名印象派画家，父亲是美国工程师，全家曾居于圣彼得堡。惠斯勒曾入读西点军校，之后自选画家为职业。 惠斯勒出生于马萨诸塞州，21岁时怀着成为艺术家的雄心前往巴黎。","bio_en":"James Abbott McNeill Whistler was an American painter in oils and watercolor, and printmaker, active during the American Gilded Age and based primarily in the United Kingdom.","p":"images/a/Q203643.jpg"},"Ivan Shishkin":{"zh":"伊凡·伊凡诺维奇·希施金","en":"Ivan Shishkin","born":"1831","died":"1898","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"伊凡·伊凡诺维奇·希施金，俄国风景画家。 1832年出生于叶拉布加商人家庭，童年在维亚特省度过，对当地的自然景色和森林留下深刻的印象。","bio_en":"Ivan Ivanovich Shishkin was a Russian Realist painter and draughtsman, best known for his landscape subjects. One of the most notable artisans to emerge during Tsar Alexander II's reign, he was among …","p":"images/a/Q193064.jpg"},"Hugo Simberg":{"zh":"胡戈·辛贝里","en":"Hugo Simberg","born":"1873","died":"1917","cty_zh":"芬兰大公国","cty_en":"Grand Duchy of Finland","bio_zh":"胡戈·耶哈德·辛贝里是一位芬兰画家和图形设计师。他是芬兰艺术史上象征主义的代表人物。他和阿克塞利·加伦-卡勒拉一道在20世纪初期把象征主义的思潮带入芬兰艺术界并探索新的欧洲艺术方向。","bio_en":"Hugo Gerhard Simberg was a Finnish symbolist painter and graphic artist.","p":"images/a/Q263080.jpg"},"Joseph Wright of Derby":{"zh":"约瑟夫·赖特","en":"Joseph Wright of Derby","born":"1734","died":"1797","cty_zh":"大不列颠王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Great Britain","bio_zh":"约瑟夫·赖特（人称「德比的赖特」），英国画家，擅长肖像与风景，尤以描绘烛光、炉火等人工光源下的科学与工业题材著称。","bio_en":"Joseph Wright , styled Joseph Wright of Derby, was an English painter who specialised in portrait painting and landscape art.","p":"images/a/Q214062.jpg"},"Ivan Kramskoi":{"zh":"伊万·克拉姆斯柯依","en":"Ivan Kramskoi","born":"1837","died":"1887","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"伊万·尼古拉耶维奇·克拉姆斯科伊，其姓氏也译克拉姆斯柯依、科拉姆斯柯伊，19世纪下半叶俄国著名的画家和艺术评论家。他是俄国艺术史上的重要人物，是独立艺术组织的创始人和精神领袖。","bio_en":"Ivan Nikolayevich Kramskoi was a Russian Realist painter and art critic. One of the most prominent artisans during Tsar Alexander II's reign, he is remembered as co-founding member and public frontman…","p":"images/a/Q207758.jpg"},"Henri Rousseau":{"zh":"亨利·卢梭","en":"Henri Rousseau","born":"1844","died":"1910","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"亨利·朱利安·费利克斯·卢梭是法国后印象派画家，以纯真、原始的风格著称。 他曾经是一名海关的收税员，也是自学成才的天才画家，其作品具有极高的艺术水准。","bio_en":"Henri Julien Félix Rousseau was a French post-Impressionist painter in the Naïve or Primitive manner. He was also known as Le Douanier , a humorous description of his occupation as a toll and tax coll…","p":"images/a/Q156386.jpg"},"Karl Bryullov":{"zh":"卡尔·布留洛夫","en":"Karl Bryullov","born":"1799","died":"1852","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"卡尔·巴甫洛维奇·布留洛夫是俄国著名画家，俄国19世纪上半期学院派的代表大师，新古典主义至浪漫主义转型时期的关键人物之一。","bio_en":"Karl Pavlovich Bryullov was a Russian painter and draughtsman during the Romantic period, remembered among the greatest visual artists in the history of Russian art.","p":"images/a/Q4768.jpg"},"John Singer Sargent":{"zh":"约翰·辛格·沙金","en":"John Singer Sargent","born":"1856","died":"1925","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"约翰·辛格·萨金特，美国艺术家，因为描绘了爱德华时代的奢华，所以是“当时的领军肖像画家”。他在一生中创作了900幅油画，2,000多幅水彩画，以及无数幅素描画、炭笔画。","bio_en":"John Singer Sargent was an American expatriate artist, considered the \"leading portrait painter of his generation\" for his evocations of Belle Époque and Edwardian-era luxury.","p":"images/a/Q155626.jpg"},"Petrus Christus":{"zh":"彼得鲁斯·克里斯蒂","en":"Petrus Christus","born":"1425","died":"1475","cty_zh":"南尼德兰","cty_en":"Southern Netherlands","bio_zh":"彼得鲁斯·克里斯蒂，是活跃于15世纪的尼德兰画家。","bio_en":"Petrus Christus was an Early Netherlandish painter active in Bruges from 1444, where, along with Hans Memling, he became the leading painter after the death of Jan van Eyck.","p":"images/a/Q312616.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/20e9cd436e0998b3d9617764a486424c":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/20e9cd436e0998b3d9617764a486424c","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/20e9cd436e0998b3d9617764a486424c","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Frederic Leighton":{"zh":"第一代雷顿男爵弗雷德里克·雷顿","en":"Frederic Leighton","born":"1830","died":"1896","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"第一代雷顿男爵弗雷德里克·雷顿，PRA[?]，1878年至1896年称为弗雷德里克·雷顿爵士，英国学院派画家和雕塑家，皇家艺术研究院院长。","bio_en":"Frederic Leighton, 1st Baron Leighton, , known as Sir Frederic Leighton between 1878 and 1896, was a British Victorian painter, draughtsman, and sculptor.","p":"images/a/Q160252.jpg"},"Emanuel Leutze":{"zh":"埃马努埃尔·洛伊策","en":"Emanuel Leutze","born":"1816","died":"1868","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"埃马努埃尔·戈特利布·洛伊策是一位德裔美国画家，以作品《华盛顿横渡特拉华河》著名。","bio_en":"Emanuel Gottlieb Leutze was a German-born American history painter, best known for his 1851 painting Washington Crossing the Delaware.","p":"images/a/Q452321.jpg"},"William-Adolphe Bouguereau":{"zh":"威廉·阿道夫·布格罗","en":"William-Adolphe Bouguereau","born":"1825","died":"1905","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"威廉·阿道夫·布格罗，是19世纪末的法国学院派最重要的画家之一。布格罗的绘画常以神话为灵感，以19世纪的现实主义绘画技巧来诠释古典主义的题材，并且经常以女性的躯体作为描绘对象。","bio_en":"William-Adolphe Bouguereau ʁo]; 30 November 1825 – 19 August 1905) was a French academic painter. In his realistic genre paintings, he used mythological themes, making modern interpretations of classi…","p":"images/a/Q483992.jpg"},"Rogier van der Weyden":{"zh":"罗希尔·范德魏登","en":"Rogier van der Weyden","born":"1390","died":"1464","cty_zh":"勃艮第尼德兰","cty_en":"Burgundian Netherlands","bio_zh":"罗希尔·范德魏登，出生于今天的比利时图尔奈，是早期尼德兰画家，现存作品以宗教三联画、祭坛画、单人或双人肖像画为主。著名作品有《最后的审判》。","bio_en":"Rogier van der Weyden ]; 1399 or 1400 – 18 June 1464), initially known as Roger de la Pasture la pastyʁ]), was an early Netherlandish painter whose surviving works consist mainly of religious triptych…","p":"images/a/Q68631.jpg"},"Hans Memling":{"zh":"汉斯·梅姆林","en":"Hans Memling","born":"1435","died":"1494","cty_zh":"德国","cty_en":"Germany","bio_zh":"汉斯·梅姆林是一位德裔早期尼德兰画家，曾在罗希尔·范德魏登于布鲁塞尔的画室中作画，范德魏登死后梅姆林成为布鲁日市民，成为了当地的主要画家之一。","bio_en":"Hans Memling was a German-Flemish painter who worked in the tradition of Early Netherlandish painting. Born in the Middle Rhine region, he probably spent his childhood in Mainz.","p":"images/a/Q106851.jpg"},"Henry Fuseli":{"zh":"约翰·亨利希·菲斯利","en":"Henry Fuseli","born":"1741","died":"1825","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"约翰·亨利希·菲斯利是一位德国-瑞士裔的英国画家、制图员及艺术家。","bio_en":"Henry Fuseli was a Swiss painter, draughtsman, and writer on art who spent much of his career in Britain. Many of his successful works depict supernatural experiences, such as The Nightmare.","p":"images/a/Q122382.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/aff25ac9d91201867caca2ac3df7ceb8":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/aff25ac9d91201867caca2ac3df7ceb8","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/aff25ac9d91201867caca2ac3df7ceb8","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Gustave Caillebotte":{"zh":"古斯塔夫·卡耶博特","en":"Gustave Caillebotte","born":"1848","died":"1894","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"古斯塔夫·卡耶博特，法国印象派画家。 卡耶博特出生于富贵家庭，除了自己作画，也不断购买同时代印象派画家好友们的绘画。他的收藏包括：莫奈14幅、毕沙罗19幅、雷诺阿10幅、西斯莱9幅、德加7幅、塞尚5幅、马奈4幅。","bio_en":"Gustave Caillebotte was a French painter who was a member and patron of the Impressionists, although he painted in a more realistic manner than many others in the group.","p":"images/a/Q295144.jpg"},"John William Waterhouse":{"zh":"约翰·威廉·沃特豪斯","en":"John William Waterhouse","born":"1849","died":"1917","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"约翰·威廉·沃特豪斯，英国新古典主义与前拉斐尔派画家。以其用鲜明色彩和神秘的画风描绘古典神话与传说中的女性人物而闻名于世。","bio_en":"John William Waterhouse was an English painter known for working first in the Academic style and for then embracing the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood's style and subject matter.","p":"images/a/Q212754.jpg"},"Giovanni Bellini":{"zh":"乔瓦尼·贝利尼","en":"Giovanni Bellini","born":"1430","died":"1516","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"乔瓦尼·贝利尼是一位意大利文艺复兴时期威尼斯画派的画家。 他在雅科波·贝利尼家中被抚养长大，雅科波·贝利尼因此被认为是他的父亲；但是，他们之间的亲属关系后来在有关研究中被怀疑。","bio_en":"Giovanni Bellini was an Italian Renaissance painter, probably the best known of the Bellini family of Venetian painters.","p":"images/a/Q17169.jpg"},"Jacopo Tintoretto":{"zh":"丁托列托","en":"Jacopo Tintoretto","born":"1519","died":"1594","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"丁托列托，原名雅科波·康明，是意大利文艺复兴晚期最后一位伟大的画家，和提香、委罗内塞并称为威尼斯画派的“三杰”之一。","bio_en":"Jacopo Robusti , best known as Tintoretto , was an Italian Renaissance painter of the Venetian school. His contemporaries both admired and criticised the speed with which he painted and the unpreceden…","p":"images/a/Q9319.jpg"},"Antonio da Correggio":{"zh":"安东尼奥·达·柯勒乔","en":"Antonio da Correggio","born":"1489","died":"1534","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":"Signoria di Correggio","bio_zh":"安东尼奥·阿莱格里·达·柯勒乔，常称柯勒乔，意大利画家。他是文艺复兴时期帕尔马画派的创始人，创作出16世纪最蓬勃有力和奢华的画作。他的画风酝酿了巴洛克艺术，而其优美的风格又影响了18世纪的法国。","bio_en":"Antonio Allegri da Correggio , usually known as just Correggio , was an Italian Renaissance painter who was the foremost painter of the Parma school of the High Renaissance, who was responsible for so…","p":"images/a/Q8457.jpg"},"Egon Schiele":{"zh":"埃贡·席勒","en":"Egon Schiele","born":"1890","died":"1918","cty_zh":"内莱塔尼亚","cty_en":"Cisleithania","bio_zh":"埃贡·席勒是奥地利画家，师承古斯塔夫·克林姆，是20世纪初期重要的表现主义画家，席勒的作品特色是表现力强烈，描绘扭曲的人物和肢体，且主题多是自画像。","bio_en":"Egon Leo Adolf Ludwig Schiele was an Austrian Expressionist painter. His work is noted for its intensity and its raw sexuality, and for the many self-portraits the artist produced, including nude self…","p":"images/a/Q44032.jpg"},"Mary Cassatt":{"zh":"玛丽·卡萨特","en":"Mary Cassatt","born":"1844","died":"1926","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"玛丽·斯蒂文森·卡萨特是美国画家和版画家，但她一生中大部分时间是居住在法国，并成为印象派画家。 卡萨特善于描绘女人，尤其是母子关系的作品。","bio_en":"Mary Stevenson Cassatt was an American painter and printmaker. She was born in Allegheny, Pennsylvania , but lived most of her adult life in France, where she befriended Edgar Degas and exhibited with…","p":"images/a/Q173223.jpg"},"François Boucher":{"zh":"弗朗索瓦·布歇","en":"François Boucher","born":"1703","died":"1770","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"弗朗索瓦·布歇 ，18世纪法国画家，洛可可风格的代表人物。曾在路易十五宫廷中担任首席画师，是庞巴度夫人最为赏识的画家。 布歇的作品种类广泛，数量惊人，将洛可可时期的精致、细腻、优雅与浮华表现到极致。","bio_en":"François Boucher was a French painter, draughtsman and etcher, who worked in the Rococo style. Boucher is known for his idyllic and voluptuous paintings on classical themes, decorative allegories, and…","p":"images/a/Q180932.jpg"},"Jean-Léon Gérôme":{"zh":"让-莱昂·热罗姆","en":"Jean-Léon Gérôme","born":"1824","died":"1904","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-莱昂·热罗姆是一位法国历史画画家。 在十九世纪中、后期，印象主义风行法国甚至全世界，不过在当时的法国也有另一股逆流，坚守学院派的古典主义，让-莱昂·热罗姆就是其中之一。","bio_en":"Jean-Léon Gérôme was a French painter and sculptor in the style now known as academicism. His paintings were so widely reproduced that he was \"arguably the world's most famous living artist by 1880.","p":"images/a/Q212499.jpg"},"Amedeo Modigliani":{"zh":"阿梅代奥·莫迪利亚尼","en":"Amedeo Modigliani","born":"1884","died":"1920","cty_zh":"意大利王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Italy","bio_zh":"亚美迪欧·莫迪利亚尼，意大利艺术家、画家和雕塑家，为表现主义画派的代表艺术家之一。 莫迪利亚尼的特色是大胆创作裸女画，曾受到当代保守风气严厉批评，时至后世才获得认可。","bio_en":"Amedeo Clemente Modigliani was an Italian painter and sculptor of the École de Paris who worked mainly in France.","p":"images/a/Q120993.jpg"},"Edward Burne-Jones":{"zh":"爱德华·伯恩-琼斯","en":"Edward Burne-Jones","born":"1833","died":"1898","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"爱德华·科利·伯恩-琼斯从男爵是一位英国艺术家和设计师，与前拉斐尔兄弟会有密切联系。他是威廉·莫里斯的朋友，创作过包括彩色玻璃在内的许多装饰艺术品。","bio_en":"Sir Edward Coley Burne-Jones, 1st Baronet was an English painter and designer associated with the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood's style and subject matter.","p":"images/a/Q216406.jpg"},"Giuseppe Arcimboldo":{"zh":"朱塞佩·阿尔钦博托","en":"Giuseppe Arcimboldo","born":"1527","died":"1593","cty_zh":"米兰公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Milan","bio_zh":"朱塞佩·阿尔钦博托是意大利文艺复兴时期著名肖像画家，他的作品包括挂毯设计和彩色玻璃装饰设计，他的作品特点是用水果、蔬菜、花、书、鱼等各种物体来堆砌成人物的肖像。","bio_en":"Giuseppe Arcimboldo, also spelled Arcimboldi , was an Italian Mannerist painter best known for creating imaginative portrait heads made entirely of objects such as fruits, vegetables, flowers, fish an…","p":"images/a/Q7751.jpg"},"George Frederic Watts":{"zh":"乔治·弗雷德里克·沃茨","en":"George Frederic Watts","born":"1817","died":"1904","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"乔治·弗雷德里克·沃茨是一位英国画家、雕塑家，与象征主义运动有关。他说：“我画的是思想，而不是东西。” 沃茨一生以寓言作品而闻名，例如他的著名作品《希望》、《爱与生命》、《体能》等。","bio_en":"George Frederic Watts was a British painter and sculptor associated with the Symbolist movement. Watts became famous in his lifetime for his allegorical works, such as Hope and Love and Life.","p":"images/a/Q183245.jpg"},"Giotto":{"zh":"乔托·迪·邦多内","en":"Giotto","born":"1276","died":"1337","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"乔托·迪·邦多内，中世纪晚期意大利画家与建筑师，被认为是意大利文艺复兴时期的开创者，享有\"西方绘画之父\"的美誉。","bio_en":"Giotto di Bondone , known mononymously as Giotto, was an Italian painter and architect from Florence during the Late Middle Ages.","p":"images/a/Q7814.jpg"},"John Trumbull":{"zh":"约翰·特伦布","en":"John Trumbull","born":"1756","died":"1843","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"约翰·特朗布尔，美国画家、军官，曾亲历美国独立战争，以描绘独立战争的历史画闻名，其《独立宣言》一作广为流传。","bio_en":"John Trumbull was an American painter and military officer best known for his historical paintings of the American Revolutionary War, of which he was a veteran.","p":"images/a/Q369263.jpg"},"William Holman Hunt":{"zh":"威廉·霍尔曼·亨特","en":"William Holman Hunt","born":"1827","died":"1910","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"威廉·霍尔曼·亨特，OM，英国画家。他是前拉斐尔派的创始人之一。","bio_en":"William Holman Hunt was an English painter and one of the founders of the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood. His paintings were notable for their great attention to detail, vivid colour, and elaborate symbol…","p":"images/a/Q211763.jpg"},"Domenico Ghirlandaio":{"zh":"多梅尼科·吉兰达约","en":"Domenico Ghirlandaio","born":"1448","died":"1494","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"多梅尼科·吉兰达约是一位意大利文艺复兴时期的画家，也是佛罗伦萨在文艺复兴时期涌现的的第三代画家之一。他曾与其兄弟达维德·吉兰达约、贝内代托·吉兰达约及妹夫塞巴斯蒂亚诺·马伊纳尔迪等家族成员一起组建了一个大型画室，并担任其中的领导人物。","bio_en":"Domenico di Tommaso Curradi di Doffo Bigordi , professionally known as Domenico Ghirlandaio , was an Italian Renaissance painter born in Florence.","p":"images/a/Q191423.jpg"},"Hans Gude":{"zh":"汉斯·古德","en":"Hans Gude","born":"1814","died":"1876","cty_zh":"挪威","cty_en":"Norway","bio_zh":"汉斯·古德，挪威浪漫民族主义风景画家，杜塞尔多夫画派的代表人物，常与蒂德曼合作，代表作《哈当厄尔的婚礼行舟》。","bio_en":"Hans Gude was a Norwegian Romantic-nationalist landscape painter and a leading figure of the Düsseldorf school, best known for Bridal Voyage in Hardanger, painted with Adolph Tidemand.","p":"images/a/Q701669.jpg"},"Norman Rockwell":{"zh":"诺曼·洛克威尔","en":"Norman Rockwell","born":"1894","died":"1978","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"诺曼·洛克威尔，是美国在20世纪早期的重要画家及插画家，作品横跨商业宣传与美国文化。他一生中的绘画作品大都经由《星期六晚邮报》刊出，其中最知名的系列作品是在1940和50年代出现的，如《四大自由》与《女子铆钉工》。","bio_en":"Norman Percevel Rockwell was an American painter and illustrator. His works have a broad popular appeal in the United States for their reflection of the country's culture.","p":"images/a/Q271884.jpg"},"Thomas Eakins":{"zh":"托马斯·埃金斯","en":"Thomas Eakins","born":"1844","died":"1916","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"托马斯·考珀思韦特·埃金斯，美国现实主义画家、摄影家、雕塑家及艺术教育家，被誉为美国绘画之父。","bio_en":"Thomas Cowperthwait Eakins was an American realist painter, photographer, sculptor, and fine arts educator. He is widely acknowledged to be one of the most important American artists.","p":"images/a/Q214905.jpg"},"Frans Hals":{"zh":"弗兰斯·哈尔斯","en":"Frans Hals","born":"1582","died":"1666","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"弗兰斯·哈尔斯，荷兰黄金时代肖像画家，以大胆流畅的笔触和打破传统的鲜明画风闻名于世。","bio_en":"Frans Hals the Elder was a Dutch Golden Age painter. He lived and worked in Haarlem, a city in which the local authority of the day frowned on religious painting in places of worship but citizens like…","p":"images/a/Q167654.jpg"},"Paul Delaroche":{"zh":"德拉罗什","en":"Paul Delaroche","born":"1797","died":"1856","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"伊波利特·保罗·德拉罗什是法国著名的学院派画家之一。 德拉罗什出身于一个富裕家庭，师从于画家格罗学画，1822年首次在沙龙中展出自己的作品，在当时非常出名，一直从事美术教育工作，直到1843年。","bio_en":"Hippolyte-Paul Delaroche was a French painter known for his depiction of scenes from English and French history.","p":"images/a/Q322582.jpg"},"Ford Madox Brown":{"zh":"福特·布朗","en":"Ford Madox Brown","born":"1821","died":"1893","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"福特·马多克斯·布朗是一位英国画家，擅长描绘道德和历史主题，以独特的图形风格以及威廉·贺加斯式的前拉斐尔派风格而闻名。他最著名的作品无疑是《作品》。","bio_en":"Ford Madox Brown was a British painter of moral and historical subjects, notable for his distinctively graphic and often Hogarthian version of the Pre-Raphaelite style.","p":"images/a/Q319843.jpg"},"Aleksander Gierymski":{"zh":"亚历山大·吉列姆斯基","en":"Aleksander Gierymski","born":"1850","died":"1901","cty_zh":"波兰","cty_en":"Poland","bio_zh":"亚历山大·吉列姆斯基是19世纪后期的波兰画家，他的作品以现实主义以及印象派为主。","bio_en":"Ignacy Aleksander Gierymski was a Polish painter of the late 19th century, the younger brother of Maksymilian Gierymski.","p":"images/a/Q958927.jpg"},"Vasily Vereshchagin":{"zh":"瓦西里·韦雷什查金","en":"Vasily Vereshchagin","born":"1842","died":"1904","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"瓦西里·韦列夏金俄罗斯知名战争艺术家、画家，是俄罗斯最早享誉世界的艺术家之一，他的作品多采用现实主义刻画了战争的残酷场景，导致他的不少画作从未得到展示。","bio_en":"Vasily Vasilyevich Vereshchagin was a Russian painter, war artist, and traveller. The graphic nature of his realist scenes led to many of them never being printed or exhibited to the public.","p":"images/a/Q127017.jpg"},"Jan Matejko":{"zh":"扬·马特伊科","en":"Jan Matejko","born":"1838","died":"1893","cty_zh":"克拉科夫自由市","cty_en":"Free City of Kraków","bio_zh":"扬·马泰科，波兰历史画家，以描绘波兰历史上的重大事件而闻名于世。他不仅是19世纪波兰最杰出的艺术家之一，亦被公认为波兰国家身份与历史记忆的视觉塑造者。","bio_en":"Jan Alojzy Matejko was a Polish painter, a leading 19th-century exponent of history painting, known for depicting nodal events from Polish history.","p":"images/a/Q189117.jpg"},"Carlo Crivelli":{"zh":"卡罗·克里韦利","en":"Carlo Crivelli","born":"1430","died":"1490","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"卡罗·克里韦利，文艺复兴时期欧洲艺术家。他出生于威尼斯，童年在威尼托度过，在意大利中部马尔凯大区偏僻的小镇阿斯科利皮切诺度过了一生。","bio_en":"Carlo Crivelli was an Italian Renaissance painter of conservative Late Gothic decorative sensibility, who spent his early years in the Veneto, where he absorbed influences from the Vivarini, Squarcion…"},"Antonello da Messina":{"zh":"安东内洛·达·梅西纳","en":"Antonello da Messina","born":"1430","died":"1479","cty_zh":"西西里王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Sicily","bio_zh":"安东内洛·达·梅西纳，是意大利文艺复兴时期的艺术家，他来自西西里。他的作品受到了早期尼德兰美术的影响。他将这种影响带给了威尼斯画派。","bio_en":"Antonello da Messina mesˈsiːna]; c. 1425–1430 – February 1479), properly Antonello di Giovanni di Antonio, but also called Antonello degli Antoni and Anglicized as Anthony of Messina, was an Italian p…","p":"images/a/Q5594.jpg"},"Frederic Edwin Church":{"zh":"弗雷德里克·埃德温·丘奇","en":"Frederic Edwin Church","born":"1826","died":"1900","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"弗雷德里克·埃德温·丘奇是一位美国风景画家，他是托马斯·科尔的学生，也是第二代哈德逊河派的中心人物之一。他的作品主要以他在美洲旅行时看到的山川、落日等宏伟的景观为主，晚年也画过一些城市景观及地中海和中东的景色。","bio_en":"Frederic Edwin Church was an American landscape painter born in Hartford, Connecticut. He was a central figure in the Hudson River School of American landscape painters, best known for painting large …","p":"images/a/Q366212.jpg"},"Rosa Bonheur":{"zh":"罗莎·波纳","en":"Rosa Bonheur","born":"1822","died":"1899","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"罗莎·博纳尔，原名玛丽·罗莎莉·博纳尔 ，19世纪最著名女性画家，以动物画出名。她的画作曾是国际间最畅销且售价最高。也是法国荣誉军团勋章设立以来首位获颁「大军官勋位」的女性。","bio_en":"Rosa Bonheur was a French painter, sculptor and animalier. Her paintings include Ploughing in the Nivernais, first exhibited at the Salon of 1849, and now in the Musée d'Orsay in Paris, and The Horse …","p":"images/a/Q241732.jpg"},"Spider-Man":{"zh":"蜘蛛人","en":"Spider-Man","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"蜘蛛侠是漫威漫画创作的一名超级英雄，本名为彼得·班杰明·帕克，由作家／编辑史丹·李及作家／画家史蒂夫·迪特科所创造，首次登场于《奇妙幻想》#15，蜘蛛侠是漫威漫画旗下最成功的角色，亦是美国漫画最受欢迎的超级英雄之一。","bio_en":"Spider-Man is a superhero in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer-editor Stan Lee and artist Steve Ditko, he first appeared in the anthology comic book Amazing Fantasy #1…"},"Henry Raeburn":{"zh":"亨利·雷布恩","en":"Henry Raeburn","born":"1756","died":"1823","cty_zh":"大不列颠王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Great Britain","bio_zh":"亨利·雷伯恩爵士 FRSE RA 是一名苏格兰肖像画画家，是乔治四世的御用画家。","bio_en":"Sir Henry Raeburn was a Scottish portrait painter. He served as Portrait Painter to King George IV in Scotland.","p":"images/a/Q561916.jpg"},"John Singleton Copley":{"zh":"约翰·科普利","en":"John Singleton Copley","born":"1738","died":"1815","cty_zh":"大英帝国","cty_en":"British Empire","bio_zh":"约翰·辛格尔顿·科普利，美国殖民地时期以及建国之后本土最重要的一位画家，擅长肖像画、历史画。","bio_en":"John Singleton Copley was an American-born British painter active in both the Thirteen Colonies and England. He is believed to have been born in Boston, Province of Massachusetts Bay, to Richard and M…","p":"images/a/Q316016.jpg"},"Antoine-Jean Gros":{"zh":"安托万-让·格罗","en":"Antoine-Jean Gros","born":"1771","died":"1835","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"安托万-让·格罗，法国新古典主义画家。","bio_en":"Antoine-Jean Gros was a French painter of historical subjects. He was granted the title of Baron Gros in 1824. Gros studied under Jacques-Louis David in Paris and began an independent artistic career …","p":"images/a/Q216999.jpg"},"Hendrick Avercamp":{"zh":"亨德里克·阿弗坎普","en":"Hendrick Avercamp","born":"1585","died":"1634","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"亨德里克·阿弗坎普是荷兰黄金时代的画家，以冬季风景画著名，例如『冰上的场景』等。","bio_en":"Hendrick Avercamp – May 15, 1634 ) was a Dutch painter during the Dutch Golden Age of painting. He was one of the earliest landscape painters of the 17th-century Dutch school, he specialized in painti…","p":"images/a/Q212593.jpg"},"Mikhail Vrubel":{"zh":"米哈伊尔·弗鲁贝尔","en":"Mikhail Vrubel","born":"1856","died":"1910","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"米哈伊尔·亚历山德罗维奇·弗鲁贝尔是一名俄罗斯画家、素描家与雕塑家。他在绘画、素描、装饰雕塑与戏剧等多种媒材中皆展现出丰富且创新的艺术实践，通常被视为俄罗斯象征主义传统中最重要的艺术家之一，也是现代艺术的先驱人物。","bio_en":"Mikhail Aleksandrovich Vrubel was a Russian painter, draughtsman, and sculptor. A prolific and innovative master in various media such as painting, drawing, decorative sculpture, and theatrical art, V…","p":"images/a/Q215100.jpg"},"Alexander Ivanov":{"zh":"亚历山大·安德烈耶维奇·伊万诺夫","en":"Alexander Ivanov","born":"1806","died":"1858","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"亚历山大·安德烈耶维奇·伊万诺夫是一位俄罗斯画家，出生于圣彼得堡。 亚历山大·安德烈耶维奇·伊万诺夫是安德烈·伊万诺夫之子，早年在帝国艺术学院学习绘画。","bio_en":"Alexander Andreyevich Ivanov was a Russian painter who adhered to the waning tradition of Neoclassicism but found little sympathy with his contemporaries.","p":"images/a/Q76829.jpg"},"Han Gan":{"zh":"韩干","en":"Han Gan","born":"0742","died":"0783","cty_zh":"唐朝","cty_en":"Tang dynasty","bio_zh":"韩干，长安人，一说蓝田人，又说大梁人，唐代画家，以画马著称。 韩干少年时只是一名酒店的雇工，后来被诗人王维赏识，资助他学画，学成后被召为宫廷画师，初师曹霸，后自独善。","bio_en":"Han Gan was a Chinese painter during the Tang dynasty. He came from a poor family in either Chang'an, modern-day Xi'an, Shaanxi; Lantian, modern-day Shaanxi; or Daliang, modern-day Kaifeng, Henan.","p":"images/a/Q561952.jpg"},"Joaquín Sorolla":{"zh":"华金·索罗拉","en":"Joaquín Sorolla","born":"1863","died":"1923","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"华金·索罗拉-巴斯蒂达是西班牙画家。他是一位多产的画家，留下的作品超过两千幅。他成熟时期的作品被人们认为是印象派,后印象派以及光影主义的杰作。","bio_en":"Joaquín Sorolla y Bastida was a Spanish painter. Sorolla excelled in the painting of portraits, landscapes, and monumental works of social and historical themes.","p":"images/a/Q351746.jpg"},"Carl Bloch":{"zh":"Carl Bloch","en":"Carl Bloch","born":"1834","died":"1890","cty_zh":"丹麦王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Denmark","bio_zh":"卡尔·布洛赫，丹麦画家，以宗教历史画和描绘耶稣生平的作品著称，是丹麦黄金时代后期的重要画家。","bio_en":"Carl Heinrich Bloch was a Danish painter.","p":"images/a/Q547055.jpg"},"Thomas Cole":{"zh":"托马斯·科尔","en":"Thomas Cole","born":"1801","died":"1848","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"托马斯·科尔是一位19世纪美国风景画家，被认为是哈德逊河派的创始人。科尔的作品均富有浪漫主义风格，细致而写实，描绘的主要是美国的自然风光。","bio_en":"Thomas Cole was an Anglo-American artist who founded the Hudson River School art movement. He painted romantic landscapes and history paintings.","p":"images/a/Q334001.jpg"},"Piero di Cosimo":{"zh":"皮耶罗·迪·科西莫","en":"Piero di Cosimo","born":"1462","died":"1522","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"皮耶罗·迪·科西莫，亦称皮耶罗·迪·洛伦佐，是意大利文艺复兴时期的一位画家。","bio_en":"Piero di Cosimo , also known as Piero di Lorenzo, was an Italian Renaissance painter, who continued to use an essentially Early Renaissance style into the 16th century.","p":"images/a/Q280851.jpg"},"Quinten Metsys":{"zh":"昆滕·马赛斯","en":"Quinten Metsys","born":"1466","died":"1530","cty_zh":"布拉班特公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Brabant","bio_zh":"昆丁·马西斯是一位早期尼德兰传统风格的佛兰德斯画家。 据传，他在成为画家之前曾是一名铁匠。昆丁·马西斯在安特卫普活跃了20多年，创作了大量宗教和讽刺倾向的作品。","bio_en":"Quentin Matsys was a Flemish painter in the Early Netherlandish tradition. He was born in Leuven. According to tradition, he trained as an ironsmith before becoming a painter.","p":"images/a/Q314275.jpg"},"Gerard van Honthorst":{"zh":"赫拉德·范洪特霍斯特","en":"Gerard van Honthorst","born":"1592","died":"1656","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"赫拉德·范洪特霍斯特是一位荷兰黄金时代画家。这位画家在当时以描绘人工照明场景的作品而闻名，获得了“夜晚的杰拉尔多”的绰号。他年轻时前往罗马，绘画风格受到卡拉瓦乔的影响，大获成功。","bio_en":"Gerard \"Gerrit\" van Honthorst was a Dutch Golden Age painter who became known for his depiction of artificially lit scenes, eventually receiving the Italian nickname Gherardo delle Notti .","p":"images/a/Q314548.png"},"Gentile da Fabriano":{"zh":"真蒂莱·达·法布里亚诺","en":"Gentile da Fabriano","born":"1370","died":"1427","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"真蒂莱·达·法布里亚诺，意大利画家，国际哥特式风格的代表，作品以华丽的金色装饰与优雅细节著称，代表作《三博士来朝》。","bio_en":"Gentile da Fabriano was an Italian painter known for his participation in the International Gothic pictorial style.","p":"images/a/Q312393.jpg"},"Paul Émile Chabas":{"zh":"保罗·埃米尔·查瓦斯","en":"Paul Émile Chabas","born":"1869","died":"1937","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"保罗·埃米尔·夏巴斯，法国画家、插画家，法兰西美术院院士，以《九月的清晨》等沐浴少女题材广为人知。","bio_en":"Paul Émile Chabas was a French painter and illustrator and member of the Académie des Beaux-Arts.","p":"images/a/Q964791.jpg"},"Frédéric Bazille":{"zh":"弗雷德里克·巴齐耶","en":"Frédéric Bazille","born":"1841","died":"1870","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让·弗雷德里克·巴齐耶，是与莫奈同时代的法国印象派画家。","bio_en":"Jean Frédéric Bazille was a French Impressionist painter. Many of Bazille's major works are examples of figure painting in which he placed the subject figure within a landscape painted en plein air.","p":"images/a/Q207298.jpg"},"Jusepe de Ribera":{"zh":"胡塞佩·德·里韦拉","en":"Jusepe de Ribera","born":"1591","died":"1652","cty_zh":"阿拉贡联合王国","cty_en":"Crown of Aragon","bio_zh":"胡塞佩·德·里韦拉，也被叫做“Lo Spagnoletto”，是一位17世纪西班牙紫金色黑暗派、卡拉瓦乔主义画家及版画家，出生于哈蒂瓦，1616年移居西班牙帝国治下的那不勒斯王国，并再没有返回过西班牙。","bio_en":"Jusepe de Ribera was a Spanish painter and printmaker. Ribera, Francisco de Zurbarán, Bartolomé Esteban Murillo, and the singular Diego Velázquez, are regarded as the major artists of Spanish Baroque …","p":"images/a/Q297838.jpg"},"Vasily Surikov":{"zh":"瓦西里·伊万诺维奇·苏里科夫","en":"Vasily Surikov","born":"1848","died":"1916","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"瓦西里·伊万诺维奇·苏里科夫，俄罗斯著名画家，1948年莫斯科国立美术学院更名为苏里科夫美术学院。 苏里科夫出生于西伯利亚的克拉斯诺亚尔斯克，1876年毕业于圣彼得堡皇家美术学院，并且获得一级艺术家称号。","bio_en":"Vasily Ivanovich Surikov was a Russian Realist painter, active in Moscow during Tsars Alexander III and Nicholas II's reigns, renowned for his large history pictures.","p":"images/a/Q110228.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/ffbef093f41550ffa45b30c5b91a3156":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/ffbef093f41550ffa45b30c5b91a3156","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/ffbef093f41550ffa45b30c5b91a3156","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/89011985b6d726cc4876ec47e46dfece":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/89011985b6d726cc4876ec47e46dfece","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/89011985b6d726cc4876ec47e46dfece","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/31aba5c4e69fdd64b4aaacaa16df5bed":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/31aba5c4e69fdd64b4aaacaa16df5bed","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/31aba5c4e69fdd64b4aaacaa16df5bed","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"William Etty":{"zh":"威廉·埃蒂","en":"William Etty","born":"1787","died":"1849","cty_zh":"大不列颠王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Great Britain","bio_zh":"威廉·埃蒂RA是英格兰画家…","bio_en":"William Etty was an English artist best known for his historical paintings containing nude figures. He was the first significant British painter of nudes and still lifes.","p":"images/a/Q766362.jpg"},"Howard Chandler Christy":{"zh":"霍华德·钱德勒·克里斯蒂","en":"Howard Chandler Christy","born":"1873","died":"1952","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"霍华德·钱德勒·克里斯是一位美国艺术家和插画家。从20世纪20年代到20世纪50年代早期…","bio_en":"Howard Chandler Christy was an American artist and illustrator. Famous for the \"Christy Girl\" – a colorful and illustrious successor to the \"Gibson Girl\" – Christy is also widely known for his iconic …","p":"images/a/Q3141534.jpg"},"Gustave Moreau":{"zh":"古斯塔夫·莫罗","en":"Gustave Moreau","born":"1826","died":"1898","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"古斯塔夫·莫罗是一位法国艺术家，是象征主义运动的重要人物。 让·卡苏称他为“卓越的象征主义画家”。他是19世纪60年代视觉艺术中具有影响力的象征主义先行者，在19世纪90年代象征主义运动的高峰期，他是最重要的画家之一。","bio_en":"Gustave Moreau was a French artist and an important figure in the Symbolist movement. Jean Cassou called him \"the Symbolist painter par excellence\".","p":"images/a/Q203828.jpg"},"Juan Bautista Martínez del Mazo":{"zh":"胡安·包蒂斯塔·马丁内斯·德尔·马佐","en":"Juan Bautista Martínez del Mazo","born":"约1612","died":"1667","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"胡安·包蒂斯塔·马丁内斯·德尔·马佐，西班牙巴洛克肖像与风景画家，委拉斯开兹的女婿及最出色的追随者，风格与其岳父极为接近。","bio_en":"Juan Bautista Martínez del Mazo was a Spanish Baroque portrait and landscape painter, the most distinguished of the followers of his father-in-law Velázquez, whose style he imitated more closely than …","p":"images/a/Q771658.jpg"},"Duccio di Buoninsegna":{"zh":"杜乔·迪·博尼塞尼亚","en":"Duccio di Buoninsegna","born":"1255","died":"1319","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"杜乔·迪·波尼赛尼亚，又译杜奇欧、杜奇奥，他是Buonisegna的儿子， 出生于13世纪中期以后。他是中世纪意大利最具影响力的画家之一，被称为锡耶纳画派的创始人。","bio_en":"Duccio di Buoninsegna , commonly known as just Duccio, was an Italian painter active in Siena, Tuscany, in the late 13th and early 14th century.","p":"images/a/Q15792.jpg"},"Giuseppe Pellizza da Volpedo":{"zh":"朱塞佩·佩利扎·达·沃尔佩多","en":"Giuseppe Pellizza da Volpedo","born":"1868","died":"1907","cty_zh":"意大利王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Italy","bio_zh":"朱塞佩·佩利扎·达·沃尔佩多，意大利点彩派（分割主义）画家，以描绘工人运动的巨作《第四等级》闻名。","bio_en":"Giuseppe Pellizza da Volpedo was an Italian Divisionist painter. Pellizza was a pupil of Pio Sanquirico. He used a Divisionist technique in which a painting is created by juxtaposing small dots of pai…","p":"images/a/Q1528580.jpg"},"Andrea del Sarto":{"zh":"安德烈亚·德尔·萨尔托","en":"Andrea del Sarto","born":"1486","died":"1530","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"安德烈亚·德尔·萨尔托，文艺复兴时期欧洲佛罗伦萨画家。他曾在皮耶罗·迪·科西莫的画室学艺。他因在佛罗伦萨的修道院以灰色模拟浮雕画法绘制的宗教题材而享有盛誉。","bio_en":"Andrea del Sarto was an Italian painter from Florence, whose career flourished during the High Renaissance and early Mannerism.","p":"images/a/Q5571.jpg"},"Q41554":{"zh":"尼古拉·普桑","en":"Q41554","born":"1594","died":"1665","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"尼古拉·普桑17世纪法国巴洛克时期重要画家，但属于古典主义画派。以《阿尔卡迪的牧人》为其代表作；《摩西的发现》是其古典主义的代表作。","bio_en":"Nicolas Poussin was a leading painter of the classical French Baroque style, although he spent most of his working life in Rome."},"Jacob van Ruisdael":{"zh":"雅各布·伊萨克松·范勒伊斯达尔","en":"Jacob van Ruisdael","born":"1628","died":"1682","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"雅各布·伊萨克松·范勒伊斯达尔是著名的荷兰风景画家。","bio_en":"Jacob Isaackszoon van Ruisdael was a Dutch painter, draughtsman, and etcher. He is generally considered the pre-eminent landscape painter of the Dutch Golden Age, a period of great wealth and cultural…","p":"images/a/Q213612.jpg"},"Peder Severin Krøyer":{"zh":"索伦·柯罗耶","en":"Peder Severin Krøyer","born":"1851","died":"1909","cty_zh":"挪威","cty_en":"Norway","bio_zh":"彼得·塞维林·柯罗耶是一名丹麦印象派画家。 柯罗耶出生于挪威斯塔凡格。19岁时从丹麦皇家美术学院毕业，不久后他前往法国，成为莱昂·博纳的学生。","bio_en":"Peder Severin Krøyer , also known as P. S. Krøyer, was a Danish painter.","p":"images/a/Q365068.jpg"},"Georges de La Tour":{"zh":"乔治·德·拉·图尔","en":"Georges de La Tour","born":"1593","died":"1652","cty_zh":"洛林公国","cty_en":"Duchy of Lorraine","bio_zh":"乔治·德·拉·图尔，法国巴洛克时代画家，生于法国洛林，以绘画烛光作为光源的晚景闻名，题材主要为宗教画和风俗画。","bio_en":"Georges de La Tour was a French Baroque painter, who spent most of his working life in the Duchy of Lorraine, which was temporarily absorbed into France between 1641 and 1648.","p":"images/a/Q203371.jpg"},"Hugo van der Goes":{"zh":"雨果·凡·德·古斯","en":"Hugo van der Goes","born":"1440","died":"1482","cty_zh":"勃艮第尼德兰","cty_en":"Burgundian Netherlands","bio_zh":"雨果·凡·德·古斯是一位生活于15世纪的佛兰德画家，是重要的早期尼德兰画家之一。他的很多作品都留存了下来，其最著名的作品是现藏于乌菲兹美术馆的波尔蒂纳里祭坛画。","bio_en":"Hugo van der Goes was a Flemish painter who was one of the most significant and original Early Netherlandish painters of the late 15th century.","p":"images/a/Q215251.jpg"},"Francisco de Zurbarán":{"zh":"弗朗西斯科·德·苏巴朗","en":"Francisco de Zurbarán","born":"1598","died":"1664","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"弗朗西斯科·德·苏巴朗—1664年8月27日），西班牙画家，成名于宗教画。擅长描绘僧侣、修女、殉道者以及静物。由于其对于明暗对照法的出色运用而被称为西班牙的卡拉瓦乔。","bio_en":"Francisco de Zurbarán was a Spanish Baroque painter. He is known primarily for his religious paintings depicting monks, nuns, and martyrs, and for his still-lifes.","p":"images/a/Q209615.jpg"},"Alexander Roslin":{"zh":"亚历山大·罗斯林","en":"Alexander Roslin","born":"1718","died":"1793","cty_zh":"瑞典","cty_en":"Sweden","bio_zh":"亚历山大·罗斯林，瑞典肖像画家，活跃于巴黎等欧洲宫廷，为众多贵族绘制了华美精致的肖像。","bio_en":"Alexander Roslin was a Swedish painter who worked in Scania, Bayreuth, Paris, Italy, Warsaw and St. Petersburg, primarily for members of aristocratic families.","p":"images/a/Q315102.jpg"},"Pisanello":{"zh":"皮萨内洛","en":"Pisanello","born":"1395","died":"1455","cty_zh":"比萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Pisa","bio_zh":"皮萨内洛，意大利文艺复兴早期最杰出的画家之一，也是纪念章艺术的开创者，以精细的动植物写生与优雅的国际哥特风格著称。","bio_en":"Pisanello , born Antonio di Puccio Pisano or Antonio di Puccio da Cereto, also erroneously called Vittore Pisano by Giorgio Vasari, was one of the most distinguished painters of the early Italian Rena…","p":"images/a/Q311082.jpg"},"John Collier":{"zh":"约翰·柯里尔","en":"John Collier","born":"1850","died":"1934","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"约翰·柯里尔，英国艺术家、作家，前拉斐尔派，擅长画肖像画，两个妻子都是托马斯·亨利·赫胥黎的女儿。1875年在慕尼黑美术学院学习绘画。","bio_en":"John Maler Collier was an English painter and writer. He was one of the most prominent portrait painters of his generation.","p":"images/a/Q453972.jpg"},"Alexandre Cabanel":{"zh":"亚历山大·卡巴内尔","en":"Alexandre Cabanel","born":"1823","died":"1889","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"亚历山大·卡巴内尔，法国学院派画家。擅长以学院派风格描绘历史、古典及宗教题材。 卡巴内尔同时也是一位知名的肖像画家，并受到拿破仑三世的青睐，被誉为御用画家。","bio_en":"Alexandre Cabanel kabanɛl]; 28 September 1823 – 23 January 1889) was a French painter. He painted historical, classical and religious subjects in the academic style.","p":"images/a/Q310437.jpg"},"Bartolomé Esteban Murillo":{"zh":"巴托洛梅·埃斯特万·牟利罗","en":"Bartolomé Esteban Murillo","born":"1617","died":"1682","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"巴托洛梅·埃斯特万·牟利罗，巴洛克时期西班牙画家。生于西班牙塞维利亚，死于塞维利亚。他是一个很有独特风格的画家。","bio_en":"Bartolomé Esteban Murillo uu-REE-oh, Spanish: [baɾtoloˈme esˈteβam muˈɾiʎo]; late December 1617, baptised 1 January 1618 – 3 April 1682) was a Spanish Baroque painter.","p":"images/a/Q192062.jpg"},"Jean-Marc Côté":{"zh":"Jean-Marc Côté","en":"Jean-Marc Côté","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Herbert James Draper":{"zh":"赫伯特·詹姆斯·德雷珀","en":"Herbert James Draper","born":"1863","died":"1920","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"赫伯特·詹姆斯·德雷珀，英国新古典主义画家，创作横跨维多利亚时代至二十世纪初，以取材古希腊神话的作品著称，如《伊卡洛斯的哀歌》。","bio_en":"Herbert James Draper 26 November 1863 – 22 September 1920) was an English Neoclassicist painter whose career began in the Victorian era and extended through the first two decades of the 20th century.","p":"images/a/Q918605.jpg"},"Annibale Carracci":{"zh":"安尼巴莱·卡拉齐","en":"Annibale Carracci","born":"1560","died":"1609","cty_zh":"教皇国","cty_en":"Papal States","bio_zh":"安尼巴莱·卡拉奇，意大利画家，巴洛克绘画的代表人物之一。他与其兄阿戈斯蒂诺·卡拉奇、堂兄卢多维科·卡拉奇合称为卡拉奇三兄弟，他们共同创办了博洛尼亚卡拉奇学院。","bio_en":"Annibale Carracci was an Italian painter and instructor, active in Bologna and later in Rome. Along with his brother Agostino and cousin Ludovico , Annibale was one of the progenitors, if not founders…","p":"images/a/Q7824.jpg"},"Alexei Savrasov":{"zh":"阿历克塞·贡德拉特维奇·萨伏拉索夫","en":"Alexei Savrasov","born":"1830","died":"1897","cty_zh":"俄罗斯帝国","cty_en":"Russian Empire","bio_zh":"阿列克谢·孔德拉季耶维奇·萨伏拉索夫，俄罗斯著名风景画家。 萨伏拉索夫出生于一个商人家庭，从8岁起就开始学习绘画，后来进入莫斯科绘画雕塑建筑学院学习。","bio_en":"Alexei Kondratyevich Savrasov was a Russian landscape painter and creator of the lyrical landscape style. The most famous and a celebrated work is The Rooks Have Returned.","p":"images/a/Q353008.jpg"},"Élisabeth Louise Vigée Le Brun":{"zh":"伊莉莎白·维杰·勒布伦","en":"Élisabeth Louise Vigée Le Brun","born":"1755","died":"1842","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"伊莉莎白·露易丝·维杰·勒布伦，18世纪后期法国杰出女画家。因给皇后玛丽·安托瓦内特绘画肖像而出名，法国大革命后离开法国在欧洲各国作画，在意大利、奥地利和俄罗斯生活和工作了几年，在那里她继续画贵族的画像。","bio_en":"Élisabeth Louise Vigée Le Brun , also known as Louise Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun or simply Madame Le Brun, was a French painter who mostly specialized in portrait painting, in the late 18th and early 19t…","p":"images/a/Q213163.jpg"},"Paul-Jacques-Aimé Baudry":{"zh":"保罗·伯哲","en":"Paul-Jacques-Aimé Baudry","born":"1828","died":"1886","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"保罗-雅克-埃梅·博德里，法国学院派画家，以为巴黎加尼叶歌剧院所作的天顶与壁画装饰闻名。","bio_en":"Paul-Jacques-Aimé Baudry was a French painter.","p":"images/a/Q911575.jpg"},"Arnold Böcklin":{"zh":"阿诺德·勃克林","en":"Arnold Böcklin","born":"1827","died":"1901","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"阿诺德·勃克林是一名瑞士象征主义画家。","bio_en":"Arnold Böcklin was a Swiss Symbolist painter. His five versions of the Isle of the Dead inspired works by several late Romantic composers.","p":"images/a/Q123071.jpg"},"Cimabue":{"zh":"契马布埃","en":"Cimabue","born":"1240","died":"1302","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"契马布埃又译齐玛布，意大利佛罗伦萨最早的画家之一，也是来自当地的马赛克设计师。 他原为镶嵌画匠，据意大利画家兼历史学家乔治·瓦萨里所述，他为乔托·迪·邦多内的老师。","bio_en":"Giovanni Cimabue , also known as Cenni di Pepo or Cenni di Pepi, was an Italian painter and designer of mosaics from Florence.","p":"images/a/Q15790.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/07f718c29caf0064631cf14e5c147a4d":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/07f718c29caf0064631cf14e5c147a4d","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/07f718c29caf0064631cf14e5c147a4d","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Giuseppe Castiglione":{"zh":"郎世宁","en":"Giuseppe Castiglione","born":"1688","died":"1766","cty_zh":"清朝","cty_en":"Qing dynasty","bio_zh":"郎世宁，意大利人，天主教耶稣会修士及中国宫廷画家，写实画风纪录了清朝初期至中期的中国宫廷人物与景色。","bio_en":"Giuseppe Castiglione S.J. , was an Italian Jesuit brother and missionary in China, where he served as an artist at the imperial court of three Qing emperors – the Kangxi, Yongzheng and Qianlong empero…","p":"images/a/Q5565375.jpg"},"Viktor Vasnetsov":{"zh":"维克多·瓦斯涅佐夫","en":"Viktor Vasnetsov","born":"1848","died":"1926","cty_zh":"苏联","cty_en":"Soviet Union","bio_zh":"维克托·米哈伊洛维奇·瓦斯涅佐夫，俄罗斯艺术家，专攻神话和历史题材。被认为是俄罗斯文艺复兴运动的关键人物之一。","bio_en":"Viktor Mikhaylovich Vasnetsov was a Russian painter and draughtsman who specialised in mythological and historical subjects.","p":"images/a/Q204138.jpg"},"Christoffer Wilhelm Eckersberg":{"zh":"克里斯托弗·威廉·埃克斯贝尔","en":"Christoffer Wilhelm Eckersberg","born":"1783","died":"1853","cty_zh":"丹麦王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Denmark","bio_zh":"克里斯托弗·威廉·埃克斯贝格，丹麦画家，被誉为「丹麦绘画之父」，奠定了丹麦黄金时代绘画的基础。","bio_en":"Christoffer Wilhelm Eckersberg was a Danish painter. He was born in Blåkrog in the Duchy of Schleswig . He went on to lay the foundation for the period of art known as the Golden Age of Danish Paintin…","p":"images/a/Q363823.jpg"},"Jan Asselijn":{"zh":"扬·阿瑟莱恩","en":"Jan Asselijn","born":"1610","died":"1652","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"扬·阿瑟林，荷兰黄金时代画家，以意大利风格的风景画和名作《受威胁的天鹅》著称。","bio_en":"Jan Asselijn was a Dutch Golden Age painter.","p":"images/a/Q541976.jpg"},"Edmund Blair Leighton":{"zh":"埃德蒙·布莱尔·莱顿","en":"Edmund Blair Leighton","born":"1852","died":"1922","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"埃德蒙·布莱尔·莱顿，英国维多利亚时代著名画家，尤其擅长英国摄政时期和中世纪画作。","bio_en":"Edmund Blair Leighton was an English painter of historical genre scenes, specialising in Regency and medieval subjects.","p":"images/a/Q142420.jpg"},"Edwin Landseer":{"zh":"埃德英·蓝道西尔","en":"Edwin Landseer","born":"1802","died":"1873","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"埃德温·亨利·兰德希尔爵士 RA是英国画家与雕塑家，以描绘动物的作品闻名，尤以马、犬与雄鹿为主。他最著名的作品为位于特拉法加广场纳尔逊纪念柱基座上的狮子雕塑。","bio_en":"Sir Edwin Henry Landseer was an English painter and sculptor, well known for his paintings of animals – particularly horses, dogs, and stags.","p":"images/a/Q328369.jpg"},"Anne Vallayer-Coster":{"zh":"安妮·瓦拉耶-科斯特","en":"Anne Vallayer-Coster","born":"1744","died":"1818","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"安妮·瓦拉耶-科斯特，法国画家，以静物画闻名，早年即入选皇家绘画与雕塑学院，深受玛丽·安托瓦内特赏识。","bio_en":"Anne Vallayer-Coster was a French painter best known for still lifes. She achieved fame and recognition very early in her career, being admitted to the Académie Royale de Peinture et de Sculpture in 1…","p":"images/a/Q468772.jpg"},"Sofonisba Anguissola":{"zh":"索福尼斯巴·安圭索拉","en":"Sofonisba Anguissola","born":"1532","died":"1625","cty_zh":"克雷莫纳","cty_en":"Cremona","bio_zh":"索福尼斯巴·安圭索拉，她是文艺复兴时期晚期欧洲首位具有国际声望的矫饰主义女画家，她因把意大利画派引入了西班牙文化而为人称道。","bio_en":"Sofonisba Anguissola was an Italian Renaissance painter born in Cremona to a relatively poor noble family. She received a well-rounded education that included the fine arts, and her apprenticeship wit…","p":"images/a/Q236038.jpg"},"Eugene de Blaas":{"zh":"尤金·布拉斯","en":"Eugene de Blaas","born":"1843","died":"1931","cty_zh":"奥匈帝国","cty_en":"Austria–Hungary","bio_zh":"尤金·布拉斯或尤金尼奥·布拉斯，1843年7月24日—1932年2月10日），生于意大利罗马附近的阿巴诺，双亲均为奥地利人，自小跟随父母一起搬到威尼斯生活。","bio_en":"Eugene de Blaas, also known as Eugene von Blaas or Eugenio Blaas , was an Italian painter in the school known as Academic Classicism.","p":"images/a/Q715036.jpg"},"Gianfrancesco Penni":{"zh":"乔万·弗朗切斯科·佩尼","en":"Gianfrancesco Penni","born":"1495","died":"1520","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"詹弗兰切斯科·潘尼，绰号「管家」，意大利文艺复兴画家，拉斐尔的主要助手之一，参与了梵蒂冈众多壁画的绘制。","bio_en":"Gianfrancesco Penni , called il Fattore, was an Italian painter. His brother Bartolommeo was an artist of the Tudor court of Henry VIII, and another brother, Luca, ended up as one of the Italian artis…","p":"images/a/Q2327761.jpg"},"Jan Steen":{"zh":"扬·斯滕","en":"Jan Steen","born":"1626","died":"1679","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"扬·哈菲克松·斯滕是17世纪荷兰风俗画油画家。他的作品以心理洞察力、幽默感以及丰富的色彩为特点。","bio_en":"Jan Havickszoon Steen was a Dutch Golden Age painter, one of the leading genre painters of the 17th century. His works are known for their psychological insight, sense of humour and abundance of colou…","p":"images/a/Q205863.jpg"},"Benjamin West":{"zh":"本杰明·委斯特","en":"Benjamin West","born":"1738","died":"1820","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"本杰明·韦斯特PRA，出生于英属宾夕法尼亚省的英格兰画家，以绘制历史画和美国独立战争场景知名。曾担任英国皇家艺术研究院第二任院长。英国皇室曾授予他骑士头衔，但被韦斯特本人拒绝。","bio_en":"Benjamin West was an American-born British painter who specialised in history painting, creating such works as The Death of Nelson, The Death of General Wolfe, the Treaty of Paris, and Benjamin Frankl…","p":"images/a/Q313498.jpg"},"Filippo Lippi":{"zh":"菲利普·利皮","en":"Filippo Lippi","born":"1406","died":"1469","cty_zh":"佛罗伦萨共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Florence","bio_zh":"菲利普·利皮，意大利文艺复兴时期的一位画家，其子菲利皮诺·利皮后来也成为了名画家。","bio_en":"Filippo Lippi , also known as Lippo Lippi, was an Italian Renaissance painter of the Quattrocento and a Carmelite priest.","p":"images/a/Q205148.jpg"},"Franz Marc":{"zh":"弗朗茨·马克","en":"Franz Marc","born":"1880","died":"1916","cty_zh":"巴伐利亚王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of Bavaria","bio_zh":"弗朗茨·莫里茨·威廉·马克，德国画家，艺术团体“青骑士”的成员。他是二十世纪最伟大的画家之一和德国表现主义的创始人之一。","bio_en":"Franz Moritz Wilhelm Marc was a German painter and printmaker, one of the key figures of German Expressionism. He was a founding member of Der Blaue Reiter , a journal whose name later became synonymo…","p":"images/a/Q44054.jpg"},"Pietro Perugino":{"zh":"彼得罗·佩鲁吉诺","en":"Pietro Perugino","born":"1448","died":"1523","cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":"彼得罗·佩鲁吉诺，是一位意大利文艺复兴时期的画家，活跃于文艺复兴全盛期。其最著名的学生是拉斐尔。","bio_en":"Pietro Perugino was an Italian Renaissance painter of the Umbrian school who developed some of the qualities that found classic expression in the High Renaissance.","p":"images/a/Q5827.jpg"},"Francisco Pradilla y Ortiz":{"zh":"弗朗西斯科·普拉迪利亚","en":"Francisco Pradilla y Ortiz","born":"1848","died":"1921","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"弗朗西斯科·普拉迪利亚·奥尔蒂斯是西班牙画家。以本土风俗风景画创作著称。","bio_en":"Francisco Pradilla y Ortiz was a prolific Spanish painter famous for creating historical scenes.","p":"images/a/Q553258.jpg"},"Juan Luna":{"zh":"胡安·卢纳·德·圣佩德罗","en":"Juan Luna","born":"1857","died":"1899","cty_zh":"菲律宾","cty_en":"Philippines","bio_zh":"胡安·卢纳，菲律宾画家、雕塑家及菲律宾革命的政治活动家，以历史画巨作《斗兽场》闻名，是菲律宾最重要的艺术家之一。","bio_en":"Juan Luna de San Pedro y Novicio was a Filipino painter, sculptor and a political activist of the Philippine Revolution during the late 19th century.","p":"images/a/Q28867.png"},"Arthur Hughes":{"zh":"Arthur Hughes","en":"Arthur Hughes","born":"1832","died":"1915","cty_zh":"大不列颠及爱尔兰联合王国","cty_en":"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland","bio_zh":"阿瑟·休斯，英国画家、插画家，与前拉斐尔派关系密切，以《四月的爱》等细腻抒情的作品著称。","bio_en":"Arthur Hughes was an English painter and illustrator associated with the Pre-Raphaelite Brotherhood.","p":"images/a/Q434575.jpg"},"Lorenzo Lotto":{"zh":"罗伦佐·洛托","en":"Lorenzo Lotto","born":"1480","died":"1556","cty_zh":"威尼斯共和国","cty_en":"Republic of Venice","bio_zh":"洛伦佐·洛托）是意大利文艺复兴时期的画家、绘图员和插画家，传统上属于威尼斯画派，但大部分职业生涯是在意大利北部其他城市度过的。他主要创作祭坛画、宗教主题和肖像画。","bio_en":"Lorenzo Lotto was an Italian Renaissance painter, draughtsman, and illustrator, traditionally placed in the Venetian school, though much of his career was spent in other north Italian cities.","p":"images/a/Q310973.jpg"},"Jean-Antoine Watteau":{"zh":"让-安东尼·华托","en":"Jean-Antoine Watteau","born":"1684","died":"1721","cty_zh":"法兰西王国","cty_en":"Kingdom of France","bio_zh":"让-安托万·华托是法国洛可可时代代表画家。","bio_en":"Jean-Antoine Watteau was a French painter and draughtsman whose brief career spurred the revival of interest in colour and movement, as seen in the tradition of Correggio and Rubens.","p":"images/a/Q183221.jpg"},"Théodore Chassériau":{"zh":"泰奥多尔·夏塞里奥","en":"Théodore Chassériau","born":"1819","died":"1856","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"泰奥多尔·夏塞里奥，法国浪漫主义画派画家，他因为曾经到阿尔及利亚旅行所以画过许多东方风味的绘画。","bio_en":"Théodore Chassériau was a Dominican-born French Romantic painter noted for his portraits, historical and religious paintings, allegorical murals, and Orientalist images inspired by his travels to Alge…","p":"images/a/Q342467.jpg"},"Q168659":{"zh":"弗朗兹·克萨韦尔·温特哈尔特","en":"Q168659","born":"1805","died":"1873","cty_zh":"德意志帝国","cty_en":"German Empire","bio_zh":"弗朗兹·克萨韦尔·温特哈尔特，德国画家。曾为众多19世纪中期的欧洲皇室成员绘像，因而知名，他的名字已经和肖像画联系在一起。他最出名的作品分别是1855年的被侍女围绕的欧仁妮皇后和1865年的奥地利皇后伊丽莎白像。","bio_en":"Franz Xaver Winterhalter was a German painter and lithographer, known for his flattering portraits of royalty and upper-class society in the mid-19th century."},"Gerard David":{"zh":"杰拉尔德·大卫","en":"Gerard David","born":"1460","died":"1523","cty_zh":"哈布斯堡荷兰","cty_en":"Habsburg Netherlands","bio_zh":"杰拉尔德·大卫，文艺复兴时期欧洲荷兰画家。他主要在布鲁日和安特卫普从事创作。他专长于描绘基督的家庭生活场景，这是一个为许多他的同时代人所仿效的流行主题。","bio_en":"Gerard David was an Early Netherlandish painter and manuscript illuminator known for his brilliant use of color.","p":"images/a/Q333380.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/fa628cbc9f70f4ff7584bf1bc4877086":{"zh":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/fa628cbc9f70f4ff7584bf1bc4877086","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/fa628cbc9f70f4ff7584bf1bc4877086","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null},"Gerard ter Borch":{"zh":"赫拉德·特博赫","en":"Gerard ter Borch","born":"1617","died":"1681","cty_zh":"荷兰共和国","cty_en":"Dutch Republic","bio_zh":"赫拉德·特博赫，荷兰黄金时代画家，主要创作风俗画。他影响了荷兰同行加布里埃尔·梅曲、赫里特·道、埃赫隆·范德内尔和扬·弗美尔，不过其在绘画方面的影响力后来被弗美尔超越。","bio_en":"Gerard ter Borch x]; December 1617 – 8 December 1681), also known as Gerard Terburg x]), was a Dutch Golden Age painter mainly of genre subjects.","p":"images/a/Q346808.jpg"},"Alonso Sánchez Coello":{"zh":"Alonso Sánchez Coello","en":"Alonso Sánchez Coello","born":"1531","died":"1588","cty_zh":"阿拉贡联合王国","cty_en":"Crown of Aragon","bio_zh":"阿隆索·桑切斯·科埃略，西班牙文艺复兴肖像画家，供职于西班牙与葡萄牙宫廷，将尼德兰的写实与意大利的理想化融为一体。","bio_en":"Alonso Sánchez Coello was an Iberian portrait painter of the Spanish and Portuguese Renaissance. He is mainly known for his portrait paintings executed in a style which combines the objectivity of the…","p":"images/a/Q503386.jpg"},"Johann Zoffany":{"zh":"约翰·佐法尼","en":"Johann Zoffany","born":"1733","died":"1810","cty_zh":"德国","cty_en":"Germany","bio_zh":"约翰·约瑟夫·佐法尼 RA 是一位德国新古典主义画家，主要活跃在英格兰、意大利和印度。","bio_en":"Johan / Johann Joseph Zoffany was a German neoclassical painter who was active mainly in England, Italy, and India.","p":"images/a/Q702272.jpg"},"Alexandre Desgoffe":{"zh":"让·奥古斯特·多米尼克·安格尔","en":"Alexandre Desgoffe","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null,"p":"images/a/Q2833597.jpg"},"Palma il Giovane":{"zh":"帕尔马·乔凡尼","en":"Palma il Giovane","born":null,"died":null,"cty_zh":null,"cty_en":null,"bio_zh":null,"bio_en":null,"p":"images/a/Q651795.jpg"},"Raymond Balze":{"zh":"让·奥古斯特·多米尼克·安格尔","en":"Raymond Balze","born":"1780","died":"1867","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让·奥古斯特·多米尼克·安格尔是法国画家，新古典主义画派的最后一位代表人物，他和浪漫主义画派的杰出代表欧仁·德拉克罗瓦之间的著名争论震动了整个法国画坛。","bio_en":"Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres was a French Neoclassical painter. Ingres was profoundly influenced by past artistic traditions and aspired to become the guardian of academic orthodoxy against the ascen…","p":"images/a/Q3420651.jpg"},"Domenico Gargiulo":{"zh":"多梅尼科·加尔朱洛","en":"Domenico Gargiulo","born":"1593","died":"1653","cty_zh":"教皇国","cty_en":"Papal States","bio_zh":"阿尔泰米西娅·洛米·真蒂莱斯基，意大利巴洛克画家。在那个女画家十分少见的年代，她率先创作了历史及宗教画。","bio_en":"Artemisia Lomi Gentileschi was an Italian Baroque painter. Gentileschi is considered among the most accomplished 17th-century artists, initially working in the style of Caravaggio.","p":"images/a/Q1170226.jpg"},"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/1cb093800baaef5b1fc45245b951b20d":{"zh":"扬·范·艾克","en":"http://www.wikidata.org/.well-known/genid/1cb093800baaef5b1fc45245b951b20d","born":"1390","died":"1441","cty_zh":"南尼德兰","cty_en":"Southern Netherlands","bio_zh":"扬·范艾克，活跃于布鲁日的弗拉芒画家。他是早期尼德兰画派的创新者之一，也是北方文艺复兴的代表人物。除与其兄许贝特·范艾克合作完成的《根特祭坛画》和签有字母「Hand G」的《都灵-米兰时光》泥金装饰手抄本之外…","bio_en":"Jan van Eyck was an early Netherlandish painter active in Bruges who was one of the early innovators of what became known as early Netherlandish painting, and one of the supreme figures of the Early N…"},"Utagawa Hiroshige":{"zh":"歌川广重","en":"Utagawa Hiroshige","born":"1797","died":"1858","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"歌川广重,日本江户时代浮世绘大师,以风景版画闻名。代表作《东海道五十三次》《名所江户百景》以诗意的构图与微妙的季节、天候氛围著称;与北斋并称,并深刻影响了梵高等欧洲画家。","bio_en":"Utagawa Hiroshige was a master of Japanese ukiyo-e landscape prints of the Edo period, celebrated for The Fifty-three Stations of the Tōkaidō and One Hundred Famous Views of Edo. His poetic compositions and subtle rendering of season and weather, alongside Hokusai's, deeply influenced European painters such as Van Gogh.","p":"images/a/Q200798.jpg"},"J.M.W. Turner":{"zh":"约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳","en":"J.M.W. Turner","born":"1775","died":"1851","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳，英国浪漫主义风景与海景画家，被誉为「光之画家」。他毕生探索光线、色彩与大气的表现，晚年近乎抽象的作品预示了印象派乃至现代绘画的方向。","bio_en":"J.M.W. Turner was an English Romantic painter of landscape and marine subjects, celebrated as 'the painter of light.' His lifelong exploration of light, colour and atmosphere culminated in near-abstract late works that anticipated Impressionism and modern painting.","p":"images/a/Q159758.jpg"},"Joshua Reynolds":{"zh":"约书亚·雷诺兹","en":"Joshua Reynolds","born":"1723","died":"1792","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"约书亚·雷诺兹，十八世纪英国最重要的肖像画家，皇家美术学院首任院长。他倡导取法古典大师的「宏伟风格」，其《艺术演讲录》深刻影响了英国的艺术教育。","bio_en":"Joshua Reynolds was the leading English portraitist of the eighteenth century and the first president of the Royal Academy. He championed the classicising 'Grand Manner,' and his Discourses on Art shaped British artistic education.","p":"images/a/Q194402.jpg"},"Winslow Homer":{"zh":"温斯洛·霍默","en":"Winslow Homer","born":"1836","died":"1910","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"温斯洛·霍默，美国现实主义画家，最初以南北战争的插画起家。他以雄浑的海景油画与清新有力的水彩著称，是十九世纪美国本土艺术的代表人物。","bio_en":"Winslow Homer was an American Realist painter who began as an illustrator of the Civil War. Renowned for his powerful marine oils and fresh, vigorous watercolours, he is a defining figure of nineteenth-century American art.","p":"images/a/Q344838.jpg"},"Albert Bierstadt":{"zh":"阿尔伯特·比尔施塔特","en":"Albert Bierstadt","born":"1830","died":"1902","cty_zh":"美国","cty_en":"United States","bio_zh":"阿尔伯特·比尔施塔特，德裔美国画家，哈德逊河画派与「发光主义」的代表。他以宏幅而光影璀璨的美国西部风景闻名，将落基山与优胜美地的壮丽气象带入画布。","bio_en":"Albert Bierstadt was a German-American painter associated with the Hudson River School and Luminism. He is celebrated for vast, luminous landscapes of the American West that brought the grandeur of the Rockies and Yosemite to canvas.","p":"images/a/Q77132.jpg"},"William Blake":{"zh":"威廉·布莱克","en":"William Blake","born":"1757","died":"1827","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"威廉·布莱克，英国诗人、画家与版画家，浪漫主义的幻想先驱。他自创浮雕蚀刻技法印制「插图诗集」，以圣经与神话为源泉营造独特的幻象世界，生前默默无闻，身后声誉日隆。","bio_en":"William Blake was an English poet, painter and printmaker and a visionary forerunner of Romanticism. Inventing relief etching to print his illuminated books, he conjured a singular imaginative world from biblical and mythic sources—little known in his lifetime, revered ever since.","p":"images/a/Q41513.jpg"},"Jacob Jordaens":{"zh":"雅各布·约尔丹斯","en":"Jacob Jordaens","born":"1593","died":"1678","cty_zh":"佛兰德斯","cty_en":"Flanders","bio_zh":"雅各布·约尔丹斯，佛兰德斯巴洛克三巨头之一（与鲁本斯、凡·戴克并列）。他以充满生活气息的风俗与神话场景著称，人物丰腴、色彩浓烈，尤擅描绘热闹的民间盛宴。","bio_en":"Jacob Jordaens was one of the three great Flemish Baroque painters, alongside Rubens and van Dyck. He is known for earthy genre and mythological scenes with full-bodied figures and rich colour, especially his boisterous depictions of popular feasts.","p":"images/a/Q270658.jpg"},"Anders Zorn":{"zh":"安德斯·佐恩","en":"Anders Zorn","born":"1860","died":"1920","cty_zh":"瑞典","cty_en":"Sweden","bio_zh":"安德斯·佐恩，瑞典画家、蚀刻版画家与雕塑家，十九世纪末最国际化的瑞典艺术家。他是出色的肖像与裸体画家，善以极简的「佐恩调色板」捕捉水光与肌肤，也深情描绘家乡达拉纳的民俗。","bio_en":"Anders Zorn was a Swedish painter, etcher and sculptor, and the most international Swedish artist of the late nineteenth century. A brilliant painter of portraits and nudes, he captured water and flesh with the spare 'Zorn palette' and lovingly recorded the folk life of his native Dalarna.","p":"images/a/Q206820.jpg"},"Giovanni Battista Tiepolo":{"zh":"乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·提埃波罗","en":"Giovanni Battista Tiepolo","born":"1696","died":"1770","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·提埃波罗，十八世纪威尼斯最伟大的画家，欧洲洛可可壁画的巅峰。他以明亮通透的色彩和轻盈的天顶构图闻名，代表作为德国维尔茨堡官邸的巨幅天顶画。","bio_en":"Giovanni Battista Tiepolo was the greatest Venetian painter of the eighteenth century and the supreme master of European Rococo fresco. Famed for luminous colour and soaring ceiling compositions, his masterpiece is the vast fresco of the Würzburg Residence.","p":"images/a/Q186202.jpg"},"Claude Lorrain":{"zh":"克劳德·洛兰","en":"Claude Lorrain","born":"1600","died":"1682","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"克劳德·洛兰，长期旅居罗马的法国巴洛克画家，理想风景画的奠基者。他以诗意的晨昏光线和港湾景致著称，作品成为后世风景画的典范，并直接启发了透纳。","bio_en":"Claude Lorrain was a French Baroque painter who worked in Rome and founded the tradition of the ideal landscape. Celebrated for poetic light and harbour scenes, his work became a model for later landscape painting and directly inspired Turner.","p":"images/a/Q214074.jpg"},"Nicolas Poussin":{"zh":"尼古拉·普桑","en":"Nicolas Poussin","born":"1594","died":"1665","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"尼古拉·普桑，法国古典主义绘画的奠基者，一生大半在罗马度过。他取材神话与历史，以理性的构图、清晰的形体与庄重的秩序，为法国学院派艺术树立了典范。","bio_en":"Nicolas Poussin was the founder of French classical painting, who spent most of his life in Rome. Drawing on myth and history, his rational compositions, clear forms and grave order set the standard for the French academic tradition.","p":"images/a/Q41554.jpg"},"George Stubbs":{"zh":"乔治·斯塔布斯","en":"George Stubbs","born":"1724","died":"1806","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"乔治·斯塔布斯，英国画家，以解剖般精准的马匹肖像闻名。他曾亲手解剖马体、出版《马的解剖》，代表作《惠斯尔杰基特》被誉为动物绘画的巅峰。","bio_en":"George Stubbs was an English painter renowned for his anatomically exact portraits of horses. Having dissected horses and published The Anatomy of the Horse, he created in Whistlejacket one of the summits of animal painting.","p":"images/a/Q381728.jpg"},"Ferdinand Hodler":{"zh":"费迪南德·霍德勒","en":"Ferdinand Hodler","born":"1853","died":"1918","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"费迪南德·霍德勒，瑞士象征主义画家，提出以对称与重复构图的「平行主义」。他创作纪念碑式的人物、寓言与阿尔卑斯风景，是十九世纪末最重要的瑞士艺术家。","bio_en":"Ferdinand Hodler was a Swiss Symbolist painter who developed 'Parallelism,' a principle of symmetry and rhythmic repetition. His monumental figures, allegories and Alpine landscapes make him the foremost Swiss artist of the late nineteenth century.","p":"images/a/Q214564.jpg"},"Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun":{"zh":"伊丽莎白·维热·勒布伦","en":"Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun","born":"1755","died":"1842","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"伊丽莎白·维热·勒布伦，十八世纪最成功的女画家之一，玛丽·安托瓦内特的御用肖像画家。她一生创作约六百幅肖像，风格优雅亲切，法国大革命期间流亡欧洲各王室宫廷。","bio_en":"Élisabeth Vigée Le Brun was one of the most successful women painters of the eighteenth century and portraitist to Marie Antoinette. She painted some six hundred portraits of elegant intimacy and, during the Revolution, worked in the courts of Europe in exile.","p":"images/a/Q213163.jpg"},"Jean-Siméon Chardin":{"zh":"让-西梅翁·夏尔丹","en":"Jean-Siméon Chardin","born":"1699","died":"1779","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-西梅翁·夏尔丹，十八世纪法国最伟大的静物与风俗画家。他摒弃洛可可的浮华，以质朴的厨房静物和宁静的家庭场景，及对光影质地的微妙把握，深深影响了马奈与莫兰迪。","bio_en":"Jean-Siméon Chardin was the greatest French painter of still life and genre of the eighteenth century. Shunning Rococo frivolity, his humble kitchen still lifes and quiet domestic scenes, with their subtle handling of light and texture, deeply influenced Manet and Morandi.","p":"images/a/Q207447.jpg"},"Berthe Morisot":{"zh":"贝尔特·莫里索","en":"Berthe Morisot","born":"1841","died":"1895","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"贝尔特·莫里索，法国印象派的核心成员，参加了几乎全部印象派画展。她以轻盈灵动的笔触描绘女性与家庭生活的私密瞬间，是运动中最重要的女性画家。","bio_en":"Berthe Morisot was a central member of the French Impressionists, exhibiting in nearly all their shows. With light, fluid brushwork she painted intimate moments of women and domestic life, and stands as the movement's foremost woman painter.","p":"images/a/Q105320.jpg"},"Pieter de Hooch":{"zh":"彼得·德·霍赫","en":"Pieter de Hooch","born":"1629","died":"1683","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"彼得·德·霍赫，荷兰黄金时代风俗画家，与维米尔同在代尔夫特活动。他以描绘阳光下宁静的庭院与室内场景著称，精妙的空间透视和光线赋予日常生活以秩序之美。","bio_en":"Pieter de Hooch was a Dutch Golden Age genre painter active in Delft alongside Vermeer. Known for serene sunlit courtyards and interiors, his refined perspective and light lend everyday life a quiet, ordered beauty.","p":"images/a/Q314889.jpg"},"Lawrence Alma-Tadema":{"zh":"劳伦斯·阿尔玛-塔德玛","en":"Lawrence Alma-Tadema","born":"1836","died":"1912","cty_zh":"英国","cty_en":"United Kingdom","bio_zh":"劳伦斯·阿尔玛-塔德玛，荷兰裔英国维多利亚学院派画家。他以考据精细、奢华绚丽的古罗马与古希腊生活场景著称，尤以对大理石、金属与织物质感的逼真描绘令人叹服。","bio_en":"Lawrence Alma-Tadema was a Dutch-British Victorian classicist painter. Famous for meticulously researched, luxuriant scenes of Greco-Roman life, he was especially admired for his astonishingly convincing rendering of marble, metal and fabric.","p":"images/a/Q240526.jpg"},"Vilhelm Hammershøi":{"zh":"维尔赫姆·哈默斯霍伊","en":"Vilhelm Hammershøi","born":"1864","died":"1916","cty_zh":"丹麦","cty_en":"Denmark","bio_zh":"维尔赫姆·哈默斯霍伊，丹麦象征主义画家，以灰调的静谧室内画闻名。他反复描绘空荡的房间与背身的女子，在极简的色彩与柔和的光线中营造出诗意而内省的沉默。","bio_en":"Vilhelm Hammershøi was a Danish Symbolist painter known for muted grey interiors. Repeatedly painting empty rooms and women seen from behind, he created a poetic, introspective silence out of spare colour and soft light.","p":"images/a/Q380706.jpg"},"Alphonse Mucha":{"zh":"阿尔丰斯·慕夏","en":"Alphonse Mucha","born":"1860","died":"1939","cty_zh":"捷克","cty_en":"Czechia","bio_zh":"阿尔丰斯·慕夏，捷克画家与装饰艺术家，新艺术运动的标志性人物。他为莎拉·伯恩哈特设计的戏剧海报风靡巴黎，以柔美的女性、繁复的花卉纹样与拜占庭式装饰定义了一个时代的美学，晚年倾力于民族史诗《斯拉夫史诗》。","bio_en":"Alphonse Mucha was a Czech painter and decorative artist and the defining figure of Art Nouveau. His theatrical posters for Sarah Bernhardt swept Paris, and his graceful women, intricate floral ornament and Byzantine motifs shaped an era's aesthetic; his last years were devoted to the nationalist Slav Epic.","p":"images/a/Q146691.jpg"},"Valentin Serov":{"zh":"瓦连京·谢罗夫","en":"Valentin Serov","born":"1865","died":"1911","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"瓦连京·谢罗夫，俄罗斯最杰出的肖像画家之一，由巡回展览画派走向「艺术世界」团体。他兼取现实主义的观察与印象派的光色，《少女与桃》等作品清新灵动，代表了俄国肖像艺术的高峰。","bio_en":"Valentin Serov was one of Russia's finest portraitists, moving from the Peredvizhniki toward the Mir iskusstva circle. Combining realist observation with Impressionist light, works such as Girl with Peaches mark a high point of Russian portraiture.","p":"images/a/Q217128.jpg"},"Isaac Levitan":{"zh":"伊萨克·列维坦","en":"Isaac Levitan","born":"1860","died":"1900","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"伊萨克·列维坦，俄罗斯巡回展览画派风景大师，「心境风景」的代表。他与作家契诃夫交谊深厚，以抒情而质朴的笔调描绘俄罗斯大地的辽阔与忧郁，深刻影响了俄国风景画。","bio_en":"Isaac Levitan was a master of the Russian Peredvizhniki landscape and of the lyrical 'mood landscape.' A close friend of the writer Chekhov, he painted the vastness and melancholy of the Russian land with poetic simplicity, profoundly shaping Russian landscape art.","p":"images/a/Q211356.jpg"},"Tsukioka Yoshitoshi":{"zh":"月冈芳年","en":"Tsukioka Yoshitoshi","born":"1839","died":"1892","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"月冈芳年，浮世绘最后的大师，跨越幕末与明治维新。他以《月百姿》《新形三十六怪撰》等系列著称，将历史、鬼怪与人物心理刻画得淋漓尽致，为衰落中的浮世绘注入最后的辉煌。","bio_en":"Tsukioka Yoshitoshi was the last great master of ukiyo-e, bridging the end of the Edo era and modern Meiji Japan. Famed for series such as One Hundred Aspects of the Moon, he brought intense psychological and dramatic power to historical and ghostly subjects, a final flowering of the tradition.","p":"images/a/Q467337.png"},"Kitagawa Utamaro":{"zh":"喜多川歌麿","en":"Kitagawa Utamaro","born":"1754","died":"1806","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"喜多川歌麿，浮世绘「美人画」的至高大师。他以半身特写捕捉女性的个性与神韵，构图优雅、线条精微，作品经由日本主义深刻影响了欧洲印象派。","bio_en":"Kitagawa Utamaro was the supreme master of bijin-ga, pictures of beautiful women. His refined half-length portraits captured individual feminine character and grace, and through Japonisme profoundly influenced European Impressionism.","p":"images/a/Q272045.jpg"},"Wang Hui":{"zh":"王翚","en":"Wang Hui","born":"1632","died":"1717","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"王翚，清初「四王」之一、虞山派领袖。他集宋元诸家山水之大成，笔墨精严，曾奉命主持绘制《康熙南巡图》长卷，是清代正统画派的集大成者。","bio_en":"Wang Hui was a leader of the orthodox 'Four Wangs' school of the early Qing. Synthesising the great Song and Yuan landscape traditions into meticulous brushwork, he directed the monumental scrolls of the Kangxi Emperor's Southern Inspection Tour.","p":"images/a/Q716222.jpg"},"Shitao":{"zh":"石涛","en":"Shitao","born":"1642","died":"1707","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"石涛，明宗室后裔、出家为僧，清初最富独创性的「四僧」之一。他反对泥古摹仿，主张「一画」之说、师法造化与自我，其奔放灵动的山水对近现代中国绘画影响深远。","bio_en":"Shitao, a descendant of the Ming royal house who became a monk, was one of the great individualist 'Four Monks' of the early Qing. Rejecting slavish imitation, he championed 'the single brushstroke' and painting from nature and self; his free, vital landscapes profoundly shaped modern Chinese painting.","p":"images/a/Q469439.jpg"},"Suzuki Harunobu":{"zh":"铃木春信","en":"Suzuki Harunobu","born":"1724","died":"1770","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"铃木春信，约 1765 年多色套印「锦绘」的开创者，使浮世绘进入full-color 时代。他以纤秀诗意的画风描绘年轻恋人与市井雅趣，色调柔美、意境含蓄。","bio_en":"Suzuki Harunobu pioneered the full-colour nishiki-e ('brocade print') around 1765, ushering ukiyo-e into the era of colour. His delicate, poetic images of youthful lovers and everyday elegance are prized for their soft palette and lyrical restraint.","p":null},"Tōshūsai Sharaku":{"zh":"东洲斋写乐","en":"Tōshūsai Sharaku","born":null,"died":"1801","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"东洲斋写乐，浮世绘史上最神秘的大师。他仅在 1794–95 年活跃约十个月，创作约 140 幅极其大胆、直指人物内心的役者绘，随即销声匿迹，真实身份至今成谜。","bio_en":"Tōshūsai Sharaku is the most mysterious master of ukiyo-e. Active for only about ten months in 1794–95, he produced some 140 startlingly candid, psychologically penetrating actor portraits and then vanished; his true identity is still debated.","p":null},"Wang Yuanqi":{"zh":"王原祁","en":"Wang Yuanqi","born":"1642","died":"1715","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"王原祁，王时敏之孙、清初「四王」之一，画论最富理论性者。他以董其昌的构成理念营造层峦叠嶂的纪念碑式山水，主持康熙朝宫廷画事，影响清代画坛甚巨。","bio_en":"Wang Yuanqi, grandson of Wang Shimin and one of the 'Four Wangs,' was the most theoretical of the group. Building monumental landscapes from Dong Qichang's structural ideas, he served as the Kangxi court's painting authority and shaped Qing painting deeply.","p":"images/a/Q716338.jpg"},"Dong Qichang":{"zh":"董其昌","en":"Dong Qichang","born":"1555","died":"1636","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"董其昌，晚明士大夫画家、书法家与理论家。他提出山水画「南北宗论」，深刻塑造了后世文人画的取向；其山水结构峻峭、笔墨秀润，是文人画的一代宗师。","bio_en":"Dong Qichang was a towering late-Ming scholar-official painter, calligrapher and theorist. His theory of 'Northern and Southern Schools' of landscape shaped the direction of later literati painting; his own austere, structural landscapes made him a defining master.","p":"images/a/Q537211.jpg"},"Hua Yan":{"zh":"华喦","en":"Hua Yan","born":"1682","died":"1756","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"华喦，清代多才的文人画家，与扬州画派关系密切。他的花鸟、人物与山水皆清新灵动、格调雅逸，尤以生动传神的禽鸟著称。","bio_en":"Hua Yan was a versatile Qing literati painter linked to the Yangzhou circle. His bird-and-flower, figure and landscape paintings are lively and refined, and he is especially admired for his vivid, spirited birds.","p":"images/a/Q1042125.jpg"},"Shen Zhou":{"zh":"沈周","en":"Shen Zhou","born":"1427","died":"1509","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"沈周，明代吴门画派的开创者、当世文人画领袖，文徵明之师。他一生不仕，以温厚质朴的山水与册页闻名，将文人画的意趣推向新的高度。","bio_en":"Shen Zhou was the founder of the Ming Wu School and the leading literati painter of his day, teacher of Wen Zhengming. Never taking office, he is celebrated for warm, unpretentious landscapes and album leaves that raised literati painting to new heights.","p":"images/a/Q558863.jpg"},"Wen Zhengming":{"zh":"文徵明","en":"Wen Zhengming","born":"1470","died":"1559","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"文徵明，吴门画派核心大师、沈周弟子，「明四家」之一。他以精工细致的山水和高洁的品格著称，兼为一代书法大家，享寿九十，影响吴地画坛数十年。","bio_en":"Wen Zhengming was a central master of the Wu School, pupil of Shen Zhou and one of the 'Four Masters of the Ming.' Renowned for refined, meticulous landscapes and upright character, he was also a great calligrapher whose long life shaped the Suzhou art world for decades.","p":"images/a/Q306673.jpg"},"Yun Shouping":{"zh":"恽寿平","en":"Yun Shouping","born":"1633","died":"1690","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"恽寿平，清初「六大家」之一，复兴了「没骨」花卉画法。他不用墨线勾勒，直接以色彩晕染花卉，清丽透明、生趣盎然，别开生面。","bio_en":"Yun Shouping, one of the 'Six Masters of the early Qing,' revived the 'boneless' (mogu) technique of flower painting. Dispensing with ink outlines and modelling blossoms directly in colour, he created delicate, luminous and lifelike studies.","p":"images/a/Q1329823.jpg"},"Bada Shanren":{"zh":"八大山人","en":"Bada Shanren","born":"1626","died":"1705","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"八大山人，明朝宗室，国破后削发为僧。他以极简而奇崛的水墨描绘鱼、鸟与山水，形象孤傲、意味冷峭，饱含亡国之痛与反讽，是个性派绘画的开山灵魂。","bio_en":"Bada Shanren was a Ming prince who became a Chan monk after the dynasty fell. His radically spare, eccentric ink paintings of fish, birds and landscapes—aloof, sardonic and charged with the grief of loss—make him a founding spirit of individualist painting.","p":"images/a/Q198097.jpg"},"Chen Hongshou":{"zh":"陈洪绶","en":"Chen Hongshou","born":"1598","died":"1652","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"陈洪绶，明末清初人物画大师。他的人物造型高古夸张、衣纹如铁线盘曲，别具奇趣；所作版画插图（如《水浒叶子》）流传极广，影响深远。","bio_en":"Chen Hongshou was a master of figure painting of the late Ming and early Qing. His figures are archaistic, elongated and strangely compelling; his widely circulated woodblock illustrations were hugely influential.","p":"images/a/Q588110.jpg"},"Kawanabe Kyōsai":{"zh":"河锅晓斋","en":"Kawanabe Kyōsai","born":"1831","died":"1889","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"河锅晓斋，幕末至明治的鬼才画家与讽刺画家。他兼修浮世绘与狩野派，笔力奔放，尤以乌鸦、妖怪和辛辣的时事讽刺闻名，充满旺盛的想象力。","bio_en":"Kawanabe Kyōsai was a fiercely inventive painter and caricaturist of the late Edo and Meiji periods. Trained in both ukiyo-e and the Kanō school, he is famous for his crows, demons and biting satire, brimming with imaginative energy.","p":"images/a/Q2838030.jpg"},"Qiu Ying":{"zh":"仇英","en":"Qiu Ying","born":"1494","died":"1548","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"仇英，出身寒微而跻身「明四家」的职业画家巨匠。他工笔精丽，尤擅青绿山水与人物故事画，摹古而能出新，设色富丽、一丝不苟。","bio_en":"Qiu Ying, of humble origins, rose to be one of the 'Four Masters of the Ming' and a supreme professional painter. A master of meticulous blue-green landscapes and narrative figure scenes, he copied the ancients yet renewed them with rich, exacting colour.","p":"images/a/Q769372.jpg"},"Ma Yuan":{"zh":"马远","en":"Ma Yuan","born":"1160","died":"1225","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"马远，南宋画院大师，人称「马一角」。他开创「一角」式构图，只取景物一隅、余处留白如烟水苍茫，营造出诗意含蓄、空灵深远的山水意境。","bio_en":"Ma Yuan was a master of the Southern Song Painting Academy, nicknamed 'One-Corner Ma.' He pioneered the asymmetric 'one-corner' composition—placing motifs to one side amid misty voids—to create poetic, spare and profoundly atmospheric landscapes.","p":null},"Abanindranath Tagore":{"zh":"阿巴宁德拉纳特·泰戈尔","en":"Abanindranath Tagore","born":"1871","died":"1951","cty_zh":"印度","cty_en":"India","bio_zh":"阿巴宁德拉纳特·泰戈尔，孟加拉画派的创始人、印度现代艺术先驱。他融合莫卧儿、拉杰普特与东亚水墨的技法，创造出富民族气质的新风格，以对抗殖民时期的西化学院派。","bio_en":"Abanindranath Tagore founded the Bengal School and pioneered modern Indian art. Blending Mughal, Rajput and East Asian wash techniques, he forged a distinctly national style in resistance to colonial-era Western academicism.","p":"images/a/Q691796.jpg"},"Xu Wei":{"zh":"徐渭","en":"Xu Wei","born":"1521","died":"1593","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"徐渭，明代才华横溢却命运坎坷的诗人画家。他开创水墨大写意花卉，以酣畅淋漓、纵横恣肆的泼墨挥洒胸中块垒，深受后世八大、石涛与齐白石推崇。","bio_en":"Xu Wei was a brilliant but tormented Ming poet-painter. Father of the free 'splashed-ink' xieyi flower style, his explosive, spontaneous brushwork poured out his inner turmoil and was revered by later individualists from Bada Shanren to Qi Baishi.","p":"images/a/Q890211.jpg"},"Katsukawa Shunshō":{"zh":"胜川春章","en":"Katsukawa Shunshō","born":"1726","died":"1793","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"胜川春章，浮世绘役者绘的革新者。他一改程式化的演员形象，首创写实的个人相貌肖像；也精于美人画，并是葛饰北斋的老师。","bio_en":"Katsukawa Shunshō reformed the actor print, replacing stylised faces with individualised likenesses. Also accomplished in bijin-ga, he was the teacher of Hokusai.","p":null},"Ni Zan":{"zh":"倪瓒","en":"Ni Zan","born":"1306","died":"1374","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"倪瓒，「元四家」之一，文人画理想的化身。他以极简的构图、疏淡的笔墨描绘荒寒的江岸小景，一河两岸、无人萧疏，格调孤高清逸，为后世推为逸品典范。","bio_en":"Ni Zan, one of the 'Four Masters of the Yuan,' embodied the literati ideal. His sparse compositions and cool, dry brush depict desolate riverbanks—water between two shores, empty and still—of extreme refinement and lofty detachment.","p":"images/a/Q731030.jpg"},"Jin Nong":{"zh":"金农","en":"Jin Nong","born":"1687","died":"1763","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"金农，「扬州八怪」之首。他博学好古，画梅、竹、人物与佛像皆奇古拙朴，独创方硬厚重的「漆书」书体，个性鲜明、别开生面。","bio_en":"Jin Nong was the leading figure of the 'Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou.' Learned and antiquarian, he painted plum, bamboo, figures and Buddhas with a deliberate archaic awkwardness, and invented the blunt, lacquer-like calligraphy that bears his distinctive stamp.","p":"images/a/Q710049.jpg"},"Ren Xiong":{"zh":"任熊","en":"Ren Xiong","born":"1823","died":"1857","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"任熊，海上画派的早期核心人物。他人物画气势雄强、造型奇崛，尤以一幅顶天立地、直视观者的巨幅《自画像》震撼后世；惜英年早逝。","bio_en":"Ren Xiong was a key early figure of the Shanghai School. His figure paintings are bold and strikingly conceived, above all his arresting life-size Self-Portrait staring out at the viewer; he died young.","p":"images/a/Q3080169.jpg"},"Raja Ravi Varma":{"zh":"拉贾·拉维·瓦尔马","en":"Raja Ravi Varma","born":"1848","died":"1906","cty_zh":"印度","cty_en":"India","bio_zh":"拉贾·拉维·瓦尔马，将欧洲学院派油画技法与印度题材相融合的先驱。他描绘的印度教神话人物经由平版印刷大量复制、深入民间，塑造了印度大众的神祇形象。","bio_en":"Raja Ravi Varma was a pioneer who fused European academic oil technique with Indian subjects. His depictions of Hindu mythological figures, mass-produced as oleograph prints, shaped popular religious iconography across India.","p":"images/a/Q333453.jpg"},"Gong Xian":{"zh":"龚贤","en":"Gong Xian","born":"1619","died":"1689","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"龚贤，「金陵八家」之首。他以层层积染的浓重墨法营造出幽深沉郁的「黑龚」山水，草木葱茏、气象森然，在清初画坛别树一帜。","bio_en":"Gong Xian was the foremost of the 'Eight Masters of Nanjing.' Building dense, brooding 'black' landscapes from layered ink washes, he created a deep, sombre and utterly distinctive vision in early-Qing painting.","p":null},"Utagawa Toyokuni":{"zh":"歌川丰国","en":"Utagawa Toyokuni","born":"1769","died":"1825","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"歌川丰国，浮世绘最强画派——歌川派的奠基者。他以富于动感、贴近舞台的役者绘风靡一时，门下国芳、国贞等名家辈出，主导了幕末浮世绘。","bio_en":"Utagawa Toyokuni founded the Utagawa school, the most powerful ukiyo-e lineage. Celebrated for dynamic, stage-vivid actor prints, he trained masters such as Kuniyoshi and Kunisada and dominated late-Edo ukiyo-e.","p":"images/a/Q950316.jpg"},"Keisai Eisen":{"zh":"溪斋英泉","en":"Keisai Eisen","born":"1791","died":"1848","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"溪斋英泉，以妖冶的美人画和风景版画著称的浮世绘师。他笔下的女性风情浓艳、别具颓废之美，并与广重合作了《木曾街道六十九次》。","bio_en":"Keisai Eisen was an ukiyo-e master known for sensuous bijin-ga and landscape prints. His women have a heavy, decadent allure, and he collaborated with Hiroshige on the Sixty-nine Stations of the Kiso Road.","p":"images/a/Q3046492.jpg"},"Zheng Xie":{"zh":"郑燮","en":"Zheng Xie","born":"1693","died":"1766","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"郑燮（郑板桥），「扬州八怪」中最受喜爱者。他画兰、竹、石清劲潇洒，配以自创的「六分半书」，诗书画三绝；为官清廉爱民，是一位耿介的文人。","bio_en":"Zheng Xie (Zheng Banqiao) was the best-loved of the 'Eight Eccentrics of Yangzhou.' His crisp ink bamboo, orchids and rocks, paired with his self-invented 'six-and-a-half-part' calligraphy, unite poetry, calligraphy and painting; he was also an upright, people-loving magistrate.","p":"images/a/Q712007.png"},"Chōbunsai Eishi":{"zh":"鸟文斋荣之","en":"Chōbunsai Eishi","born":"1756","died":"1829","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"鸟文斋荣之，出身武士的浮世绘大师。他笔下的美人身姿修长、气质高华，透着贵族式的优雅娴静，自成一格。","bio_en":"Chōbunsai Eishi was a samurai-born ukiyo-e master. His beauties are slender and aristocratic, radiating a refined, courtly grace all his own.","p":"images/a/Q2972127.jpg"},"Wu Zhen":{"zh":"吴镇","en":"Wu Zhen","born":"1280","died":"1354","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"吴镇，「元四家」之一，隐居不仕的高士。他擅画墨竹与渔父山水，用墨湿润苍茫、书法气息浓厚，意境冷寂而深远。","bio_en":"Wu Zhen, one of the 'Four Masters of the Yuan,' was a recluse who never served. Painting ink bamboo and misty fishermen-in-landscape with a wet, calligraphic brush, he achieved a still, remote and profound mood.","p":null},"Wang Meng":{"zh":"王蒙","en":"Wang Meng","born":"1308","died":"1385","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"王蒙，「元四家」之一，赵孟頫之外孙。他的山水繁密苍郁、皴法层叠繁复，以「解索皴」「牛毛皴」写出重峦叠嶂的蓬勃生机，在四家中最见繁复之美。","bio_en":"Wang Meng, one of the 'Four Masters of the Yuan' and grandson of Zhao Mengfu, painted densely textured, restless mountain landscapes. His layered, intricate brushwork conjures teeming, luxuriant peaks—the most complex vision among the four.","p":null},"Utagawa Kuniyoshi":{"zh":"歌川国芳","en":"Utagawa Kuniyoshi","born":"1798","died":"1861","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"歌川国芳，歌川派巨匠，幕末浮世绘的奇想天才。他以气势磅礴的武者绘（《水浒传》豪杰、历史合战）名震一时，又擅长诙谐的戏画、拟人化的猫与金鱼，想象力天马行空，是浮世绘晚期最富创造力的大师之一。","bio_en":"Utagawa Kuniyoshi was a giant of the Utagawa school and a wildly inventive genius of late ukiyo-e. Renowned for dynamic warrior prints—heroes of the Suikoden and historical battles—he also delighted in caricature and anthropomorphic cats and fish, one of the most imaginative masters of the tradition's last age.","p":"images/a/Q235886.jpg"},"Utagawa Kunisada":{"zh":"歌川国贞","en":"Utagawa Kunisada","born":"1786","died":"1865","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"歌川国贞（后称三代歌川丰国），幕末最多产、商业上最成功的浮世绘师。他一生设计版画数以万计，尤以歌舞伎役者绘与时尚美人画称霸市场，是歌川派鼎盛的代表。","bio_en":"Utagawa Kunisada (later Toyokuni III) was the most prolific and commercially successful ukiyo-e designer of the late Edo period. Producing tens of thousands of prints, he dominated the market with kabuki actor portraits and fashionable beauties, epitomising the Utagawa school at its height.","p":null},"Torii Kiyonaga":{"zh":"鸟居清长","en":"Torii Kiyonaga","born":"1752","died":"1815","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"鸟居清长，鸟居派宗师，天明年间美人画的定义者。他笔下修长挺拔、雍容端丽的全身美人，构图开阔、气度高华，将浮世绘美人画推向黄金时代的一个高峰。","bio_en":"Torii Kiyonaga, head of the Torii school, defined the bijin-ga of the 1780s. His tall, stately full-length beauties, set in spacious compositions of great elegance, brought the ukiyo-e depiction of women to one of its golden-age peaks.","p":null},"Kobayashi Kiyochika":{"zh":"小林清亲","en":"Kobayashi Kiyochika","born":"1847","died":"1915","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"小林清亲，人称「最后的浮世绘大师」。他开创「光线画」，以西洋式的光影明暗描绘明治东京的煤气灯、铁道与暮色，为古老的木版画注入近代都市的诗意；亦作战争题材版画。","bio_en":"Kobayashi Kiyochika is often called the last great master of ukiyo-e. He pioneered kōsen-ga ('light-ray pictures'), using Western-influenced light and shadow to capture the gaslight, railways and twilight of Meiji Tokyo, bringing a modern urban poetry to the old woodblock medium; he also made war prints.","p":"images/a/Q3121142.png"},"Utagawa Yoshiiku":{"zh":"落合芳几","en":"Utagawa Yoshiiku","born":"1833","died":"1904","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"落合芳几，歌川国芳门下，幕末明治的浮世绘师。他以役者绘著称，曾与芳年合作骇人的「无惨绘」，明治维新后转向新闻插画，是浮世绘走向近代报刊的过渡人物。","bio_en":"Utagawa Yoshiiku, a pupil of Kuniyoshi, was an ukiyo-e artist of the late Edo and Meiji eras. Known for actor prints, he collaborated with Yoshitoshi on the gruesome 'bloody prints' (muzan-e) and later turned to newspaper illustration—a bridge from ukiyo-e to the modern Meiji press.","p":null},"Francesco Guardi":{"zh":"弗朗切斯科·瓜尔迪","en":"Francesco Guardi","born":"1712","died":"1793","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"弗朗切斯科·瓜尔迪，威尼斯画派最后一位伟大的景观画大师。他继卡纳莱托之后描绘潟湖之城，却以疏松灵动的笔触、颤动的光影与如梦的「随想景」（capricci），将精准的城市写实升华为诗意的氛围，被视为浪漫主义与印象派的先声。","bio_en":"Francesco Guardi was the last great master of the Venetian view painting. Working after Canaletto, he rendered the lagoon city with loose, shimmering brushwork and dreamlike capricci, transforming topographical precision into poetic atmosphere and foreshadowing Romanticism and Impressionism.","p":"images/a/Q318769.jpg"},"Guido Reni":{"zh":"圭多·雷尼","en":"Guido Reni","born":"1575","died":"1642","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"圭多·雷尼，博洛尼亚画派的巴洛克大师。他以理想化的优雅、澄澈的色彩与虔敬的宗教题材著称，天顶壁画《曙光》（Aurora）尤为传世，古典之美深受后世推崇。","bio_en":"Guido Reni was a leading Baroque master of the Bolognese school. Celebrated for idealized grace, luminous color, and devout religious subjects, his ceiling fresco Aurora remains among the most admired examples of classical beauty in seventeenth-century painting.","p":"images/a/Q109061.jpg"},"Guercino":{"zh":"圭尔奇诺","en":"Guercino","born":"1591","died":"1666","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"圭尔奇诺，博洛尼亚巴洛克绘画的代表人物。早年作品以强烈的明暗对比与充沛的动感震撼人心，罗马路多维西别墅的天顶壁画《曙光》（Aurora）气势恢宏；晚年则转向更为古典宁静的风格。","bio_en":"Guercino was a major figure of Bolognese Baroque painting. His early works astonish with bold chiaroscuro and dynamic energy—epitomized by the sweeping ceiling fresco Aurora in Rome's Casino Ludovisi—while his later manner grew more classical and serene.","p":"images/a/Q334262.jpg"},"Salvator Rosa":{"zh":"萨尔瓦托·罗萨","en":"Salvator Rosa","born":"1615","died":"1673","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"萨尔瓦托·罗萨，那不勒斯出身的巴洛克画家、诗人与叛逆的浪漫先驱。他钟情于荒野崎岖的风景、战争场面与巫术奇想，狂放不羁的想象与阴郁氛围，深深影响了后世的浪漫主义。","bio_en":"Salvator Rosa was a Neapolitan Baroque painter and poet, and a rebellious proto-Romantic spirit. Drawn to wild, rugged landscapes, battle scenes, and scenes of witchcraft, his untamed imagination and brooding mood would deeply inspire later Romanticism.","p":"images/a/Q359421.jpg"},"Bernardo Bellotto":{"zh":"贝尔纳多·贝洛托","en":"Bernardo Bellotto","born":"1722","died":"1780","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"贝尔纳多·贝洛托，卡纳莱托的外甥与门生，威尼斯景观画传统的杰出继承者。他游历德累斯顿、维也纳与华沙，以冷冽精确、纤毫毕现的城市全景闻名；其华沙景观日后甚至成为战后重建这座城市的依据。","bio_en":"Bernardo Bellotto, nephew and pupil of Canaletto, was an outstanding heir to the Venetian view-painting tradition. Working across Dresden, Vienna, and Warsaw, he is renowned for cool, exacting cityscapes of meticulous detail—his Warsaw views later guiding the city's postwar reconstruction.","p":"images/a/Q164688.jpg"},"Cima da Conegliano":{"zh":"奇马·达·科内利亚诺","en":"Cima da Conegliano","born":"1459","died":"1517","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"奇马·达·科内利亚诺，威尼斯文艺复兴时期的重要画家。他承继乔瓦尼·贝利尼的传统，以宁静庄严的「圣母与圣徒对话」及背景中澄明温润的风景著称，画面充满恬静的虔敬之美。","bio_en":"Cima da Conegliano was a significant painter of the Venetian Renaissance. Following the tradition of Giovanni Bellini, he is admired for serene sacred conversations set against luminous, gentle landscapes, works imbued with a quiet and devout beauty.","p":null},"Federico Barocci":{"zh":"费代里科·巴罗奇","en":"Federico Barocci","born":"1535","died":"1612","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"费代里科·巴罗奇，出身乌尔比诺，是连接手法主义与巴洛克的关键画家。他以柔和的晕染、温暖细腻的色彩与充满情感的宗教场景著称，虔敬动人的画风对后来的巴洛克绘画影响深远。","bio_en":"Federico Barocci, from Urbino, was a pivotal painter bridging Mannerism and the Baroque. Known for soft sfumato, warm and tender coloring, and emotionally charged religious scenes, his devout and moving style profoundly influenced later Baroque painting.","p":"images/a/Q316731.jpg"},"Pietro da Cortona":{"zh":"彼得罗·达·科尔托纳","en":"Pietro da Cortona","born":"1596","died":"1669","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"彼得罗·达·科尔托纳，罗马盛期巴洛克的领军画家兼建筑师。他擅长气势磅礴、幻觉深远的天顶壁画，巴贝里尼宫的《神意的寓言》即为其宏伟装饰风格的巅峰之作。","bio_en":"Pietro da Cortona was a leading painter and architect of the Roman High Baroque. A master of grand, illusionistic ceiling frescoes, his Allegory of Divine Providence in the Palazzo Barberini stands as the summit of his magnificent decorative style.","p":"images/a/Q333323.jpg"},"Giovanni Battista Moroni":{"zh":"乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·莫罗尼","en":"Giovanni Battista Moroni","born":"1525","died":"1578","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·莫罗尼，文艺复兴时期伦巴第地区最杰出的肖像画家。他摒弃理想化，以质朴真切的目光描绘各阶层人物，《裁缝》一作直视观者、平实动人，被誉为最早的世俗写实肖像之一。","bio_en":"Giovanni Battista Moroni was the finest portraitist of Renaissance Lombardy. Rejecting idealization, he portrayed sitters of every rank with unvarnished truth; his Tailor, meeting the viewer's gaze with candid dignity, ranks among the earliest naturalistic secular portraits.","p":"images/a/Q504949.jpg"},"Luca Signorelli":{"zh":"卢卡·西尼奥雷利","en":"Luca Signorelli","born":"1450","died":"1523","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"卢卡·西尼奥雷利，意大利文艺复兴早期的重要画家。他在奥尔维耶托大教堂绘制的《末日审判》系列壁画气势撼人，以对人体解剖与肌肉动感的大胆刻画著称，直接启发了米开朗琪罗。","bio_en":"Luca Signorelli was an important painter of the early Italian Renaissance. His powerful Last Judgment fresco cycle in Orvieto Cathedral, celebrated for its bold rendering of the muscular nude in dramatic movement, directly influenced Michelangelo.","p":"images/a/Q7031.jpg"},"Rosalba Carriera":{"zh":"罗萨尔巴·卡列拉","en":"Rosalba Carriera","born":"1675","died":"1757","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"罗萨尔巴·卡列拉，威尼斯洛可可时期的女画家，粉彩肖像画的开创者。她以轻盈柔美、光泽细腻的粉彩笔法风靡全欧宫廷，是当时最负盛名的女性艺术家之一，并当选罗马圣路加学院院士。","bio_en":"Rosalba Carriera was a Venetian Rococo painter and a pioneer of pastel portraiture. Her light, delicate, and luminous handling of pastel enchanted the courts of Europe, making her one of the era's most celebrated women artists and a member of Rome's Accademia di San Luca.","p":"images/a/Q237726.jpg"},"Sebastiano del Piombo":{"zh":"塞巴斯蒂亚诺·德尔·皮翁博","en":"Sebastiano del Piombo","born":"1485","died":"1547","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"塞巴斯蒂亚诺·德尔·皮翁博，威尼斯出身、后活跃于罗马的盛期文艺复兴画家。他将威尼斯的丰润色彩与罗马的宏伟造型熔于一炉，与米开朗琪罗交谊深厚，《拉撒路的复活》即为二人合作精神的杰作。","bio_en":"Sebastiano del Piombo was a High Renaissance painter, Venetian by birth but active in Rome. Fusing Venetian richness of color with Roman monumentality, he was a close associate of Michelangelo, and his Raising of Lazarus embodies the fruits of that collaboration.","p":"images/a/Q285423.jpg"},"Pinturicchio":{"zh":"平图里基奥","en":"Pinturicchio","born":"1454","died":"1513","cty_zh":"意大利","cty_en":"Italy","bio_zh":"平图里基奥，翁布里亚画派的文艺复兴早期画家，以华美繁丽的装饰性壁画著称。他为梵蒂冈的波吉亚寓所与锡耶纳大教堂的皮科洛米尼图书馆绘制的壁画，色彩绚烂、细节精致，尽显盛期装饰艺术之富丽。","bio_en":"Pinturicchio was an early Renaissance painter of the Umbrian school, renowned for his sumptuous decorative frescoes. His cycles for the Borgia Apartments in the Vatican and the Piccolomini Library in Siena, brilliant in color and rich in detail, epitomize the splendor of Renaissance decoration.","p":"images/a/Q5591.jpg"},"David Teniers the Younger":{"zh":"小大卫·特尼耶斯","en":"David Teniers the Younger","born":"1610","died":"1690","cty_zh":"佛兰德斯","cty_en":"Flanders","bio_zh":"小大卫·特尼耶斯，佛兰德斯巴洛克最多产的风俗画家。他以农人宴饮、酒肆嬉闹与卫兵室场景闻名，又曾任奥地利大公利奥波德·威廉的宫廷画师，绘制其画廊藏品的「画中画」，为后世留下珍贵的收藏图录。","bio_en":"David Teniers the Younger was the most prolific genre painter of the Flemish Baroque. Celebrated for his peasant feasts, tavern scenes and guardrooms, he also served as court painter to Archduke Leopold Wilhelm, documenting the archduke's picture gallery in his renowned 'gallery paintings.'","p":"images/a/Q335022.jpg"},"Jan Brueghel the Elder":{"zh":"老扬·勃鲁盖尔","en":"Jan Brueghel the Elder","born":"1568","died":"1625","cty_zh":"佛兰德斯","cty_en":"Flanders","bio_zh":"老扬·勃鲁盖尔，老彼得·勃鲁盖尔之子，因笔触细腻柔润而得「天鹅绒勃鲁盖尔」之名。他精于繁花静物、精微风景与乐园题材，常与鲁本斯合作，共同绘就《感官寓言》等杰作。","bio_en":"Jan Brueghel the Elder, son of Pieter Bruegel the Elder, was nicknamed 'Velvet Brueghel' for his soft, refined touch. A master of flower still lifes, minutely detailed landscapes and paradise scenes, he frequently collaborated with Rubens on works such as the 'Allegory of the Senses.'","p":"images/a/Q209050.jpg"},"Nicolaes Maes":{"zh":"尼古拉斯·马斯","en":"Nicolaes Maes","born":"1634","died":"1693","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"尼古拉斯·马斯，伦勃朗最富才华的弟子之一。早年以温情的家庭风俗画著称，尤擅「偷听者」题材与操持家务的妇女形象；晚年转向优雅的肖像画，成为多德雷赫特与阿姆斯特丹的时尚画师。","bio_en":"Nicolaes Maes was one of Rembrandt's most gifted pupils. Known first for tender domestic genre scenes—especially his 'eavesdropper' pictures and women at household tasks—he later turned to elegant portraiture, becoming a fashionable painter in Dordrecht and Amsterdam.","p":"images/a/Q505150.jpg"},"Willem van de Velde the Younger":{"zh":"小威廉·凡·德·维尔德","en":"Willem van de Velde the Younger","born":"1633","died":"1707","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"小威廉·凡·德·维尔德，荷兰黄金时代最杰出的海景画家。他以精准而富诗意的笔触描绘舰船、海战与波光云影，后赴英国供职于查理二世宫廷，其海洋画风影响英国画坛逾一个世纪。","bio_en":"Willem van de Velde the Younger was the foremost marine painter of the Dutch Golden Age. Rendering ships, sea battles and the play of light on water with precision and poetry, he moved to England to serve Charles II, shaping British marine painting for over a century.","p":"images/a/Q432266.jpg"},"Aelbert Cuyp":{"zh":"阿尔伯特·库普","en":"Aelbert Cuyp","born":"1620","died":"1691","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"阿尔伯特·库普，多德雷赫特的风景大师。他将意大利式的金色暖光引入荷兰田园，河畔牛群沐浴在夕照之中，静谧而辉煌，其光影处理深受后世英国风景画家推崇。","bio_en":"Aelbert Cuyp was the great landscapist of Dordrecht. He bathed the Dutch countryside in a golden, Italianate light—cattle resting by luminous rivers in the glow of evening—an atmospheric treatment later much admired by British landscape painters.","p":"images/a/Q313194.jpg"},"Hendrick Goltzius":{"zh":"亨德里克·霍尔奇乌斯","en":"Hendrick Goltzius","born":"1558","died":"1617","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"亨德里克·霍尔奇乌斯，北方风格主义的代表人物、荷兰最伟大的雕版大师。他以出神入化的刻刀技艺创造出富于韵律的「膨胀线条」，晚年方转攻油画，是版画艺术承前启后的关键人物。","bio_en":"Hendrick Goltzius was a leading figure of Northern Mannerism and the greatest Dutch engraver of his age. His virtuoso handling of the burin produced a rhythmic swelling line of extraordinary control, and only late in life did he turn to painting.","p":"images/a/Q165367.jpg"},"Gerrit Dou":{"zh":"格里特·道","en":"Gerrit Dou","born":"1613","died":"1675","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"格里特·道，伦勃朗的首位弟子，莱顿「精细画派」的开创者。他以珍宝般精微的小幅画作闻名，常以拱窗为框构图，对烛光与质感的刻画细致入微，生前声名甚至一度超过其师。","bio_en":"Gerrit Dou, Rembrandt's first pupil, founded the Leiden school of fijnschilders ('fine painters'). Famous for jewel-like small panels—often framed within a stone niche—and his exquisite rendering of candlelight and texture, he was in his day even more celebrated than his master.","p":"images/a/Q335927.jpg"},"Pieter Claesz":{"zh":"彼得·克拉斯","en":"Pieter Claesz","born":"1597","died":"1660","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"彼得·克拉斯，哈勒姆静物画的核心人物。他与同侪共创「单色早餐画」，以银灰的调子、简朴的杯盘与鲱鱼面包，营造出低回内敛的氛围，是荷兰调性静物的奠基者之一。","bio_en":"Pieter Claesz was a central figure of Haarlem still life. A pioneer of the 'monochrome breakfast piece' (ontbijtje), he composed humble arrangements of glassware, herring and bread in restrained silvery tones, helping to found the Dutch tradition of tonal still life.","p":"images/a/Q354832.jpg"},"Adriaen Brouwer":{"zh":"阿德里安·布劳威尔","en":"Adriaen Brouwer","born":"1605","died":"1638","cty_zh":"佛兰德斯","cty_en":"Flanders","bio_zh":"阿德里安·布劳威尔，横跨佛兰德斯与荷兰的农民生活画家。他以粗犷生动的笔触描绘酒肆斗殴、烟客与市井百态，情感炽烈而直率，虽英年早逝，却深刻影响了特尼耶斯与奥斯塔德。","bio_en":"Adriaen Brouwer painted low-life scenes across both Flanders and Holland. With rough, vivid brushwork he captured tavern brawls, smokers and rustic revelry with raw immediacy, and though he died young, he profoundly influenced Teniers and Ostade.","p":"images/a/Q364139.jpg"},"Gabriël Metsu":{"zh":"加布里埃尔·梅曲","en":"Gabriël Metsu","born":"1629","died":"1667","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"加布里埃尔·梅曲，荷兰黄金时代精致风俗画的名家。他活跃于莱顿与阿姆斯特丹，擅绘室内场景中的书信往还与日常生活，色彩温润、情致细腻，与维米尔的题材遥相呼应。","bio_en":"Gabriël Metsu was a master of refined genre painting in the Dutch Golden Age. Working in Leiden and Amsterdam, he excelled at intimate interiors—letter-writers and readers, quiet domestic moments—rendered with warm color and delicate feeling akin to Vermeer's themes.","p":"images/a/Q355213.jpg"},"Jan van Huysum":{"zh":"扬·凡·海瑟姆","en":"Jan van Huysum","born":"1682","died":"1749","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"扬·凡·海瑟姆，十八世纪荷兰花卉静物的集大成者。他以浅色背景衬托繁复绚烂的花束，果实与花瓣的质感纤毫毕现，技艺登峰造极，享誉全欧，为荷兰花卉画划下辉煌的句点。","bio_en":"Jan van Huysum was the supreme flower painter of the eighteenth-century Netherlands. Setting sumptuous, elaborate bouquets against light backgrounds and rendering petal and fruit with dazzling finish, his technical brilliance won fame across Europe and crowned the Dutch flower-painting tradition.","p":"images/a/Q527869.jpg"},"Meindert Hobbema":{"zh":"梅因德特·霍贝玛","en":"Meindert Hobbema","born":"1638","died":"1709","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"梅因德特·霍贝玛，雅各布·凡·雷斯达尔的弟子、荷兰黄金时代最后一位风景大师。他钟情于水磨坊与林间小径，代表作《米德尔哈尼斯的林荫道》以笔直延伸的透视线享誉画史。","bio_en":"Meindert Hobbema, pupil of Jacob van Ruisdael, was among the last great landscapists of the Dutch Golden Age. Drawn to watermills and wooded lanes, he is celebrated above all for 'The Avenue at Middelharnis,' with its bold, receding line of perspective.","p":"images/a/Q336908.jpg"},"Rachel Ruysch":{"zh":"拉赫尔·勒伊斯","en":"Rachel Ruysch","born":"1664","died":"1750","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"拉赫尔·勒伊斯，荷兰最负盛名的女性花卉画家。她以深色背景衬托精巧的花果昆虫构图，笔触细腻、植物学般精确，艺术生涯逾六十载，是十八世纪最受推崇的静物名家之一。","bio_en":"Rachel Ruysch was the most renowned woman flower painter of the Netherlands. Composing intricate arrangements of blossoms, fruit and insects against dark grounds with delicate, near-botanical precision, she sustained a career of over sixty years as one of the most admired still-life painters of her time.","p":"images/a/Q234385.jpg"},"Willem Kalf":{"zh":"威廉·卡尔夫","en":"Willem Kalf","born":"1619","died":"1693","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"威廉·卡尔夫，荷兰「炫饰静物」的巅峰代表。他偏爱描绘中国瓷器、鹦鹉螺杯与银器等奢华器物，在幽暗背景中令光泽与色彩熠熠生辉，将静物画提升至近乎肖像的庄重气度。","bio_en":"Willem Kalf was the supreme master of the Dutch pronkstilleven, or sumptuous still life. Favoring luxurious objects—Chinese porcelain, nautilus cups and silver—he made their surfaces glow with light and color against dark grounds, lending still life an almost portrait-like gravity.","p":"images/a/Q28144.jpg"},"Hendrick ter Brugghen":{"zh":"亨德里克·特·布吕亨","en":"Hendrick ter Brugghen","born":"1588","died":"1629","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"亨德里克·特·布吕亨，乌得勒支卡拉瓦乔派的领军人物。他游学罗马，深受卡拉瓦乔明暗对照法启迪，归国后以强烈的光影描绘乐师、饮者与宗教场景，将意大利画风引入荷兰北部。","bio_en":"Hendrick ter Brugghen was a leading figure of the Utrecht Caravaggisti. Having studied in Rome under Caravaggio's spell, he returned to paint musicians, drinkers and religious scenes in dramatic chiaroscuro, bringing the Italian manner to the northern Netherlands.","p":"images/a/Q437233.jpg"},"Judith Leyster":{"zh":"尤迪特·莱斯特","en":"Judith Leyster","born":"1609","died":"1660","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"尤迪特·莱斯特，哈勒姆圣路加行会中罕见的女性画师。她身处弗兰斯·哈尔斯的圈子，以明快灵动的笔触描绘欢宴人物与烛光场景，代表作《求爱》细腻动人，是荷兰黄金时代杰出的女性画家。","bio_en":"Judith Leyster was one of the few women admitted to the Haarlem Guild of St Luke. Working within the circle of Frans Hals, she painted merry company and candlelit scenes with a lively, spontaneous touch, her 'The Proposal' among the finest works by a woman of the Dutch Golden Age.","p":"images/a/Q232423.jpg"},"Adriaen van Ostade":{"zh":"阿德里安·凡·奥斯塔德","en":"Adriaen van Ostade","born":"1610","died":"1685","cty_zh":"荷兰","cty_en":"Netherlands","bio_zh":"阿德里安·凡·奥斯塔德，哈勒姆农民风俗画的代表大师。他以温厚幽默的笔调描绘农舍与酒肆中的市井生活，光影柔和、人物生动，与其师弗兰斯·哈尔斯及布劳威尔的传统一脉相承。","bio_en":"Adriaen van Ostade was the leading painter of peasant genre in Haarlem. With warm humor he depicted cottage interiors and tavern life, his figures animated by soft, glowing light, carrying forward the tradition of his teacher Frans Hals and of Adriaen Brouwer.","p":"images/a/Q352438.jpg"},"Hubert Robert":{"zh":"于贝尔·罗贝尔","en":"Hubert Robert","born":"1733","died":"1808","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"于贝尔·罗贝尔，十八世纪法国最负盛名的废墟与建筑风景画家，人称「废墟的罗贝尔」。他将古罗马遗迹与想象的宫苑熔于笔下，营造出诗意而略带感伤的怀古幻境，晚年更参与筹建卢浮宫，是最早的博物馆策展人之一。","bio_en":"Hubert Robert was eighteenth-century France's foremost painter of ruins and architectural landscape, nicknamed 'Robert des Ruines.' Fusing Roman remains with imaginary gardens and palaces into poetic, wistfully evocative capricci, he also helped organize the new Louvre, becoming one of its earliest curators.","p":"images/a/Q548205.jpg"},"Jean-Baptiste Greuze":{"zh":"让-巴蒂斯特·格勒兹","en":"Jean-Baptiste Greuze","born":"1725","died":"1805","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-巴蒂斯特·格勒兹，十八世纪法国感伤风俗画的代表人物。他以《乡村订婚》一类富于道德训诫的家庭场景打动观众，为狄德罗所激赏，其煽情叙事与朴素平民题材，回应了洛可可之外对真挚情感的追求。","bio_en":"Jean-Baptiste Greuze was the leading figure of sentimental genre painting in eighteenth-century France. With moralizing domestic scenes such as The Village Betrothal, admired by Diderot, his emotive storytelling and humble subjects answered a growing appetite for sincerity beyond Rococo elegance.","p":"images/a/Q347139.jpg"},"Philippe de Champaigne":{"zh":"菲利普·德·尚帕涅","en":"Philippe de Champaigne","born":"1602","died":"1674","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"菲利普·德·尚帕涅，十七世纪法国巴洛克绘画的重要大师，尤以肃穆内敛的宗教画与肖像著称。他与冉森派的波尔-罗亚尔修道院往来密切，代表作《一六六二年还愿图》以清冷严整的构图与虔敬气质，成为法国古典主义精神的写照。","bio_en":"Philippe de Champaigne was a major master of seventeenth-century French Baroque, celebrated for his austere, restrained religious paintings and portraits. Closely tied to the Jansenist convent of Port-Royal, his Ex-Voto of 1662, with its cool and rigorous composition, embodies the devout spirit of French classicism.","p":"images/a/Q314814.jpg"},"Nicolas de Largillière":{"zh":"尼古拉·德·拉吉利埃","en":"Nicolas de Largillière","born":"1656","died":"1746","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"尼古拉·德·拉吉利埃，十七至十八世纪法国巴洛克肖像画的巨匠。他为巴黎的富裕市民与贵族留下大量气派而生动的肖像，以华丽的衣饰质感、丰盈的色彩与从容姿态，与里戈同为路易时代肖像艺术的双璧。","bio_en":"Nicolas de Largillière was a great master of French Baroque portraiture spanning the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries. He left a vast gallery of grand yet lively likenesses of Parisian bourgeoisie and nobility, and with his sumptuous fabrics, rich color and easy poses stood alongside Rigaud atop the portrait art of the age of Louis.","p":"images/a/Q550302.jpg"},"Hyacinthe Rigaud":{"zh":"亚森特·里戈","en":"Hyacinthe Rigaud","born":"1659","died":"1743","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"亚森特·里戈，路易十四时代最负盛名的宫廷肖像画家。他一七〇一年所作《路易十四像》，以雍容的仪态、飘扬的加冕披风与炫目的织物，确立了欧洲君主国事肖像的典范，影响绵延一个多世纪。","bio_en":"Hyacinthe Rigaud was the most celebrated court portraitist of the age of Louis XIV. His 1701 State Portrait of Louis XIV, with its majestic bearing, sweeping coronation robes and dazzling fabrics, defined the model of the European royal state portrait for well over a century.","p":"images/a/Q49898.jpg"},"Simon Vouet":{"zh":"西蒙·武埃","en":"Simon Vouet","born":"1590","died":"1649","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"西蒙·武埃，将意大利巴洛克引入法国的关键人物。早年久居罗马声名鹊起，归国后成为路易十三时代最具影响力的画家，以明快的色彩与舒展的构图重塑法国画坛，并培育出勒布伦等一代英才。","bio_en":"Simon Vouet was the key figure who brought the Italian Baroque to France. After winning fame during long years in Rome, he returned to become the most influential painter under Louis XIII, reshaping French art with luminous color and expansive compositions and training a generation that included Le Brun.","p":"images/a/Q317920.jpg"},"Charles Le Brun":{"zh":"夏尔·勒布伦","en":"Charles Le Brun","born":"1619","died":"1690","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"夏尔·勒布伦，路易十四时代法国艺术的绝对主宰。身为国王首席画师与皇家绘画雕塑学院的实际领袖，他主持哥白林制造厂并设计凡尔赛镜厅的天顶装饰，为法国确立了庄严宏大的古典主义官方风格。","bio_en":"Charles Le Brun was the absolute arbiter of French art under Louis XIV. As First Painter to the King and effective head of the Royal Academy, he directed the Gobelins manufactory and designed the ceiling decorations of the Hall of Mirrors at Versailles, forging France's grand, official classical style.","p":"images/a/Q271676.jpg"},"Jean-Baptiste Oudry":{"zh":"让-巴蒂斯特·乌德里","en":"Jean-Baptiste Oudry","born":"1686","died":"1755","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"让-巴蒂斯特·乌德里，法国洛可可时期杰出的动物、狩猎与静物画家。他以精准而生动的笔触描绘走兽、猎犬与野味，深得王室喜爱，并长期主持博韦挂毯厂，为拉封丹《寓言》所作插图亦广为流传。","bio_en":"Jean-Baptiste Oudry was an outstanding Rococo painter of animals, the hunt and still life. His precise, vivid renderings of beasts, hounds and game won royal favor, and he long directed the Beauvais tapestry works, while his illustrations for La Fontaine's Fables enjoyed wide renown.","p":"images/a/Q737137.jpg"},"Nicolas Lancret":{"zh":"尼古拉·朗克雷","en":"Nicolas Lancret","born":"1689","died":"1743","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"尼古拉·朗克雷，洛可可「雅宴」题材的代表画家，华托最出色的追随者之一。他以轻盈明丽的笔调描绘贵族男女的游园、舞会与嬉游场景，气氛欢愉优雅，深受路易十五宫廷的青睐。","bio_en":"Nicolas Lancret was a leading painter of the Rococo fête galante and one of Watteau's most gifted followers. With a light, luminous touch he depicted elegant ladies and gentlemen at garden parties, balls and amusements, their gaiety and grace much prized at the court of Louis XV.","p":"images/a/Q188172.jpg"},"Maurice Quentin de La Tour":{"zh":"莫里斯·康坦·德·拉图尔","en":"Maurice Quentin de La Tour","born":"1704","died":"1788","cty_zh":"法国","cty_en":"France","bio_zh":"莫里斯·康坦·德·拉图尔，十八世纪法国最伟大的粉彩肖像画家。他以粉彩捕捉人物神情的细腻与鲜活著称，人称「灵魂的绘写者」，曾为路易十五、蓬帕杜夫人及众多启蒙名士传神写照。","bio_en":"Maurice Quentin de La Tour was the greatest French pastel portraitist of the eighteenth century. Renowned for capturing the vivacity and subtle expression of his sitters, and dubbed the painter of souls, he portrayed Louis XV, Madame de Pompadour and many luminaries of the Enlightenment.","p":"images/a/Q314655.jpg"},"Angelica Kauffman":{"zh":"安杰莉卡·考夫曼","en":"Angelica Kauffman","born":"1741","died":"1807","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"安杰莉卡·考夫曼，十八世纪最负盛名的女画家之一，瑞士裔新古典主义大师。她以取材古典神话与历史的叙事画和优雅的肖像享誉欧洲，是伦敦皇家艺术学院仅有的两位女性创始成员之一。","bio_en":"Angelica Kauffman was one of the most celebrated women painters of the eighteenth century and a leading Neoclassical artist of Swiss origin. Renowned across Europe for her history paintings drawn from classical myth and her graceful portraits, she was one of only two women among the founding members of London's Royal Academy.","p":"images/a/Q123098.jpg"},"Anton Raphael Mengs":{"zh":"安东·拉斐尔·门斯","en":"Anton Raphael Mengs","born":"1728","died":"1779","cty_zh":"德国","cty_en":"Germany","bio_zh":"安东·拉斐尔·门斯，德意志-波希米亚裔画家，十八世纪新古典主义的奠基者之一。他与温克尔曼交往密切，以罗马阿尔巴尼别墅的天顶壁画《帕纳索斯山》确立典范，其理论与实践共同推动了对古典理想的回归。","bio_en":"Anton Raphael Mengs was a German-Bohemian painter and a founding figure of eighteenth-century Neoclassicism. A close associate of Winckelmann, he set a model with his ceiling fresco Parnassus at the Villa Albani in Rome, and through both theory and practice helped drive the return to classical ideals.","p":"images/a/Q76718.jpg"},"Jean-Étienne Liotard":{"zh":"让-艾蒂安·利奥塔尔","en":"Jean-Étienne Liotard","born":"1702","died":"1789","cty_zh":"瑞士","cty_en":"Switzerland","bio_zh":"让-艾蒂安·利奥塔尔，瑞士裔肖像画家，十八世纪最杰出的粉彩大师。他以细腻入微的写实和柔润的粉彩笔触闻名，代表作《美丽的巧克力女孩》尤为脍炙人口；旅居君士坦丁堡的经历也令他常着东方装束作画，得名「土耳其画家」。","bio_en":"Jean-Étienne Liotard was a Swiss portraitist and the finest pastel master of the eighteenth century. Celebrated for his meticulous realism and the soft luminosity of his pastels—epitomized by The Chocolate Girl—his years in Constantinople led him to paint in Turkish dress, earning him the nickname 'the Turkish painter.'","p":"images/a/Q123757.jpg"},"Juan de Valdés Leal":{"zh":"胡安·德·巴尔德斯·莱亚尔","en":"Juan de Valdés Leal","born":"1622","died":"1690","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"胡安·德·巴尔德斯·莱亚尔，塞维利亚西班牙巴洛克画派的代表人物。他画风热烈动荡、色彩浓烈，尤以为慈善医院所作的两幅「死亡的寓意」（《转瞬之间》与《世间荣耀的终结》）震撼人心，将虚空派题材推向极致。","bio_en":"Juan de Valdés Leal was a leading figure of the Seville school of Spanish Baroque painting. Working in a fervent, restless style with intense color, he is best known for his two allegories of death for the Hospital de la Caridad, In Ictu Oculi and Finis Gloriae Mundi, which pushed the vanitas theme to its haunting extreme.","p":"images/a/Q518898.png"},"Alonso Cano":{"zh":"阿隆索·卡诺","en":"Alonso Cano","born":"1601","died":"1667","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"阿隆索·卡诺，西班牙巴洛克时期集绘画、雕塑与建筑于一身的全才，素有「西班牙的米开朗琪罗」之称。他画风典雅细腻、造型温润，晚年主持格拉纳达主教座堂正立面的设计，为西班牙巴洛克建筑留下典范。","bio_en":"Alonso Cano was a Spanish Baroque master who excelled equally as painter, sculptor, and architect, earning the epithet 'the Spanish Michelangelo.' His refined, tender style is matched by his design for the façade of Granada Cathedral, a landmark of Spanish Baroque architecture.","p":"images/a/Q378783.jpg"},"Luis de Morales":{"zh":"路易斯·德·莫拉莱斯","en":"Luis de Morales","born":"1509","died":"1586","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"路易斯·德·莫拉莱斯，西班牙文艺复兴晚期最富虔敬气质的画家，因其笔下神圣题材而被誉为「神圣者」（El Divino）。他融合尼德兰的精细与意大利的样式主义，专擅《圣母子》《戴荆冠的基督》等冥想式宗教小幅，情感深沉内敛。","bio_en":"Luis de Morales was the most devout painter of the late Spanish Renaissance, called 'El Divino' for the sacred character of his images. Blending Netherlandish precision with Italian Mannerism, he specialized in intimate, meditative devotional works such as the Virgin and Child and the Ecce Homo, marked by deep restrained emotion.","p":"images/a/Q703250.jpg"},"Juan Sánchez Cotán":{"zh":"胡安·桑切斯·科坦","en":"Juan Sánchez Cotán","born":"1560","died":"1627","cty_zh":"西班牙","cty_en":"Spain","bio_zh":"胡安·桑切斯·科坦，西班牙静物画（bodegón）的开创者之一。他以近乎苦修的极简构图，将瓜果菜蔬悬于幽暗龛中，令强烈的明暗对照赋予寻常之物近乎神圣的静谧，深刻影响了后世西班牙静物传统。","bio_en":"Juan Sánchez Cotán was one of the pioneers of the Spanish still life, or bodegón. In austere, almost ascetic compositions he suspended fruits and vegetables against a dark niche, using stark chiaroscuro to lend humble objects an almost sacred stillness that profoundly shaped the later Spanish still-life tradition.","p":"images/a/Q919806.jpg"},"Vasily Polenov":{"zh":"瓦西里·波列诺夫","en":"Vasily Polenov","born":"1844","died":"1927","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"瓦西里·波列诺夫，俄国「巡回展览画派」的代表画家与杰出美术教育家。他兼擅风景与历史题材，《莫斯科小院》以质朴亲切的光色捕捉市井午后，开创了俄国「情绪风景」的一脉，并培育了列维坦等一代名家。","bio_en":"Vasily Polenov was a leading painter of the Russian Peredvizhniki (Wanderers) and an influential teacher. Equally gifted in landscape and history painting, his intimate Moscow Courtyard, bathed in gentle light, helped found the Russian tradition of the lyrical 'mood landscape' and shaped pupils such as Levitan.","p":"images/a/Q318393.jpg"},"Arkhip Kuindzhi":{"zh":"阿尔希普·库因吉","en":"Arkhip Kuindzhi","born":"1841","died":"1910","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"阿尔希普·库因吉，俄国风景画中最富诗意的光影大师。他痴迷于对光的极致表现，《第聂伯河上的月夜》以近乎发光的月色令观者惊叹，将自然景象升华为神秘而崇高的视觉诗篇。","bio_en":"Arkhip Kuindzhi was the most poetic master of light in Russian landscape painting. Obsessed with luminous effects, his Moonlit Night on the Dnieper astonished audiences with its almost glowing moonlight, transforming natural scenery into visions of mystery and the sublime.","p":"images/a/Q353628.jpg"},"Boris Kustodiev":{"zh":"鲍里斯·库斯托季耶夫","en":"Boris Kustodiev","born":"1878","died":"1927","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"鲍里斯·库斯托季耶夫，二十世纪初俄国民俗风情的欢快歌者。他以明艳饱满的色彩描绘外省市镇的集市、狂欢节与丰腴的商人之妻，《品茶的商妇》等作品将旧俄生活定格为一幅幅热烈而怀旧的画卷。","bio_en":"Boris Kustodiev was the joyful chronicler of Russian folk life in the early twentieth century. In vivid, saturated color he painted provincial fairs, Shrovetide festivals, and buxom merchants' wives, and works such as The Merchant's Wife at Tea preserve old Russia in scenes of warm, nostalgic exuberance.","p":"images/a/Q313275.jpg"},"Konstantin Makovsky":{"zh":"康斯坦丁·马科夫斯基","en":"Konstantin Makovsky","born":"1839","died":"1915","cty_zh":"俄罗斯","cty_en":"Russia","bio_zh":"康斯坦丁·马科夫斯基，俄国学院派历史风俗画的名家与广受追捧的肖像画家。他钟情于古俄罗斯波雅贵族的华服盛宴，以《波雅婚宴》一类作品铺陈细腻的织物与珠饰，营造出富丽堂皇的历史想象。","bio_en":"Konstantin Makovsky was a celebrated academic painter of historical genre and a sought-after society portraitist. Enamored of the sumptuous life of old Russian boyars, works such as The Boyar Wedding Feast lavish attention on rich fabrics and jewels, conjuring an opulent vision of the national past.","p":"images/a/Q460337.jpg"},"Kamisaka Sekka":{"zh":"神坂雪佳","en":"Kamisaka Sekka","born":"1866","died":"1942","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"神坂雪佳，日本近代京都画家、图案家，被视为琳派最后一位重要传人。生于京都粟田口，早年习四条派绘画，后随岸光景研习工艺图案而转向琳派。1901年受派赴欧洲考察图案，正值新艺术运动兴起。他为染织、陶艺、漆艺设计纹样，1909年起由芸艸堂刊行木版图案集《百々世草》三卷。","bio_en":"Kamisaka Sekka (1866–1942), born in Kyoto, was a painter and design artist, and the last major figure of the Rinpa tradition. Trained first in Shijō-school painting, he turned to Rinpa through his craft-design teacher Kishi Kōkei. Sent to Europe in 1901 to study design, he encountered Art Nouveau. He designed patterns for textiles, ceramics and lacquer, and published the three-volume woodblock album Momoyogusa from 1909."},"Shibata Zeshin":{"zh":"柴田是真","en":"Shibata Zeshin","born":"1807","died":"1891","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"柴田是真（1807—1891），日本江户末至明治的漆艺家兼画家，生于江户。十一岁入莳绘师古满宽哉门下学漆工，后随铃木南岭、冈本丰彦习四条派绘画。他复兴失传已久的青海波涂技法，并创出在纸上直接以漆作画的“漆绘”。1873年作品在维也纳世博会获奖，1890年任帝室技艺员。","bio_en":"Shibata Zeshin (1807–1891) was a lacquer artist and painter active in Edo and Meiji Japan. Apprenticed at eleven to the maki-e master Koma Kansai, he later studied Shijō-school painting under Suzuki Nanrei and Okamoto Toyohiko. He revived the long-disused seigaiha lacquer finish and devised urushi-e, painting with lacquer directly on paper. In 1890 he was named an Imperial Household Artist."},"Wang Gai":{"zh":"王概","en":"Wang Gai","born":"1645","died":"1710","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"王概（1645—1710），中国清代画家，浙江秀水（今嘉兴）人，字安节，初名匄，久居江宁（今南京）。曾从龚贤学画，用墨浓重，擅大幅山水与松石。1679 年，他在明人李流芳遗留的画稿基础上增补编成《芥子园画传》初集，专讲山水画法；后与兄王蓍、弟王臬续编二、三集，木版彩色套印，长期是学画者通用的入门范本。","bio_en":"Wang Gai (1645–1710) was a Qing-dynasty painter from Xiushui, Zhejiang, who lived mainly in Nanjing. He studied landscape under Gong Xian and painted in dense ink on a large scale. In 1679 he expanded sketches left by the Ming painter Li Liufang into the first part of the Mustard Seed Garden Manual of Painting; with his brothers he completed two later parts, colour-printed from woodblocks and long used to teach Chinese painting."},"Aoki Shukuya":{"zh":"青木夙夜","en":"Aoki Shukuya","born":"","died":"1802","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"青木夙夜，日本江户中后期南画（文人画）画家，名俊明（一作浚明），通称庄右卫门，号春塘、八岳，以山水、人物为主，画风细密。宝历年间经表亲、书家韩天寿引荐，师从池大雅。1776年大雅去世、1784年其妻玉澜去世后，他住进京都东山双林寺境内的大雅堂，自称「大雅堂二世」，守堂作画十余年，并以鉴定、临摹大雅之作见称。晚年移居伊势，1802年（享和二年十月二十三日）殁于松阪。生年不详（欧美馆藏多标作1737年）。","bio_en":"Aoki Shukuya (birth year unknown; died 1802) was a Japanese literati (nanga) painter of the mid-to-late Edo period. His personal name was Shunmei (also written Junmei), his common name Shōemon, and his art names Shuntō and Hachigaku; he painted landscapes and figure subjects in a fine, meticulous manner. Introduced by his cousin, the calligrapher Kan Tenju, he studied under Ike no Taiga in Kyoto from around the Hōreki era. After Taiga died in 1776 and his wife Gyokuran in 1784, Shukuya lived at the Taigadō within the precincts of Sōrin-ji in Kyoto's Higashiyama, called himself its second master, and kept the hall for over a decade, becoming known for authenticating and faithfully copying Taiga's work. He later moved to Ise and died at Matsusaka. (Western collections often give his birth year as 1737, but Japanese reference works record it as unknown.)"},"Maruyama Ōkyo":{"zh":"円山応挙","en":"Maruyama Ōkyo","born":"1733","died":"1795","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"円山応挙，日本江户中期京都画家，圆山派开创者。生于丹波国桑田郡穴太村（今京都府龟冈市），少年赴京都，入狩野派系统画师石田幽汀门下。二十多岁时在玩具商尾张屋绘制过借窥镜观看的「眼镜绘」，由此接触西洋透视法。他随身带写生帖，多角度对照实物描摹动植物。代表作《雪松图屏风》为国宝，藏三井纪念美术馆。门人有长泽芦雪等；松村月溪（呉春）本师从与谢芜村，曾求入其门，応挙不受而以友相待，月溪后另开四条派。","bio_en":"Maruyama Ōkyo (1733–1795) was a Kyoto painter of the mid-Edo period and founder of the Maruyama school. Born in Ano-o village in Tanba Province, he trained as a boy under the Kanō-lineage painter Ishida Yūtei; in his twenties, working for a Kyoto toy dealer, he made megane-e, peep-box pictures that introduced him to Western perspective. He carried sketchbooks everywhere, drawing plants and animals from direct observation. His Pine Trees in Snow screens are designated a National Treasure and are held by the Mitsui Memorial Museum, Tokyo. Nagasawa Rosetsu studied under him; Matsumura Goshun, a pupil of Yosa Buson, asked to enter his studio but Ōkyo declined and treated him as a friend and equal, and Goshun later founded the Shijō school."},"Tani Bunchō":{"zh":"谷文晁","en":"Tani Bunchō","born":"1763","died":"1841","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"谷文晁（1763–1841），日本江户后期画家。早年学狩野派，后转向南画，兼取汉、和、洋诸法，画风有「八宗兼学」之称。曾为白河藩主松平定信近习，1793年随其巡视相模、伊豆沿海海防，作《公余探胜图》。在江户设画塾写山楼，渡边华山、立原杏所等出其门下。","bio_en":"Tani Bunchō (1763–1841) was a Japanese painter of the late Edo period. Trained first in the Kanō school and then in the nanga manner, he freely combined Chinese, Japanese and Western techniques, a range often summed up as \"a student of all eight sects\". He served Matsudaira Sadanobu, lord of Shirakawa, accompanying his 1793 coastal-defence inspection of the Sagami and Izu shores to produce the Kōyo tanshō zu. His Edo studio Shazanrō taught Watanabe Kazan and Tachihara Kyōsho."},"Kikukawa Eizan":{"zh":"菊川英山","en":"Kikukawa Eizan","born":"1787","died":"1867","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"菊川英山（1787–1867），日本江户后期浮世绘画师，以美人画著称。父菊川英二在江户市谷经营造花业「近江屋」，兼习狩野派画艺（狩野东舍门人）；英山先随父学画，后师从圆山四条派的铃木南岭（1775–1844）。文化三年（1806）歌麿猝逝后，他接续歌麿风的美人样式，成为文化年间美人绘的第一人；进入文政年间，时尚转向其门人溪斋英泉与歌川国贞的艳丽新样，英山声势渐衰。溪斋英泉出其门下，他本人则被视为菊川派之祖。文政末年（约1830）版画工作渐止，晚年专事肉笔画。","bio_en":"Kikukawa Eizan (1787–1867) was an ukiyo-e designer best known for bijin-ga, images of beauties. He first studied with his father Eiji, who ran an artificial-flower business in Edo and painted in the Kanō manner, and then with Suzuki Nanrei (1775–1844) of the Maruyama-Shijō school. After Utamaro's sudden death in 1806 Eizan took up his manner of depicting women and became the foremost bijin designer of the Bunka era (1804–18); in the Bunsei era taste moved on to the more sensuous beauties of his own pupil Keisai Eisen and of Utagawa Kunisada, and his popularity faded. He is regarded as the founder of the Kikukawa school. His print work tailed off around the end of Bunsei (c. 1830), and in later years he worked mainly as a painter."},"Song Xu":{"zh":"宋旭","en":"Song Xu","born":"1525","died":"1606","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"宋旭（1525—1606），明代画家，字初旸（一作初阳），号石门山人，浙江人，后徙居松江。擅山水，兼画人物。上承吴门沈周，论画又推崇李成、关仝、范宽，笔墨雄劲古拙，自成一家。好云游，常寄居寺院，晚年出家为僧，法名祖玄。赵左、宋懋晋皆出其门下，晚明苏松、云间两派导源于他，世称松江画派之源。","bio_en":"Song Xu (1525–1606) was a late Ming Chinese painter. Born in Zhejiang, he settled in Songjiang. He specialised in landscapes and also painted figures, working in the Wu-school tradition of Shen Zhou, while holding the earlier masters Li Cheng, Guan Tong and Fan Kuan to be the supreme landscapists. His brushwork is vigorous and archaic. He wandered widely, lodging in temples, and took Buddhist orders late in life under the name Zuxuan. Zhao Zuo and Song Maojin studied under him, and the late-Ming Susong and Yunjian currents of the Songjiang school trace back to him."},"Tsubaki Chinzan":{"zh":"椿椿山","en":"Tsubaki Chinzan","born":"1801","died":"1854","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"椿椿山（1801—1854），日本江户后期南画家，出身幕府下级武士（旗本枪组同心之家）。先随金子金陵学沈南苹派花鸟，后入谷文晁门下，十七岁起终生师事渡边华山。擅花鸟与人物写照，设色秀润，肖像兼取西洋明暗法。华山自尽后，他收养并教授其子渡边小华；代表作《渡边华山像》成于1853年（今藏田原市博物馆，日本重要文化财），身后另有木刻本《椿山画谱》辑印行世。","bio_en":"Tsubaki Chinzan (1801–1854) was a nanga painter of late Edo Japan, born in Edo to a low-ranking shogunal retainer family. He first learned Shen Nanpin-style bird-and-flower painting from Kaneko Kinryō, then studied under Tani Bunchō, and from about seventeen followed Watanabe Kazan as his lifelong teacher. Known for delicately colored birds and flowers and for portraits using Western shading, he completed his portrait of Kazan in 1853."},"Yoshitsugu Haizan":{"zh":"吉嗣拝山","en":"Yoshitsugu Haizan","born":"1846","died":"1915","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"吉嗣拜山（1846—1915），日本幕末至大正时期的南画家，筑前太宰府（今福冈县）人。少时习汉学，后赴京都从中西耕石学南画。维新后曾任仓敷地方官，1871年因意外失去右手，此后专用左手作画，别号“左手拜山”。擅山水，尤以芦雁图见称，与儿玉果亭、山本梅庄并称地方南画三大家。","bio_en":"Yoshitsugu Haizan (1846–1915) was a Japanese nanga painter from Dazaifu in Chikuzen, present-day Fukuoka. He studied Chinese classics at the Kangien academy in Hita before taking up literati painting under Nakanishi Kōseki in Kyoto. After serving briefly as a local official in Kurashiki, he lost his right hand in an 1871 accident and painted left-handed thereafter, taking the art-name \"Left-hand Haizan\" (左手拝山). He specialized in landscapes and reed-and-geese subjects, and was ranked alongside Kodama Katei and Yamamoto Baisō as one of the three great provincial nanga masters."},"Hu Zhengyan":{"zh":"胡正言","en":"Hu Zhengyan","born":"1582","died":"1672","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"胡正言，明末清初书画篆刻家、出版家，安徽休宁人，长期寓居南京鸡笼山下，因庭中植竹十余竿而名其居为十竹斋。他主持刻成《十竹斋书画谱》（1619—1633 年间分谱陆续刊成）与《十竹斋笺谱》（1644）：前者以饾版分色分版叠印，使木版套印能再现毛笔的浓淡晕染；后者兼用拱花压出无墨凸纹。二书并为中国彩色版画的代表成果。","bio_en":"Hu Zhengyan was a seal carver, calligrapher and publisher of the late Ming and early Qing, born in Xiuning, Anhui, and long resident in Nanjing. His Ten Bamboo Studio issued the Manual of Calligraphy and Painting, produced in instalments between 1619 and 1633, and the Album of Letter Paper of 1644. The first used douban multi-block colour printing to reproduce the tonal washes of brushwork; the second added gonghua blind embossing for uninked relief designs."},"Kitao Masayoshi":{"zh":"北尾政美","en":"Kitao Masayoshi","born":"1764","died":"1824","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"北尾政美，日本江户后期浮世绘师，师从北尾重政，早年为黄表纸等通俗读物作插图。宽政六年（1794）受聘为津山藩御用绘师并剃发，后改号锹形蕙斋，又随幕府奥绘师狩野惟信习狩野派笔法。自宽政七年（1795）起刊行《略画式》《鸟兽略画式》等画谱，以极简笔线概括人物鸟兽形体；文化六年（1809）作鸟瞰名所图《江户一目图屏风》（津山乡土博物馆藏）。","bio_en":"Kitao Masayoshi trained under Kitao Shigemasa and began as an illustrator of popular fiction in Edo. In 1794 he was engaged as official painter to the Tsuyama domain and took the tonsure, later adopting the name Kuwagata Keisai; he also studied Kanō-school painting under the shogunal painter Kanō Korenobu. From 1795 he issued the Ryakugashiki drawing manuals, reducing figures, birds and animals to a few strokes, and in 1809 painted the panoramic bird's-eye view of the city, Edo ichimoku-zu byōbu."},"Zhang Ruoai":{"zh":"张若霭","en":"Zhang Ruoai","born":"1713","died":"1746","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"张若霭（1713—1746），清代画家，字景采，号晴岚，安徽桐城人，大学士张廷玉长子。雍正十一年（1733）中二甲一名进士，入直南书房，以书画供奉内廷。工山水，尤长花鸟，其花鸟得明代王谷祥、周之冕写生一路遗意。奉命鉴定品第内府藏画，参与编纂《秘殿珠林》《石渠宝笈》。乾隆十一年（1746）随帝西巡，途中患病，归京后卒，年三十四，谥文僖。","bio_en":"Zhang Ruoai (1713–1746) came from Tongcheng in Anhui and was the eldest son of the Grand Secretary Zhang Tingyu. He took the jinshi degree in 1733 and served as a scholar-official at court, where the Qianlong emperor valued him for his painting and calligraphy. He painted landscapes as well as birds and flowers, the latter following the descriptive manner of the Ming masters Wang Guxiang and Zhou Zhimian. Charged with appraising and grading works in the imperial collection, he was among the officials who compiled its catalogues, the Midian zhulin and the Shiqu baoji. He fell ill while accompanying the emperor on a tour to the west and died in 1746, in his thirty-fourth year."},"Zha Shibiao":{"zh":"查士标","en":"Zha Shibiao","born":"1615","died":"1698","cty_zh":"中国","cty_en":"China","bio_zh":"查士标（1615—1698），中国明末清初画家、书法家，安徽休宁人，字二瞻，号梅壑。明诸生，明亡后弃举子业，绝意仕进，往来于扬州、镇江、金陵等地，晚年寓居扬州。山水取法倪瓒、吴镇、黄公望，兼受董其昌影响，用笔疏简，较同乡渐江更显润泽；书法出自米芾、董其昌，长于行草。与渐江、孙逸、汪之瑞并称\"新安四家\"（又称\"海阳四家\"）。","bio_en":"Zha Shibiao (1615–1698) was a Chinese painter and calligrapher of the late Ming and early Qing, born in Xiuning, Anhui. A licentiate under the Ming, he abandoned the examination path after the dynasty fell and took no office under the new one, moving between Yangzhou, Zhenjiang and Nanjing before settling in Yangzhou in his later years. His landscapes follow Ni Zan, Wu Zhen and Huang Gongwang, with Dong Qichang a further influence; his brushwork is sparse and spare, yet wetter than that of his fellow Xin'an painter Hongren. His calligraphy derives from Mi Fu and Dong Qichang, and he excelled at running and cursive script. He is counted among the Four Masters of Xin'an (also called the Four Masters of Haiyang)."},"Isoda Koryūsai":{"zh":"矶田湖龙斋","en":"Isoda Koryūsai","born":"1735","died":"","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"矶田湖龙斋（1735年生，卒年不详），日本江户时代中期浮世绘画师，本名矶田正胜，通称庄兵卫。原为土浦藩土屋家武士，后成浪人，居江户两国药研堀。画风深受铃木春信影响，尤擅狭长的柱绘，所作至少三百五十图，数量为同期画师之冠。1776 年起刊行美人画系列《雏形若菜の初模样》，图逾百幅；1782 年获法桥僧位，晚年转以肉笔浮世绘为主。","bio_en":"Isoda Koryūsai (born 1735; date of death unknown) was a Japanese ukiyo-e artist of the mid-Edo period. A samurai in the service of the Tsuchiya clan of Tsuchiura, he became a rōnin and lived in the Yagenbori district of Edo. Working in a manner close to Suzuki Harunobu's, he specialised in narrow pillar prints, designing at least 350 of them — more than any other artist of his generation. From 1776 he issued the long beauty series Hinagata Wakana no Hatsu Moyō, received the Buddhist rank of hokkyō in 1782, and in his later years worked mainly as a painter."},"Kubo Shunman":{"zh":"窪俊満","en":"Kubo Shunman","born":"1757","died":"1820","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"窪俊満，日本江户后期浮世绘画师，兼作狂歌，狂歌号南陀伽紫兰。初从胜川春章习画，后受鸟居清长影响，人物取修长挺秀之姿。他以摺物（私家订制的小幅版画，多配狂歌）见长，常刻意舍去红色而用灰、褐、蓝的低彩度配色，人称「红嫌」，在浮世绘中别具一格。亦为狂歌本绘制插图并参与编纂。","bio_en":"Kubo Shunman (1757–1820) was an ukiyo-e artist of the late Edo period who was also active as a kyōka poet under the name Nandaka Shiran. He first studied under Katsukawa Shunshō and later absorbed the tall, slender figure style of Torii Kiyonaga. He is best known for surimono — privately commissioned prints, usually paired with kyōka verse — and for a restrained palette of greys, browns and blues that deliberately avoids red, a manner known as beni-girai."},"Utagawa Hiroshige II":{"zh":"二代目歌川广重","en":"Utagawa Hiroshige II","born":"1826","died":"1869","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"二代目歌川广重，初代广重的门人，本名铃木镇平，早年署「重宣」。1858 年初代殁后娶其女、袭「广重」之名。代表作为名所绘《诸国名所百景》。后与师门失和，移居横滨，改号「立祥」，为出口用的丝绸与茶箱绘制图样。","bio_en":"Utagawa Hiroshige II (1826–1869) was a pupil of the first Hiroshige, signing his early work Shigenobu. After his master died in 1858 he married Hiroshige’s daughter and took the name Hiroshige. His main series is One Hundred Famous Views in the Various Provinces. He later parted from the studio, moved to Yokohama and worked under the name Risshō, designing patterns for export silk and tea-chest labels."},"Totoya Hokkei":{"zh":"鱼屋北溪","en":"Totoya Hokkei","born":"1780","died":"1850","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"鱼屋北溪，葛饰北斋门下最主要的弟子之一。早年以鱼商为业，故号「鱼屋」。与俊満同为摺物名手，所作多为狂歌连所订制的小幅精印之作，用色典雅、常施云母与金银。亦为狂歌本与读本绘制插图。","bio_en":"Totoya Hokkei (1780–1850) was one of the foremost pupils of Katsushika Hokusai. He worked as a fishmonger in his youth, which gave him the art name Totoya (“fish shop”). Like Shunman he was a master of surimono, producing finely printed small-format works commissioned by kyōka poetry circles, often enriched with mica and metallic pigments, and he also illustrated kyōka anthologies and popular fiction."},"Yamada Hōgyoku":{"zh":"山田宝玉","en":"Yamada Hōgyoku","born":"1804","died":"1844","cty_zh":"日本","cty_en":"Japan","bio_zh":"山田宝玉，日本江户后期浮世绘画师，活跃于文政至天保年间。存世作品以摺物为主——狂歌连订制的小幅版画，题材多为器物、花卉、动物与店铺招牌一类的应景之作。其生平记载极少。","bio_en":"Yamada Hōgyoku (1804–1844) was an ukiyo-e artist of the late Edo period, active in the Bunsei and Tenpō eras. His surviving work consists largely of surimono — small privately commissioned prints made for kyōka poetry circles — depicting objects, flowers, animals and shop signs. Little is recorded of his life."}};
